he black market, their humors fetch prices high enough to fund their research labs and unsanctioned experiments. Behind closed doors, they steal Vitae to bestow themselves with powers of the Blood that should be beyond their reach. They are magicians and hucksters and court advisers, but like all Blights, it\u2019s only a matter of time before they arouse too much ire and bring all they\u2019ve built crashing down. If the brightest flames burn out fastest, then Tweakers self-destruct like, well, a firestorm. But hey, it\u2019s better to burn out than to fade away \u2014 even if they have to take half the domain with them.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> Bloodily Embracing victims, suckling like babes from pliant ghouls, chasing a vicious cycle of bestial hunger? Such <i>unevolved </i>approaches to immortality. There\u2019s a more elegant solution, a tidier way to live out eternity. Free yourself from your primitive shackles of self. We can give you the power to face any challenge, to be all things to all people. Move past the petty weakness you call a personality and become the god you were always meant to be.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> Knowledge is more than power; it\u2019s perfection. Our humors let us stand above the weaknesses of vampiric nature, unrestrained by humanity, unhindered by frenzy. With the right humor, neither the Beast nor even our own bodies can hold us back from achieving what we want. We\u2019ll learn your weaknesses and customize ourselves into the perfect antithesis. We\u2019re better. More versatile. We\u2019ll not just outpace you \u2014 we\u2019ll replace you.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> We can\u2019t make the magic happen without the right ingredients. Not just the Divine Fire, but the raw materials, and there\u2019s only so much you can hollow out till you\u2019ve got nothing left. How much are you willing to forget in the pursuit of those great heights