l dividing the Kindred community, the Chameleons strain for legitimacy. Thus begins their enduring drive to be deemed good enough, to be useful, to be <i>indispensable</i>. Perhaps something buried deep in the desert might teach them a thing or two about the alchemy of eternal life and the ravages of memory...<br /> <br /> <b>New Merit: Alkahest (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Hypatian, Blood Chymistry \u2022<br /> <br /> <b>Effect: </b>Purity comes from dissolution. The Sacrosanct can turn their victims into living athanors, dissolving away the bonds that hold their memories in place to produce a caustic substance called Alkahest, a brassy, shimmering liquid that can act as a \u201csuccedaneum,\u201d a substitute for Pyros in both Blood Chymistry and Hypatian Embraces. In return, the victim perfects a particular mundane ability to its pinnacle, all at the cost of a little piece of herself.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback: </b>This substance is only half as potent as the genuine article, so the ratio of required Pyros in Blood Chymistry recipes is doubled when using Alkahest instead.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost: </b>Variable Vitae<br /> <br /> <b>Requirement: </b>Your character must pump the cost through the body of a conscious victim.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Resolve + Science + Alkahest vs. Stamina + Blood Potency (if unwilling)<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Contested; resistance is reflexive<br /> <br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <br /> <b>Success: </b>Your character produces one point of Alkahest per Vitae spent. Each point lasts a night, dissolving into nothing at the next sunrise.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the subject gains the Amnesia Condition (<b>Vampire</b>, p. 301), forgetting an important aspect of who they are; typically, this is random, though some Tweakers pretend they can extract specific memories. The process fills in new gaps in her mind, granting three dots in a Skill of her player\u2019s choice.<br /> <br /> The Amnesia Condition isn\u2019t (quite) literal; the subject\u2019s memory is more askew than absent. Amnesia lasts for nights equal to Alkahest produced, and the subject cannot be used to produce the substance again until it resolves. When Amnesia fades, so do the Skill dots.<br /> <br /> Some Chameleons are rumored to be able to make these changes permanent, but this would be a closely guarded trade secret. If it were true\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> Your character produces one point of Alkahest per Vitae spent, plus <i>two </i>for each dot in this Merit. This does not extend the period Amnesia lasts.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure: </b>Your character produces sludge.<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The subject dies or falls to torpor and cannot be used as an athanor again.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's funny just how many vampires are obssessed with self-iprovement,funny and inspiring really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-21T21:48:02-07:00","id":1493504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1493484#post1493484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Partly, it's because we wanted to make Asphyx pretty blood-heavy. Asphyx isn't too bad if you're only fighting off a Brother one or two dots of her Discipline, BUT, if she's taken the time to pump a lot of Vitae in it, it's not going to be pretty (this is partly why they get more out of feeding from poisoned victims). That said, I just noticed that the resistance for The Cough includes Resolve, and I meant to change that to <i>just </i>Stamina, so I'll fix that in errata. (I also just noticed it's a bit unclear <i>when </i>you reduce the Toxicity by Blood Potency: it's after you're poisoned, not before, and I'll make that clearer as well.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that would do it!<br /> I definitely got the impression on my read that it was supposed to be an expensive Discipline, and thought it was very cool that using it before feeding helps recoup that cost a little [and kinda nods to their old bane]. But the numbers just weren't adding up for me. Knowing that its resistance had an extra trait and Potency is supposed to subtract from Toxicity after you've been hit definitely clears up my confusion!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tell you what, I'll cover them on Friday! Today, though, we're doing one you illustrated: <b>The Sacrosanct</b> of &quot;Clan&quot; Hypatian. </div> </div> </div>Oh heck yeah, I can't wait! I'm very interested in seeing those dev notes... \ud83d\udc40<br /> <br /> And while I'm here, I guess I can say a little about the Sacrosanct illustration, because it was kind of involved. And that was despite having a very clear vision for it!<br /> <br /> A big part of that was my decision to give her four drip bags, when the notes only described one. However, they also said the Sacrosanct &quot;remix their personalities and mental abilities with humour based potions,&quot; and I wanted to convey that visually. So I decided to gave her a drip bag of each humour. This... ended up being complicated, and maybe even a little silly looking [aside from the blood bag, doesn't it kind of look like she is pumping a soda machine into her body?]. The tangle of unused IVs was a nightmare to represent visually, and I really do not know how well the humours actually end up reading. It probably would have been safer to stick with the one bag, but hopefully this way gives her more personality [lol].<br /> <br /> Speaking of the IVs, they were difficult too. I did a lot of backtracking and experimentation in my quest to get them to read as both transparent and filled. I ultimately made the tubes and bags all a semi-transparent grey color, and I think it works... mostly. The unused IVs aren't quite as visible in the final product as I wanted them to be, but there is still enough to their shape that they read well if you're not looking directly at them.<br /> <br /> And all of that isn't to say I don't like the final illustration, or think it is bad! It was just challenging, and I know parts of it could still be better. Other parts turned out really well, some better than I would have expected. In particular I think the base of the IV stand turned out really well [thanks references!], and I am pleased with the interplay of the linework and shading of her lab coat. She might not have the cyber arms of the Hypatian in <b>Spilled Blood</b> [and what is up with that, anyway?], but she definitely looks like a scientist who has sacrificed her personality for progress!<br /> <br /> She also ended up kinda looking like an old Hunter character of mine. Oops! At least I managed to dial back the resemblance <i>a little</i> in the final product [it was downright uncanny in my initial sketches].<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-21T22:08:17-07:00","id":1493505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SomethingFishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1493504#post1493504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, that would do it!<br /> I definitely got the impression on my read that it was supposed to be an expensive Discipline, and thought it was very cool that using it before feeding helps recoup that cost a little [and kinda nods to their old bane]. But the numbers just weren't adding up for me. Knowing that its resistance had an extra trait and Potency is supposed to subtract from Toxicity after you've been hit definitely clears up my confusion!<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh heck yeah, I can't wait! I'm very interested in seeing those dev notes... \ud83d\udc40<br /> <br /> And while I'm here, I guess I can say a little about the Sacrosanct illustration, because it was kind of involved. And that was despite having a very clear vision for it!<br /> <br /> A big part of that was my decision to give her four drip bags, when the notes only described one. However, they also said the Sacrosanct &quot;remix their personalities and mental abilities with humour based potions,&quot; and I wanted to convey that visually. So I decided to gave her a drip bag of each humour. This... ended up being complicated, and maybe even a little silly looking [aside from the blood bag, doesn't it kind of look like she is pumping a soda machine into her body?]. The tangle of unused IVs was a nightmare to represent visually, and I really do not know how well the humours actually end up reading. It probably would have been safer to stick with the one bag, but hopefully this way gives her more personality [lol].<br /> <br /> Speaking of the IVs, they were difficult too. I did a lot of backtracking and experimentation in my quest to get them to read as both transparent and filled. I ultimately made the tubes and bags all a semi-transparent grey color, and I think it works... mostly. The unused IVs aren't quite as visible in the final product as I wanted them to be, but there is still enough to their shape that they read well if you're not looking directly at them.<br /> <br /> And all of that isn't to say I don't like the final illustration, or think it is bad! It was just challenging, and I know parts of it could still be better. Other parts turned out really well, some better than I would have expected. In particular I think the base of the IV stand turned out really well [thanks references!], and I am pleased with the interplay of the linework and shading of her lab coat. She might not have the cyber arms of the Hypatian in <b>Spilled Blood</b> [and what is up with that, anyway?], but she definitely looks like a scientist who has sacrificed her personality for progress!<br /> <br /> She also ended up kinda looking like an old Hunter character of mine. Oops! At least I managed to dial back the resemblance <i>a little</i> in the final product [it was downright uncanny in my initial sketches].</div> </div> </div> </div>I got that they were humors right away, but I'm a nerd, haha. I really liked that touch; I wish I'd thought of it myself, but I'm glad you were more on the ball than me! Anyway, I think she ended up looking great. I really love the colour choices you went with for all the lost clan bloodlines; it's a little different for the usual palette for <b>Vampire</b>.<br /> <br /> Also, quick sidebar unrelated to art: Normally I don't post errata, but I apparently input the Iltani bloodline Disciplines incorrectly in editing. They should have Animalism, Auspex, Obfuscate, and Protean. I just wanted to mention that here, as I'm not planning on implementing an errata'd version of the book just yet (still got typos to hunt down), and that's a pretty important one.<br /> <br /> Anyway, hope everyone's enjoying the thread, and I'll be back tomorrow with more previews!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 09-22-2022, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-22T04:28:19-07:00","id":1493519,"title":"","content":"The system for sacrificing ephemera and humours sounds interestin, though I definitely understand why that was scrapped in the end. The Sacrosanct as presented here are still a wonderful bloodline addition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-22T11:36:23-07:00","id":1493529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TrueMrMultiverse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1493519#post1493519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The system for sacrificing ephemera and humours sounds interestin, though I definitely understand why that was scrapped in the end. The Sacrosanct as presented here are still a wonderful bloodline addition.</div> </div> </div> </div>It survives in a somewhat simplified form in the Iatrocehmistry Merit. The original concept was ambitious but just a bit too complex for a bloodline. It was also a matter of needing to define a bunch of new terms, which I find can make a system seem more complicated than it actually is.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-22T15:47:45-07:00","id":1493536,"title":"","content":"Alright, let's look at the Sta-Au. From a distance.<br /> <br /> This is one of the very, very few &quot;any/multi-clan&quot; bloodlines from First Edition, which for some reason was a thorny issue in early <b>Requiem</b>. Infamously, the Moroi bloodline write-up includes a sidebar that goes out of its way to declare that they're in fact two bloodlines that are exactly the same. To a lesser extent, then Mortifiers of the Flesh made you jump through several hoops if you wanted to play a non-Daeva. At any rate, that reluctance seems to have tapered off by the time <b>Ancient Bloodlines </b>came out, because there don't seem to be any caveats about who can join. At any rate, this is all to say that I like all-clan bloodlines. I feel like a future project might be to do a book of them, although I have to admit I'm a little bloodline'd out at this juncture.<br /> <br /> Anyway, my big directive for the Sta-Au was to make them more playable. Their original weakness was that they could never buy back Humanity which, uh, certainly scales with that trait, but is maaaaaaaybe a little harsh; direct quote from my outline: &quot;Boy their bane goes hard.&quot; It's a weakness that's interesting in concept but in practice (and with apologies to the sidebar on p. 35 of <b>Ancient Bloodlines</b>) mostly relegates them to Storyteller character territory, in which case that particular weakness doesn't really matter anymore. I'm sure one could play a Sta-Au with their original bane, but even ignoring how narrow it is, it's a tad boring. As such, I really like their new bane. We have a few more &quot;externality&quot; banes in this book (e.g., the Brothers of Ypres, the Nehebkau), in that they don't directly affect the character, but still influence behaviour. This bane also integrates the Land of the Worms more intimately with the bloodline, making them direct vectors for its spread.<br /> <br /> Speaking of the Land of the Worms, I'm really happy with how our version turned out. It's not too heavy mechanically, but it's a bit more modular than the original. I'm a big fan of Mysterious Places, so I'm always happy to fit them in where we can.<br /> <br /> I don't have much to say about the development process here, as not too much changed from the final draft apart from a couple of tweaks here and there. This was one of the bloodlines that was really solid right from the start. My only major addition was adding an additional Dark Era (the Lifting of the Veil one), as well as the &quot;Who We Are Tonight&quot; list. My biggest contribution was mostly the art.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I believe the author wanted to talk a bit about the writing process here, so I'll end on that note.<br /> <br /> So, here are the Sta-Au. As always, if you like the book, consider leaving us a review. Tomorrow, let's finish the week with the chilling <b>Caporetti</b>...<br /> <br /> <b>Sta-Au: The Ones Who Slaughter You</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Wolves to them; sheep to us.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Across the Great Plains, Kindred tell tales of the Sta-Au, ashen-skinned boogeymen with jagged teeth like rows of knives, covered in trinkets and trophies of human bone. This bloodline makes its home in the inhospitable badlands of the region, where all trespassers are dealt with accordingly. \u201cNormal\u201d vampires in the area cleave to humans as much as possible, spending their nights in cities and only traveling on heavily trafficked roads if possible; anything to avoid facing the Sta-Au and their hunting parties, or coming across the skull-adorned borders of the Land of the Worms.<br /> <br /> The Wicked Ones live up to their moniker. They have no regard for morality, instead celebrating depravity and cruelty as if they were virtues. The Sta-Au act as if they\u2019re the Beast incarnate, seemingly giving in to every dark urge and instinct with abandon. Yet unlike the draugr, they\u2019re not mindless monsters incapable of higher reasoning \u2014 which only serves to make them more insidious.<br /> <br /> The Sta-Au take their name from the ghosts of Blackfoot belief, the wicked dead who choose to harry the living instead of passing on to the Great Sand Hills. Unlike their incorporeal counterparts, the Wicked Ones believe all vampires have failed to properly die, reprobates eternally stuck in their corpses. To break free from these shackles, the Sta-Au die a second time, bringing themselves ever closer to a true death. After that, it\u2019s just a matter of finding the passage to an afterlife befitting such vile creatures as vampires and, finally, proving worthy of entrance.<br /> <br /> The Sta-Au\u2019s afterlife is said to link to the locations collectively known as the Land of the Worms (p. 91). It\u2019s within the Land of the Worms that Sta-Au traditionally dwell, reinforcing its ruinous resonance and preparing themselves for what lies beyond. By deliberately and carefully shedding each remaining scrap of his mortal life, a Wicked One shall become a pure monster, unfettered by any inhibitions yet not reduced to a simple animal. When he\u2019s freed from the limitations of his Humanity, the Twice-Dead sheds his human body and enters his new hunting grounds.<br /> <br /> True monsters don\u2019t abide by any rules, but until the Sta-Au can escape their immortal coils, rules serve a crucial purpose. As a group, the Sta-Au would\u2019ve self-destructed long ago were it not for the traditions and customs they developed centuries ago. One seeker\u2019s path to transcendence shall not interfere with another\u2019s, and a threat to one\u2019s road is a threat to all. While violence is the natural way to settle conflicts between Wicked Ones, it\u2019s ritualized, and the victor is expected to respect their opponent\u2019s defeat. Even bitter rivals cease their attacks once the other lies in torpor, and they even band together should another Twice-Dead break one of their few taboos, or fail their quest and fall to the Beast.<br /> <br /> However, not all Sta-Au are committed to anarcho-primitivist deaths in the wilderness. As the American frontier drew to a close, towns and cities boomed. During the Great Depression a few decades later, hunting parties discovered the Land of the Worms could manifest in built-up areas, such as derelict industries and abandoned residencies. Since then, more and more Wicked Ones have made their homes in urban environments, though not without adaptation. Rather than existing in bands separate from the All Night Society, they hide by intermingling with the uninitiated \u2014 joining mixed coteries and even participating in the covenants.<br /> <br /> This is not to say traditional Sta-Au are rigid and unchanging. Elders expect new blood to adapt to their brutal ways, with scarification and the filing of one\u2019s teeth being common ways to show dedication to the goal of transcendence, but individuality is otherwise encouraged. New ideas just mean new possibilities to explore \u2014 and ultimately, the goal is for <i>you </i>to become the best monster you can be.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> The first death cursed you. You\u2019re caught in the world of the living, unable to break free of your invisible bonds and move on. You play make-believe and hide behind petty schemes. It\u2019s pathetic. We discard all these meaningless pursuits, fetters that would keep us from reaching our true potential. We know what we\u2019ve become, and we\u2019ll show you how to become more.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> Your second death is a promise. The world is violent, and sooner or later, everyone dies for good. Sooner if you give us a reason. But we aren\u2019t beasts who attack on sight. We act deliberately. With reason. Just make sure to always treat us with respect, stay out of our way, and never, ever show weakness. If you can do that, you\u2019ll be fine.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> Our third death lies ahead of us. We know the path. We only need to reach beyond the Land of the Worms and grasp our reward\u2026 but the path is narrow and treacherous. Violence begets violence, and many of us perish before we ever reach our goal. We celebrate our dark desires and denounce our vestigial Humanity, but without restraint, they will surely destroy us, and only darkness will be our reward.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan: </b>Any<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Twice-Dead, the Wicked Ones<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Ruinous Curse):</b> The Sta-Au are creatures of defilement and destruction, both physical and moral, and wherever they go, they bring this nature with them. Whenever a Wicked One suffers a breaking point or causes another to suffer a breaking point against Humanity or Integrity, roll her Humanity. On a failure, the location around them suffers the Spiritual Infestation Tilt.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b><i>Auspex</i>, Obfuscate, <i>Protean</i>, Resilience<br /> <br /> <b>Spiritual Infestation (Environmental Tilt)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Description: </b>The curse of the Wicked Ones has infested the area. It eats through the spiritual foundation of the world, perforating its structure and leaving nothing but refuse behind.<br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> The area takes on the traits of the Land of the Worms. When this Tilt is applied, the area suffers the Spiritual Blight Aspect (p. 93). Additional breaking points suffered within the same area reset the Tilt\u2019s duration, and if a breaking point leads to the loss of Humanity or Integrity, the area gains an additional minor Aspect (Potency 1, if needed).<br /> <br /> If the area would gain a fourth Aspect, it\u2019s major. At this point, the area is at the cusp of deteriorating into a true Land of the Worms. Provided the location is not otherwise unfitting (such as being populated or heavily trafficked by humans or wildlife) a single significant push will end the Tilt and create a Land of the Worms at Potency 2.<br /> <br /> <b>Causing the Tilt: </b>A Sta-Au suffers or causes a breaking point.<br /> <br /> <b>Ending the Tilt:</b> The Tilt ends after a number of nights equal to the Sta-Au\u2019s Blood Potency times the number of Aspects that currently apply to the area.<br /> <br /> <b>In the Dark Eras (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> <b>A Handful of Dust \u2014 1933\u20131944 CE (DE1, p. 470):</b> Amid economic hardship and ecological disaster, the Sta-Au became yet another scourge afflicting the Midwest. Barren fields, abandoned factories, and storm-struck towns allow the Land of the Worms to grow at an unprecedented rate. The Sta-Au are quick to follow, and they find unlikely rivals. Animated piles of dust and detritus, also known as Dust Devils, have no aversion to the Land, and they stalk the same human victims as the Wicked Ones. They\u2019re also strangely drawn to the dead who dwell in Twilight\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Gift: A Path Between Worlds</b><br /> <br /> The Wicked Ones do not act as they do due to blind faith alone. No, they see clearly what lies ahead of them. Every step they take on their journey of transcendence is clear.<br /> <br /> The first step is as simple as opening your eyes. As soon as a Sta-Au joins her new siblings, she also starts perceiving the dead who were freed from their physical forms yet still linger in the world of the living. Ghosts in the state of Twilight (see <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b>, p. 124) appear as if physical to her \u2014 only their muted colors and lightly distorted voices betray their true insubstantiality. Other entities and phenomena of ghostly ephemera are similarly visible.<br /> <br /> As she sheds more and more of her chains, the Wicked One unlocks additional benefits along the path. As long as her Humanity does not exceed five dots, she can shift her body into Twilight as per the following systems:<br /> <br /> [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-22T16:25:02-07:00","id":1493538,"title":"","content":"Wonder what\u2019d happen if the Sta-Au and Belial\u2019s Brood meet up\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-22T16:46:40-07:00","id":1493539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1493538#post1493538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wonder what\u2019d happen if the Sta-Au and Belial\u2019s Brood meet up\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iypUpv9xelg\" target=\"_blank\">I couldn't tell you specifically, but I'm sure a good time would be had by all.</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-22T17:03:14-07:00","id":1493541,"title":"","content":"I must say that I really like the strange similarity between the Sta Au being Twice Dead and the Twice Damned variants- like they present two faces of the same coin, to a degree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-22T17:06:16-07:00","id":1493542,"title":"","content":"The Sta-Au are wonderful, the Tilt they cause and their ability to see into the Twilight are neat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-22T17:19:10-07:00","id":1493544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1493536#post1493536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, let's look at the Sta-Au. From a distance.<br /> <br /> This is one of the very, very few &amp;quot;any/multi-clan&amp;quot; bloodlines from First Edition, which for some reason was a thorny issue in early <b>Requiem</b>. Infamously, the Moroi bloodline write-up includes a sidebar that goes out of its way to declare that they're in fact two bloodlines that are exactly the same. To a lesser extent, then Mortifiers of the Flesh made you jump through several hoops if you wanted to play a non-Daeva. At any rate, that reluctance seems to have tapered off by the time <b>Ancient Bloodlines </b>came out, because there don't seem to be any caveats about who can join. At any rate, this is all to say that I like all-clan bloodlines. I feel like a future project might be to do a book of them, although I have to admit I'm a little bloodline'd out at this juncture.<br /> <br /> Anyway, my big directive for the Sta-Au was to make them more playable. Their original weakness was that they could never buy back Humanity which, uh, certainly scales with that trait, but is maaaaaaaybe a little harsh; direct quote from my outline: &amp;quot;Boy their bane goes hard.&amp;quot; It's a weakness that's interesting in concept but in practice (and with apologies to the sidebar on p. 35 of <b>Ancient Bloodlines</b>) mostly relegates them to Storyteller character territory, in which case that particular weakness doesn't really matter anymore. I'm sure one could play a Sta-Au with their original bane, but even ignoring how narrow it is, it's a tad boring. As such, I really like their new bane. We have a few more &amp;quot;externality&amp;quot; banes in this book (e.g., the Brothers of Ypres, the Nehebkau), in that they don't directly affect the character, but still influence behaviour. This bane also integrates the Land of the Worms more intimately with the bloodline, making them direct vectors for its spread.<br /> <br /> Speaking of the Land of the Worms, I'm really happy with how our version turned out. It's not too heavy mechanically, but it's a bit more modular than the original. I'm a big fan of Mysterious Places, so I'm always happy to fit them in where we can.<br /> <br /> I don't have much to say about the development process here, as not too much changed from the final draft apart from a couple of tweaks here and there. This was one of the bloodlines that was really solid right from the start. My only major addition was adding an additional Dark Era (the Lifting of the Veil one), as well as the &amp;quot;Who We Are Tonight&amp;quot; list. My biggest contribution was mostly the art.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I believe the author wanted to talk a bit about the writing process here, so I'll end on that note.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm the author for this particular bloodline and I'm quite happy with how it turned out. It's way too late over here, though (dang time zones), so I'll try be short.<br /> I think the original writeup for the Sta-Au is kinda fantastic, if a bit flawed at some points. It's impressive how vampires who are evil for the sake of being evil could work so well and not seem completely juvenile. Unfortunately, what's holding them back is the fact that they weren't approachable as a player option. The last page for them in Ancient Bloodlines is even dominated by a sidebar trying to convince the reader they're actually written for player characters.<br /> So yeah, playability was a big focus. And I don't mean that in a strictly mechanical sense: A lot of effort went into trying to balance their unapologetically monstrous behaviour with the ability to have any meaningful interactions with the rest of Kindred society outside of threats and violence. I hope I did a good job giving them some much needed nuance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1493541#post1493541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must say that I really like the strange similarity between the Sta Au being Twice Dead and the Twice Damned variants- like they present two faces of the same coin, to a degree.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think I kept it in (I blame wordcount), but the original text says that they are probably based on Gangrel or Mekhet, or both if the story of the two founders is true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TrueMrMultiverse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1493542#post1493542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sta-Au are wonderful, the Tilt they cause and their ability to see into the Twilight are neat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you think so!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-22T17:33:13-07:00","id":1493545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1493541#post1493541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must say that I really like the strange similarity between the Sta Au being Twice Dead and the Twice Damned variants- like they present two faces of the same coin, to a degree.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sta-Au being more &quot;successful&quot; Gangrel/Mekhet Twice-Cursed is cool interpretation (compare the Moroi being successful Gangrel/Nosferatu Twice-Cursed, as hinted at in <b>Spilled Blood</b>). What happens when you combine fierce hunters with weird occult voyeurs? A death cult.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I think Tessie did an excellent job of broadening the kind of characters you can play with them. The original kind of assumes you'd be playing an all-Sta-Au chronicle, but this version slots in pretty easily (if not <i>comfortably</i>) with the more mainstream factions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 09-22-2022, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-23T00:32:02-07:00","id":1493567,"title":"","content":"On the topic of the Sta-Au's original bane (not being able to raise Humanity): I absolutely agreed that it had to go, but not because it's harsh, imo. In second edition it's very difficult encountering breaking points at Humanity 1 (unless you play a diablerist). Rather, it's quite ineffectual (as in it wouldn't ever be a limitation if you play into the type) and just boring (as it isn't something you can really interact with during play).<br /> <br /> That said, it <i>is</i> extremely thematic for the bloodline so I couldn't get rid of it completely. Now buying Humanity becomes punishing as you lose access to parts of the Bloodline Gift, and, conversely, the Gift is a carrot for losing Humanity in the first place.<br /> It also grants in-setting legitimacy to their monstrous quest; doing what they do leads directly to (in)tangible progress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-23T12:08:44-07:00","id":1493592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1493567#post1493567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the topic of the Sta-Au's original bane (not being able to raise Humanity): I absolutely agreed that it had to go, but not because it's harsh, imo. In second edition it's very difficult encountering breaking points at Humanity 1 (unless you play a diablerist). Rather, it's quite ineffectual (as in it wouldn't ever be a limitation if you play into the type) and just boring (as it isn't something you can really interact with during play).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, harsh is maybe too strong a word. I've had one (1) fellow player hit Humanity 0 in a game via breaking points (it was great), but I do think not being able to buy up Humanity is narratively limiting in a way that's not very fun (even if you're playing to type). That said, not being all that interesting was definitely the bigger problem. Dull is always the greater sin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, it <i>is</i> extremely thematic for the bloodline so I couldn't get rid of it completely. Now buying Humanity becomes punishing as you lose access to parts of the Bloodline Gift, and, conversely, the Gift is a carrot for losing Humanity in the first place.<br /> It also grants in-setting legitimacy to their monstrous quest; doing what they do leads directly to (in)tangible progress. </div> </div> </div>I forgot to mention this in my commentary, but this is a <i>such </i>cool detail. We don't often have &quot;lower humanity = better&quot; powers, but I'm a fan of them. You have to play it just right, but I think it works well for the Sta-Au, both honoring the spirit of their original weakness and expanding into more interesting narrative territory.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, here's today's excerpt and commentary: The Caporetti.<br /> <br /> The original Shivers are kind of a missed opportunity, in my opinion. They\u2019ve got a great aesthetic \u2014 frost-bitten corpse Nosferatu \u2014 but they don\u2019t quite go beyond that. Their powers are also a bit redundant with Protean, and their weakness involves a design choice I\u2019m not very fond of: making it harder to use a clan Discipline (namely, Obfuscate). I\u2019m fine with making the inherent Kindred abilities a little wonky in service to a bane, bit I don\u2019t really care for flaws that devalue your hard-earned Experiences.<br /> <br /> That being said, I didn\u2019t really have a specific direction for this bloodline. I suggested they could perhaps have Protean instead of Celerity (which we didn\u2019t end up doing), but I more or less gave the author carte blanche to rebuild them, and I think he really built on their original concept without losing the creepy mood. Whereas the version in <b>Ancient Bloodlines </b>are mostly just cold-weather survivalists, our update expands that by giving them an inherent ability to store dead blood and bottle it in frozen corpses, giving them mercantile angle that opens up a lot more character concepts.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s an interesting parallel between the Caporetti and their fellow WWI vets, the Brothers of Ypres, one that was entirely unintentional on the authors\u2019 part. Both produce a kind of horror: Whereas the Brothers of Ypres create Phosgene Angels, Caporetti who feed too much of cold, dead blood <i>become </i>the monster. This is a theme we\u2019ve explored previously with the electricity-eating Keravnos in <b>False Gods: Ventru</b>e. I\u2019m generally of the opinion that Kindred who try to find alternate sources of food are doomed to become something much worse than vampires. The Curse can only be denied so much before something breaks. Anyway, I like the thematic complementariness of this: The Brothers of Ypres are about what you leave behind; the Caporetti are about what you bring back with you.<br /> <br /> There wasn\u2019t too much dev to do on this one, apart from adding the Into the Cold Dark Era, which was too perfect an implied pun to pass up (and, like, the themes an\u2019 shit).<br /> <br /> The only other thing I have to say about the Caporetti is that I wanted the colour palette of their character illustration to be that of a cheap pool toy. Judge for yourselves if I succeeded.<br /> <br /> Without further adieu, take a sleighride with the Caporetti:<br /> <br /> <b>Caporetti: The Ones Who Leave You Cold</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cLet it snow.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Blood is everything to the Kindred. The rush of fresh, hot Vitae over the tongue is better than any living pleasure, and they spend most of their endless nights in pursuit of more.<br /> <br /> However, one group of Haunts prefers their drink of choice on ice. Fresh Vitae burns the throats of the Caporetti; only the thick, syrupy blood pulled from the cold flesh of the dead is safe for them to consume. Fortunately, the Shivers are uniquely adapted to their strange palette, able to take far more sustenance from stored blood than their Kindred. Even more remarkable, they can preserve corpses with frigid arts that allow blood to remain viable for consumption long past the point it should congeal into sludge. Normally, a vampire can guzzle a cooler\u2019s worth and barely gain any sustenance, but a sip taken from a corpse preserved by a Caporetto is as nourishing as one taken from pumping arteries \u2014 they just can\u2019t do anything about the taste.<br /> <br /> Originating from a single mountainous region in Italy, the Caporetti have spread far and wide in modern nights, though they do still favor frigid climates. Called \u201cShivers\u201d (or \u201cSnowmen\u201d behind their backs), they were once a bloodline of hermits and urban legends leading isolated Requiems, their frozen pantries hidden by the driven snow and deep caves. As modern refrigeration technology became more ubiquitous, however, many Caporetti came down from the mountains to find the same abilities that allow them to survive all alone are now in high demand by the rest of the All Night Society.<br /> <br /> Over the last century, many Shivers have transformed from isolated spooks to procurement specialists, Vitae loan sharks, and even emergency medics. Not all Kindred can manage to hunt down a fresh meal every night or two, and for those willing to pay, Caporetti blood larders can provide a time-saving (if foul-tasting) alternative. Sure, the Snowmen are creepy, like all Haunts, and they\u2019re often difficult to reach, but they\u2019re also a way for a Lick to get a lot of blood in a hurry that doesn\u2019t involve murder. At least, not directly \u2014 those cold-storage corpses have to come from <i>somewhere</i>. Just make sure you pay for what you drink: The Caporetti may not be a formal crime family, but they\u2019re as brutal as any mafia about collecting what they\u2019re owed.<br /> <br /> Even in modern nights, some Caporetti still prefer to lead a more traditional existence, haunting ski runs, hiking trails, campgrounds, and other isolated spots where a few disappearances aren\u2019t going to be questioned. These Shivers enjoy the independence their powers provide them, able to sustain themselves on just a few victims for months, or even years. However, it\u2019s whispered among the bloodline that those who spend too long existing like this start to lose what makes them Kindred. The cold creeps deeper into their bones and warps them into something more elemental, but just as hungry. While it\u2019s rare enough that most Caporetti have only heard the tale second- or thirdhand, the term <i>ghiacciati</i> is muttered in industrial meat lockers and icicle-lined caverns across domains where the bloodline makes their frozen homes.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> Cold is the natural Kindred condition, so why not make it work for you? It\u2019s better to be needed than wanted, and the satisfaction when some pretty Serpent or stuck-up Lord crawls into our freezers with hat (and cash) in hand is almost as sweet as the blood itself. Or maybe you\u2019re just fucking <i>tired</i> of the rotting song and dance of our so-called \u201csociety.\u201d Well, we can give you a way to leave it all behind\u2026 for a while, at least.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> Most Licks don\u2019t remember what it\u2019s like to be really, truly cold. To have your hands shake so bad you can\u2019t hold a gun, teeth chattering so hard your fangs chip, to feel the blood turn to ice in your veins. Point being: Payment upfront when you want a snack, and the next time you see a KEEP OUT sign on a lonely, snow-filled trail? Obey it.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> The cold sets us apart, and if you give into it, it\u2019ll twist what little of you isn\u2019t a monster into something freezing and ravenous. Just because you can exist with nothing but snow and stolen life doesn\u2019t mean you should\u2026 but if warmth and life keep rejecting us, what else is there?<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan:</b> Nosferatu<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames:</b> Shivers, Snowmen<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Frozen Curse):</b> Shivers crave blood like all Kindred, but fresh Vitae can scald their frigid veins with its warmth. When a Caporetto feeds from a living creature (including ghouls), her player must roll Humanity. Success means the blood is merely uncomfortably hot as it goes down, but on a failure, the Shiver suffers bashing damage equal to half the amount consumed, rounded up. This damage cannot be reduced with Resilience or other supernatural powers. The Frozen Curse does not apply to feeding from Kindred, corpses, or deathly beings such as Sin-Eaters. In addition, Caporetti blood struggles to heat itself in counterfeiting mortality. When a Shiver uses the blush of life, she must spend two Vitae.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Celerity, <i>Nightmare</i>, Obfuscate, Vigor<br /> <br /> <b>In the Dark Eras (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Into the Cold \u2014 1961 CE (DE1, p. 530): </b>The Cold War keeps the temperature just right for Berlin\u2019s Shivers, who find they can remain safely apolitical as long as their supply chains are unmolested. Doesn\u2019t matter if you\u2019re a capitalist pig or a commie rat, everyone needs to eat eventually. Of course, there are Kindred in both East and West Berlin who distrust the Caporetti for \u201cfailing to choose a side,\u201d and some believe that, if they could take control of the Snowmen\u2019s business, appropriating their sizable blood stores, they could strike a blow against their ideological foes on the other side of the Wall.<br /> <br /> <b>Horror: Ghiacciati</b><br /> <br /> Something lurks in the Caporetti bloodline that hungers for more than just blood. A Shiver who spends too long subsisting on nothing but cold, dead Vitae runs the risk of turning into a flesh-eating creature of killing frost and ravening appetite. Referred to as <i>ghiacciati</i> (roughly, \u201cfrozen ones\u201d) among the bloodline, these beasts are akin to draugr, but their hunting patterns are much more destructive.<br /> <br /> A <i>ghiacciato</i> craves not just blood but also the meat of its victims, consuming them down to their very bones. What\u2019s more, the creatures are always hungry no matter how many victims they eat, perpetually searching for more flesh to fill their aching bellies. Inevitably, their hunger drives them out of their isolated environs and into more populated areas, where they\u2019ll proceed to kill and eat anything living they can get their fangs on. Left alone, a <i>ghiacciato</i> can slaughter an entire community and is a dire threat to the Masquerade. For these reasons, the Caporetti make sure the phenomenon stays secret as much as they possibly can, and keep tabs on the more isolated members of their line. If a <i>ghiacciato</i> is discovered, the bloodline handles it in-house, putting it down before it can do too much damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Systems</b><br /> <br /> [REDACTED]<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 09-23-2022, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-23T14:33:08-07:00","id":1493600,"title":"","content":"Yes! Caporetti time!<br /> <br /> It isn't exactly a secret that the Caporetti are my favorite bloodline. The idea of abominable snowmen vampires that are perfectly adapted to hunting in mountains just tickles my monkey brain, and their write up in <b>Ancient Bloodlines</b> is <i>so</i> evocative. I really like the fiction at the start of <b>Ancient Mysteries</b> that <i>sorta</i> suggests they might be older than the Great War. It gives them a subterranean, primeval quality that meshes nicely with the blood and snow aesthetic. It all just goes so well with what makes mountains scary! As I said earlier, I've been really looking forward to seeing NMD's take on them.<br /> <br /> And it does not disappoint! While the focus is no longer on bloodthirsty snow monsters, the new identity is slick and suits really contemporary and politically active character concepts. Even better, nothing about it actually keeps someone [me] from still playing them like mountaintop boogeymen. In fact, I think it makes it <i>easier</i>, since they can preserve the blood in corpses for later consumption, which is a neat trick in such a harsh environment. It is a smart way to take their larders, and not only mechanize them, but tie them back into the bloodline's identity through more than reputation. They are still the extremophile mountain vampires I love, but in a way that lets them come down and play with others more.<br /> <br /> I also like the way their burrowing Devotion was updated. I am firmly of the opinion that the Caporetti should not have Protean just because a couple of their old Devotions are now baked into the Discipline, and Beneath the Surface is a good compromise. It <i>basically</i> lets them do what they used to [minus wall crawling], but not in a way that steps on Protean's toes or requires them to lose Celerity [which I think is key to their horror]. It is also has great imagery, really upping the wintery cryptid vibes. I like it a lot. It is also basically a merit, even though it is a Devotion, and those are my favorite bloodline goodies.<br /> <br /> I quite like the new bane in general. I was a fan of the aura of oppressive cold from 1e, but mostly for visual reasons, so I'm not too sad to see it go. I can <i>almost</i> see a resources death spiral if a character gets really unlucky on the damage rolls while feeding at low Vitae, but it would require really contrived circumstances. It would probably also be a fun story to talk about later, if it did happen. It is also interesting that the bane doesn't apply to blood from the Bound. Not really going anywhere with that, I just think it is fun.<br /> <br /> This one really surpassed my expectations [not that I really kept any aside from a nebulous, &quot;it will probably be good&quot;]. I will probably use it over my own conversion in basically its entirety. Well, maybe not the Ghiacciati. Not because I don't like them; they are fun and chilling alternate draugr [and I think it is neat that the Trenchers get a revenant variant and the Shivers get a draugr variant], but because they bring a lot of extra stuff that I will not always want to deal with. Sometimes, being a vampire is enough of a threat to hold over a character's head.<br /> <br /> Also, gotta say, I love your art for this one. It is really goofy, but it works. He may not resemble the blue, skull-faced Caporetti from 1e, but he has just as much personality, imo.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-23T16:30:38-07:00","id":1493606,"title":"","content":"Do the Caporetti get ice/cold powers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-23T19:08:02-07:00","id":1493611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SomethingFishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1493600#post1493600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes! Caporetti time!<br /> <br /> It isn't exactly a secret that the Caporetti are my favorite bloodline. The idea of abominable snowmen vampires that are perfectly adapted to hunting in mountains just tickles my monkey brain, and their write up in <b>Ancient Bloodlines</b> is <i>so</i> evocative. I really like the fiction at the start of <b>Ancient Mysteries</b> that <i>sorta</i> suggests they might be older than the Great War. It gives them a subterranean, primeval quality that meshes nicely with the blood and snow aesthetic. It all just goes so well with what makes mountains scary! As I said earlier, I've been really looking forward to seeing NMD's take on them.<br /> <br /> And it does not disappoint! While the focus is no longer on bloodthirsty snow monsters, the new identity is slick and suits really contemporary and politically active character concepts. Even better, nothing about it actually keeps someone [me] from still playing them like mountaintop boogeymen. In fact, I think it makes it <i>easier</i>, since they can preserve the blood in corpses for later consumption, which is a neat trick in such a harsh environment. It is a smart way to take their larders, and not only mechanize them, but tie them back into the bloodline's identity through more than reputation. They are still the extremophile mountain vampires I love, but in a way that lets them come down and play with others more.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can <i>definitely </i>still play them as boogeymen; now they're just a little more liable to contribute to the All Night Society. I kind of want to run a chronicle with a bunch of Caporetti who are the vampire equivalent of the St. Bernard Hospice, with ghoul St. Bernards with little Vitae barrels around their necks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also like the way their burrowing Devotion was updated. I am firmly of the opinion that the Caporetti should not have Protean just because a couple of their old Devotions are now baked into the Discipline, and Beneath the Surface is a good compromise. It <i>basically</i> lets them do what they used to [minus wall crawling], but not in a way that steps on Protean's toes or requires them to lose Celerity [which I think is key to their horror]. It is also has great imagery, really upping the wintery cryptid vibes. I like it a lot. It is also basically a merit, even though it is a Devotion, and those are my favorite bloodline goodies. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, we ultimately felt that it wasn't worth changing around the Discipline spread just for one effect of Protean. I'm also just a fan of Nosferatu with Celerity; it's a frightening addition to their spread, and Celerity is arguably the spookiest physical Discipline.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I quite like the new bane in general. I was a fan of the aura of oppressive cold from 1e, but mostly for visual reasons, so I'm not too sad to see it go. I can <i>almost</i> see a resources death spiral if a character gets really unlucky on the damage rolls while feeding at low Vitae, but it would require really contrived circumstances. It would probably also be a fun story to talk about later, if it did happen. It is also interesting that the bane doesn't apply to blood from the Bound. Not really going anywhere with that, I just think it is fun. </div> </div> </div>I think you could read them as still having that, it just doesn't have a mechanical effect anymore. That said, you could also play a Caporetto with the Frost Touch bane from <b>Strange Shades</b>...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This one really surpassed my expectations [not that I really kept any aside from a nebulous, &quot;it will probably be good&quot;]. I will probably use it over my own conversion in basically its entirety. Well, maybe not the Ghiacciati. Not because I don't like them; they are fun and chilling alternate draugr [and I think it is neat that the Trenchers get a revenant variant and the Shivers get a draugr variant], but because they bring a lot of extra stuff that I will not always want to deal with. Sometimes, being a vampire is enough of a threat to hold over a character's head. </div> </div> </div>I'm glad we lived up to expectations! The author who did the Shivers did all the Nosferatu in the book (except the Order of Sir Martin), mostly because he's a big Haunt fan, but the Caporetti were definitely his favourites. They're actually in the chronicle he's currently running!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, gotta say, I love your art for this one. It is really goofy, but it works. He may not resemble the blue, skull-faced Caporetti from 1e, but he has just as much personality, imo. </div> </div> </div>When I got to the Caporetti illustration, I thought, &quot;What if instead of something cool or dangerous or sexy, we made this one a mafia guy on vacation?&quot;<br /> <br /> (I'll should take a post to talk about my art contribution at some point, because it very nearly killed me, but that's for another day.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1493606#post1493606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the Caporetti get ice/cold powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>They have some illusory (and not so illusory) Devotions to make people feel very, very cold.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-24T12:26:40-07:00","id":1493643,"title":"","content":"You know what, let's do one more for the week, and I'll take a day off on Sunday. Let's talk about the <b>Maiyarap</b>.<br /> <br /> This is a bloodline that went through a lot of changes from its original incarnation (pun unintended). Readers of <b>Ancient Bloodlines </b>will pretty quickly notice that we combined the Maiyarap with the <b>Sakadagami </b>covenant. This was for a couple of reasons: As per the sidebar I included on p. 71, we wanted to make the Treasures of Mae Ji more accessible to non-Thai characters. We were originally going to update the Sakadagami as a proper covenant, but I couldn't really find a hook for them that didn't leave them entirely regional; I'm sure there <i>is </i>a hook for them in the broader All Night Society, but I had trouble finding it. However, the writer assigned to the Maiyarap pretty early on asked if he could steal them away from me and combine the two, and that solved the problem pretty cleanly (work smart, not hard, that's what I always say.)<br /> <br /> The other reason that we discussed was that, all told, there wasn't much to the Maiyarap in the original write-up, as they were so strongly associated with the covenant already. So, it made sense to us to save some space and merge the two concepts. YMMV on that, but I think they ended up stronger together. And you can pretty easily use our updated systems with the old lore if that's your fancy.<br /> <br /> Apart from the big lore adjustment, the other change was their Discipline. Bhumisparsa is ultimately kind of a mashup of Celerity and Resilience, and we didn't feel a need to update it. Normally we try to add a little shoutout to the original Discipline if we're getting rid of it, but we felt the Treasures were a much more interesting and thematic advantage. Since the Maiyarap already had Resilience in <b>Ancient Bloodlines</b>, we considered just replacing Bhumisparsa with Celerity, but Auspex was a bit more thematic. Not quite a literal translation, but I think it's a better fit for the bloodline on the whole. And who doesn't like a religious fanatic Nosferatu who can read your sins with a glance?<br /> <br /> This one did go through a few changes in dev. The initial version was a tad too &quot;vampire Buddhists&quot;, so I asked the author to really amp up the body horror, which is a bit more Nosferatu. I also added the <i>i </i>to their name; it's a slightly more accurate transliteration of the demon they're named after; there were a few linguistic choices in the book I wanted to fix up (we'll talk a lot more about that when we get the Geihemen).<br /> <br /> Alright, that's it for me for the weekend (though feel free to throw me questions). I'll be back on Monday with more Nosferatu: <b>The </b><b>Order of Sir Martin</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Maiyarap: The Ones Who Teach You</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cAll desire must be released to reach enlightenment. Your desire to end this suffering is no different.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <i>He\u2019s back again tonight: the thin man with the shaved head, sitting crossed-legged by the side of the bus station. He\u2019s been there every night the past week, never seeming to mind the constant cold drizzle, even though he\u2019s only wearing a rough black robe. He speaks in gentle tones to those who pass, but you can never hear what he says from across the street. Most walk by without a glance, and you\u2019ve never seen anyone actually stop to talk.</i><br /> <br /> <i>You feel sorry for him, so tonight, you decide to cross the street, a cup of hot coffee in hand. He looks up as your approach, and his eyes are dark and still. He smiles. \u201cMay I teach you about dharma in exchange for a few moments of your life?\u201d The words are accented, but carefully rehearsed, so you understand well enough.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Not sure how to respond to this unexpected gravitas, you smile back and nod, just hoping that whatever he has to say won\u2019t take much time. The man begins speaking, and you realize he must be some kind of monk, as he speaks of enlightenment and \u201cmaking merit\u201d \u2014 whatever that is. You mostly nod along, mind elsewhere. When he finishes, you thank him and hold out the coffee.</i><br /> <br /> <i>He smiles again. \u201cYou\u2019re kind.\u201d The monk reaches out, but not for the cup, and his too-cold hand closes on your wrist in an unbreakable grip. \u201cThank you for sharing your life with me\u2026\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <i>That\u2019s when you realize that you didn\u2019t understand at all. </i><br /> <br /> Kindred suffer. They suffer from a craving for blood, from the rages of the Beast, from their very existence as dead things clinging to a semblance of Humanity.<br /> <br /> Kindred <i>cause </i>suffering. They steal life from the living and fight each other in a never-ending struggle for dominance. They ruin and kill in the name of both survival and politics. This is how it has always been, but the Maiyarap say it doesn\u2019t have to be. The Beggar Monks claim to have squelched their thirst, silenced their Beast, and are free of the need to advance at the expense of their peers. They say the way is long and difficult, but along it lies a Requiem where one no longer experiences \u2014 or is the cause of \u2014 the suffering endemic to Kindred existence.<br /> <br /> \u201cBullshit,\u201d is the near-universal response when the Maiyarap travel abroad with their claims, but the proof is in the message. Or the messenger, in this case. Other vampires witness Beggar Monks shrug off the most violent provocations to frenzy, ignore the most desperate blood dolls, and smile serenely through the disrespect inevitably slung their way. A few of those Kindred are intrigued enough to listen to what the Maiyarap have to say, though even fewer keep listening after the Beggar Monks describe burning limbs off with sacred pyres, or slowly removing their own internal organs by hand, and other harsh practices required to master their teachings. Still, the Maiyarap persist, extending a hand no matter how many times it\u2019s slapped away \u2014 they\u2019re serving something greater than themselves. <br /> <br /> In their native Thailand, the Maiyarap are an institution, and few question their teachings. The black-robed monks have operated out of their central temple of Wat Ning for centuries, and they\u2019ve expanded to many other temples and shrines throughout the country. The respect the bloodline enjoys originates with their founder, the notorious Naga Monk, a formerly tyrannical monster who spread suffering in Thailand for centuries as the Naga King before undergoing a radical conversion to Buddhism. The Monk exists in a state of barely contained fury, his near-constant meditation and total commitment to mindfulness the only things holding his monstrous nature at bay.<br /> <br /> While the Naga Monk accepted his tenuous existence, his childer seek a better Requiem for their sire and believe they can balance his dharma by making merit in his name, using the methods he taught them. \u201cMaking merit\u201d is an integral concept in Buddhism, a beneficial force that accumulates as a result of good deeds, acts, or thoughts. Essentially, the Maiyarap believe that if they do enough good in the name of their founder, he can be fully redeemed and move on to a higher state of being. This belief is behind the bloodline\u2019s recent efforts to spread its teachings beyond Thailand and into the wider world. It\u2019s also bred a brutally utilitarian view of ethics; a Coiled Snake won\u2019t hesitate to snuff out innocent life or cause immense suffering if he believes his actions will prevent greater evil in the future, and thus create more merit for the Naga Monk. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s in pursuit of this holy mission that the Beggar Monks depart from where they\u2019re respected to spread their teachings in places where they\u2019re mocked and ignored \u2014 the places most in need of enlightenment, in their reckoning. Behind their gentle smiles, however, lurks unyielding zealotry. Not every convert to the Maiyarap\u2019s teachings is a willing one, and more than one Lick claims to have a Haunt coterie-mate who went missing only to turn up years later with a black robe and many, many scars\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> Do you really? Consider carefully, as the road to enlightenment is long and painful \u2014 most fall to ashes before they complete it. However, the agony of the journey can free you from craving, and thus from the suffering you feel every night. Torment is a small price to pay for serenity.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> We would rather not be feared, though we appreciate respect. Of course, a reluctance to do harm does not equate to an inability to do so. We no longer share the same weaknesses, but we have strengths you can\u2019t conceive. Humbling you will require penance, but we have a very long time to balance the scales. <br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> We have a responsibility to the Naga Monk to make merit in his name, but do our methods actually make us better Kindred, or are we simply more polite monsters? Is it possible for creatures whose existences rely on suffering to ever create less of it? The best of us consider this question nightly, but thus far, we have no answer. <br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan: </b>Nosferatu<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames:</b> Coiled Snakes, Sakadagami (\u201conce-returners\u201d), Beggar Monks (abroad)<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Curse of Detachment): </b>The Maiyarap teach that letting go of all cravings will pave the way to enlightenment. However, some of the things Kindred crave, such as acceptance and community, are what help them cling to their Humanity, and denying them makes it harder to hold on. A Beggar Monk [REDACTED]. Due to this, Maiyarap hold themselves to exceptionally high standards of behavior and self-control, knowing they cannot count on attachments to others to stave off the Beast.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b><i>Auspex</i>, <i>Nightmare</i>, Obfuscate, Resilience<br /> <br /> <b>Treasures of the Mae Ji</b><br /> <br /> The Naga Monk became the Mae Ji\u2019s student, and he was able to halt his slide into total degeneracy from what he learned. He passed these teachings onto his childer, who\u2019ve spread this philosophy across Thailand and beyond in an attempt to redeem their repentant founder.<br /> <br /> The practical results of these teachings are the <i>Treasures of the Mae Ji</i>, states of being that permanently alter a vampire\u2019s mind and body. On a surface level, the Treasures resemble the Coils of the Dragon, but their methods differ greatly. The Coiled Snakes aren\u2019t scientists; they\u2019re philosophers. They use meditation, asceticism, and the recitation of sutras to hone their forms, with a focus on enduring intense physical suffering to strengthen the mind.<br /> <br /> To an outsider, the Maiyarap\u2019s methods may seem crude, or even needlessly cruel. Initiates are often made to remove their own limbs and leave them for the sun to better understand the impermanence of all things, and many supplicants fall into torpor or meet Final Death while training. All of this is an acceptable price to the Maiyarap, for they understand that to suffer in the name of making merit is a merit-making act in and of itself, and thus benefits the dharma of both student and teacher.<br /> <br /> There are three Treasures recognized by the Maiyarap: Anicca (Impermanence), Dukkha (Suffering), and Tahna (Thirst). Anicca is identical to the Coil of the Ascendant and Dukkha is the same as the Coil of the Wyrm, though the Maiyarap focus on harshly taming the Beast rather than growing closer to it. The Mystery of the Voivode is unknown to the Coiled Snakes.<br /> <br /> All Maiyarap may purchase Treasures for the same cost as Coils of the Dragon. They must choose a favored Treasure, but this confers no cost break, and Status in their bloodline limits the number of dots a character can learn in other Treasures. Treasures and Coils that alter the same aspects of the Kindred condition are incompatible with each other, and so no character can ever purchase both Coil of the Ascendant and the Treasure of Anicca, Coil of the Wyrm and the Treasure of Dukkha, or Coil of the Voivode and the Treasure of Tahna. Theoretically, mixing the studies in other ways is possible; for example, a character could learn the Coil of the Wyrm from the Ordo Dracul and the Treasure of Anicca from the Maiyarap.<br /> <br /> <b>Treasured Terminology</b><br /> <br /> Like the Dragons, the Sakadagami have unique titles based on their mastery of different Treasures. A beginning student who has learned up to the first two tiers of a Treasure refers to herself as having \u201ca mind like an open sore.\u201d A more advanced learner identifies as having \u201ca mind like a flash of lightning.\u201d Finally, a master of all five tiers of a Treasure can claim to have \u201ca mind like a diamond.\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>Tahna: The Thirst</b><br /> <br /> This Treasure focuses on releasing Kindred from their most powerful craving. Students of this Treasure routinely starve themselves of Vitae, and are forbidden from feeding on blood that is not offered freely in order to learn both patience and humility. Diamond minds of this Treasure can subsist on minuscule quantities of blood, and it is through Tahna that the Naga King denies the weight of true torpor despite his immense age.<br /> <br /> <b>Denial \u2022</b><br /> <br /> The first step in forgoing cravings is to cease forming new ones, for yourself or others. By spending a point of Willpower, the vampire\u2019s Vitae does not cause blood addiction for the rest of the evening. Furthermore, she enjoys a bonus equal to her dots in Tahna to any rolls made to resist Vitae addiction. <br /> <br /> <b>Hunger\u2019s Silence \u2022\u2022</b><br /> <br /> [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>Grains Fall Gently \u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <br /> [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>Pass Between Chains \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <br /> [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>Blood of All \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <br /> [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-24T14:12:21-07:00","id":1493646,"title":"","content":"An interesting approach about the Maiyarap/Sakadagami situation. Honestly I generally feel that a covenant offers a wider range of options than a bloodline so my preference is have them as such, but as you said it is easy to adapt them using the mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-24T16:25:19-07:00","id":1493648,"title":"","content":"The Treasures are a nice contrast with Coils, like how it leaves the possibility of getting both as long as they don't overlap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-24T21:58:09-07:00","id":1493661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TrueMrMultiverse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1493648#post1493648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Treasures are a nice contrast with Coils, like how it leaves the possibility of getting both as long as they don't overlap.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Indeed, The dynamic also opens up room for STs to experiment with their own ideas of regional covenants or mystery cults that delve into into peculiar combinations of Coil-like arts or teachings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-24T22:06:35-07:00","id":1493662,"title":"","content":"Meanwhile, the pseudo-Coils being named \u2018Treasures\u2019 gets a +1 from me. Really shows how they\u2019re a (vampirically corrupt) Buddhist cult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-25T00:43:49-07:00","id":1493663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1493661#post1493661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Indeed, The dynamic also opens up room for STs to experiment with their own ideas of regional covenants or mystery cults that delve into into peculiar combinations of Coil-like arts or teachings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something I've tried to emphasize through all these books is that the Ordo Dracul is only the best at <i>creating </i>Coils, but it doesn't have a monopoly on possessing them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1493662#post1493662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile, the pseudo-Coils being named \u2018Treasures\u2019 gets a +1 from me. Really shows how they\u2019re a (vampirically corrupt) Buddhist cult.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always liked that too. There's a really compelling, subtle corruption that permeates their whole concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 09-25-2022, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-25T14:49:09-07:00","id":1493680,"title":"","content":"me reading the Twice Cursed bloodline<br /> &quot;Oh she's so pretty.... HOLY FUCJ&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-25T16:24:42-07:00","id":1493688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1493663#post1493663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Something I've tried to emphasize through all these books is that the Ordo Dracul is only the best at <i>creating </i>Coils, but it doesn't have a monopoly on possessing them.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is a quite fair take of it, imho. Who knows how many times some of the Coils or similar ways of dealing with the banes of kindred existence have been found, lost and rediscovered in a form or another by undead of multiple cultures before the coming of the Ordo with its proto-scientific methodology to bring its own spin into the exploration of that field?<br /> <br /> Damn, the Dragon i played in the last Requiem game i was part of had a mindset possibly closer to the black monks than scientist in how he delved on kindred nature, though he was neither buddhist or particularly monastic in any way or form.<br /> <br /> I also remember once playing with the Coil of the Locust and the attainments of 1e Tremere liches in sketching out a version of sorts for the kindred line or mystery cult that inadvertently spawned them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-25-2022, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-25T16:44:13-07:00","id":1493690,"title":"","content":"...You know what could be scarier than a <i>ghiacciato</i>? A <i>Claimed <i>ghiacciato</i></i>. The thought of Belial's Brood &quot;recruiting&quot; Shivers through force-feeding them frozen blood is definitely a scary one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-25T22:18:47-07:00","id":1493704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1493611#post1493611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can <i>definitely </i>still play them as boogeymen; now they're just a little more liable to contribute to the All Night Society. I kind of want to run a chronicle with a bunch of Caporetti who are the vampire equivalent of the St. Bernard Hospice, with ghoul St. Bernards with little Vitae barrels around their necks.<br /> [...]<br /> I'm glad we lived up to expectations! The author who did the Shivers did all the Nosferatu in the book (except the Order of Sir Martin), mostly because he's a big Haunt fan, but the Caporetti were definitely his favourites. They're actually in the chronicle he's currently running!</div> </div> </div> </div>This has got me wondering how people actually <i>use</i> bloodlines in their games, which I have never really thought about before! My group has historically stuck with just the core book, which barely has anything on bloodlines, so we've never done anything with them [and the clans are so rich on their own].<br /> But I think this is its own thread! If it hasn't already been discussed a thousand years ago in 2014 or something, that is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (I'll should take a post to talk about my art contribution at some point, because it very nearly killed me, but that's for another day.) </div> </div> </div>!!!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1493680#post1493680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">me reading the Twice Cursed bloodline<br /> &quot;Oh she's so pretty.... HOLY FUCJ&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, isn't she dreamy?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-26T11:29:23-07:00","id":1493751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SomethingFishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1493704#post1493704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has got me wondering how people actually <i>use</i> bloodlines in their games, which I have never really thought about before! My group has historically stuck with just the core book, which barely has anything on bloodlines, so we've never done anything with them [and the clans are so rich on their own].<br /> But I think this is its own thread! If it hasn't already been discussed a thousand years ago in 2014 or something, that is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've found they come up a lot. I'm actually in a chronicle right now, and the ST basically said &quot;Take a bloodline if you want it&quot; and we all fell for the siren call of a fourth in-clan Discipline. We're a Malocusian, a Macellarius, a Nelapsi, and a Von Schreck.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> !!! </div> </div> </div>I exaggerate (slightly). Basically, I had to (read: foolishly made myself) do almost <i>20 </i>illustrations, including bloodline logos, and I've never been so exhausted. And that was even with me splitting some of the work with another artist (he did the outlines, I did the shading/painting/colouring). But, that's a story for a different day!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, isn't she dreamy? </div> </div> </div>She's got a great smile... But, I digress. Let's talk about the <b>Order of Sir Martin</b>.<br /> <br /> In a quirk of development, all the Nosferatu bloodlines were written by one author \u2014 except for the Order of Sir Martin, who went to a different author. Originally. Unfortunately, that other author had to drop out pretty early on in production (for entirely understandable reasons), so I ended up taking on his material rather than hiring someone else; we were just a little too far in, and I'd more or less finished my own writing work, so I figured I'd save some back and forth. Originally, I was just writing the Corajosos, because, for some reason, on every single project, I fool myself into thinking I'll do a bit less writing and a bit more admin. I like writing, and (I like to think) I'm good at writing, but I find it to be a very tiring process, whereas my brain is not as taxed by art, editing, etc. Cut to me doing 5 bloodlines instead of 1.<br /> <br /> <i>Anyway</i>, this is all to say, despite the sudden new workload, I found a hook for this bloodline almost right away. I've always liked the Order of Sir Martin, and my version is ultimately not <i>too </i>different from the First Edition version. &quot;Knightly Nosferatu who are so repugnant they serve as secret police&quot; is a very fun idea, and while I think the original doesn't <i>quite </i>take that far enough, it was a solid basis to build new stuff. My main issue with the original was that it was a bit too on the nose; I wanted their low status in the Invictus to be a bit more complicated.<br /> <br /> The big change was making their advantages mostly Merit-based. Specifically, Oaths. I <i>love </i>Invictus Oaths. They're such an interesting mechanic, and there really isn't anything like them in any other CofD game (I need to find more reasons to do two-way, asymmetric Merits). So, it made sense to me that the Order of Sir Martin, being ostensibly knights, would have a lot of their own Oaths, and the liege/vassal structure of those effects gave me the idea of them being designated Scapegoats for the First Estate: Want to be the life of the party? Go see a Leper. Need to hide your diablerie? The Martinists will do it. Happily! All they ask is the freedom to do their work, and the lower they fall in the Invictus \u2014 the more oaths they take to be punching bags while you party in the Ivory Tower \u2014 the better they get at it. That allowed me to make their &quot;Leper&quot; designation more metaphorical, but also very <i>deliberate </i>on the bloodline's part. This also allowed me to adjust their bane, which is the only thing in the original I more or less just changed outright. Instead of, uh, dyspepsia, their Lonely Curse is worsened, and they have difficulty making Socialize actions with other Kindred. I <i>almost </i>had the Nos bane apply to other vampires, but A) we've done that before (with the Azerkatil, I believe) and B) I didn't want them to be <i>too </i>screwed socially by default considering what some of their Oaths do to them.<br /> <br /> The other thing I wanted to do was give them a bit more of a reason to be in other covenants, but without breaking their ties to the Invictus. I did consider just making them more mercenary, but I liked the idea of them having their own Oaths, which are actually probably the hardest covenant advantages to rip off (maybe apart from Carthian Law?) So, I gave them a loophole (see below).<br /> <br /> So, here's the Order of Sir Martin. I'm including a few extras in this one, as their intro is a bit short, and I think showing a little more of their mechanics will give you all a better sense of how they work.<br /> <br /> Tomorrow, let's take a break from the Nosferatu and check in on the Shadows: the <b>Iltani</b>. As always, like and subscribe consider leaving us a review if you're enjoying the book!<br /> <br /> <b>Order of Sir Martin: The Ones You Blame</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I die to serve.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Everyone needs a fall guy.<br /> <br /> The Invictus was built on the idea that you can get ahead by stepping on the little people, so it should come as no surprise that this includes other members of the First Estate. Few Unconquered think twice about this fact, and fewer still would be bothered much if they did. Of course, resistance is also part of climbing that ladder. Reaching the top means fighting for it at every rung, and for each victory you earn, another Lick is waiting a few feet below to scramble past your corpse as you fall. You can\u2019t really expect Kindred to just roll over for you.<br /> <br /> Ah, but that\u2019s where you\u2019d be wrong. The Order of Sir Martin will let you shit on them with a smile. Indeed, as one of the oldest knightly organizations of the First Estate, these Haunts are professionally obligated to take your abuse. Scapegoats in the most literal sense of the word, public derision and ostracization are this bloodline\u2019s primary sources of strength, and with their own special Oaths, the so-called Leper Knights assume the mantle of their lieges\u2019 sins to grow ever more powerful. To serve the Conspiracy of Silence and the Masquerade, a Martinist becomes anathema to her Kindred: Contemptible. Repugnant. Beneath notice\u2026<br /> <br /> But only fools judge Lepers by their appearance rather than their reputation. Intellectually, if not emotionally, the Invictus knows the burden these knights take on is fictitious (at least in part), but the Conspiracy of Silence also knows how powerful a well-told story can be. Who would think the sanitation worker reeking of raw sewage is the deadliest and wealthiest assassin in the city? Who would suspect the shy secretary whose presence feels like absence of being the finest swordswoman in the state? And who would ever believe the ranting, pockmarked derelict who uses the stoop as a toilet is the master of the largest spy ring in the country?<br /> <br /> In other words, it\u2019s not bad work if you can get it. Haunts whose curses would otherwise relegate them to the margins of the First Estate \u2014 and the All Night Society \u2014 find acceptance among the Lepers, turning their personal horror into a valuable and deadly asset. However, knighthood is a privilege, not a right. The Order only takes those Haunts it deems worthy, and just having a particularly crusty skin condition won\u2019t cut it. Their training regimen puts the Marine Corps to shame, a physical, mental, and spiritual crucible that, at the best of times, amounts to torture. But one can\u2019t argue with results. Leper Knights are some of the most elite secret police in the Invictus, and even those Unconquered who openly deride them are careful not to earn their wrath, or say anything incriminating in their presence.<br /> <br /> The Lepers know where all the bodies are buried, and they can and will dig them up when it serves their purposes, whether in defending the Masquerade or fucking with their self-proclaimed betters. Just the suggestion of their presence is enough to set a prince\u2019s teeth on edge, and even in domains where the Order has no official presence, it can exert a surprising amount of influence \u2014 after all, how would you ever know we\u2019re here?<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> Because no one else wants you. No one can see the strength behind the squirming skin or the jet-black eyes. They call you a leper already, so why not become one in truth? There\u2019s power in being at rock bottom; that\u2019s where everyone winds up in the end, and you can be there first, mouth wide open.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> We can\u2019t sink any lower than this, and if you don\u2019t think that makes us dangerous, our blades will make quick work of your ignorance. Remember: The rules don\u2019t apply to us \u2014 but they do to you.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> The problem with being everyone\u2019s punching bag is that your start buying into the press. Maybe you really are only good for killing and creeping. Maybe you really <i>are </i>just a worm who managed to wriggle ahead of all the other worms. What you think you are is far less important than what everyone else believes.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Origins</b><ul><li>When the Crusades came to the Holy Land, the violence awakened a Nosferatu known as Martinus Leprosus, a legionnaire of Rome who was killed and Embraced into the Army of the Damned during Titus\u2019s siege of Jerusalem. An outcast among his Kindred for both his allegiance and the awful blight that covered his skin, Martinus believed survival meant being too disgusting for anyone to look too closely at what you\u2019re doing. The ancient liked the invaders, for they reminded him of his nights as a soldier, and he began to use them as a herd when they slaughtered most of the local populace. He learned much from the pilgrims, and he soon Embraced a handful so they might teach him of modern, holy warfare. Taking on the titles and rites of a Catholic military order, \u201cSir Martin the Leper\u201d and his knights began a campaign of slaughter on behalf of any who could pay their price, spreading their philosophy of power through repugnance to any Haunts who would listen. Eventually, the Invictus proved to be their most reliable customer, and it\u2019s been a lucrative hate\u2013hate relationship ever since.</li> <li>The legend of Sir Martin is just that: a legend. The first Leper Knights belonged to a powerful faction of Invictus Nosferatu that controlled vast domains in the Levant during the Crusades. Fearing their growing influence, the First Estate tricked them into a massacre, using mercenaries to decimate their numbers. Humiliated and chastened in defeat, they were forced to swear new Oaths, ones that guaranteed they would never again claim prestige or power in the Invictus. However, even in defeat, these Haunts knew they\u2019d only lost the battle, not the war. They crafted the story of Sir Martin as a rallying cry for other Nosferatu, a way to teach them to revel in their repulsiveness so the Establishment won\u2019t ever realize what they\u2019re really up to.</li> <li>Once upon a midnight darkly, a pious knight-errant searched the whole world over for the Holy Grail. He fought many battles and rescued many maids, but none brought him any closer to his prize. Eventually, he came upon a loathly lady, who told the knight she knew the secret of the Grail, but that she would not reveal it unless he married her. The gallant agreed, and on their wedding night, he asked the hag to fulfill their bargain. In a blinding light, she transformed into a beauty without peer, revealing she was the holy prize he sought. However, he could only keep her if he passed a final test: to choose whether she should be comely in the day and hideous in the night or lovely in the moonlight and frightful in the sun. The knight replied that she should choose for herself, for a wife should always have her <i>sovereynt\u00e9</i>. Oh, how his lady smiled! And so, she chose to be beautiful day and night, and with the sacred blood from her bosom, she fed her loyal knight all her hideousness. Thus he serves his wife and sovereign still \u2014 loathsomely ever after.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Parent Clan:</b> Nosferatu<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Leper Knights, Lepers, Scapegoats, Martinists<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Blighted Curse):</b> They ain\u2019t called lepers for nothing. Whatever a Scapegoat\u2019s flaw before her becoming, it magnifies in Sir Martin\u2019s blood: A Leper Knight treats her Humanity as an additional dot lower for the purposes of the Lonely Curse. In addition, Socialize actions with other Kindred [REDACTED]. The latter effect does not apply to other Lepers, nor to vampires who know the Scapegoat <i>very </i>well, such as coterie-mates, mentors, retainers, etc.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b><i>Nightmare</i>, Obfuscate, Resilience, Vigor<br /> <br /> <b>New Invictus Oaths</b><br /> <br /> The following are Oaths available only to Leper Knights. Squires must swear the Oath of the Scapegoat (p. 81) to join the Order, and if they ever break it, all other Martinist Oaths are considered null and void. Any Notary can preside over these Oaths, and any member of the Invictus can act as the liege unless otherwise noted, but only a Scapegoat can be the vassal.<br /> <br /> In addition, due to the Order\u2019s rigorous training, Scapegoats who meet the prerequisites gain a dot of Kindred Dueling for free. If she has five dots already, she takes an Experience instead.<br /> <br /> Note that not all Leper Knights are Nosferatu. While rare, Invictus members of any clan can join the Order of Sir Martin if they can prove themselves, though only Haunts can be inducted into the associated bloodline, which tends to occupy a place of privilege, such as it is.<br /> <br /> <b>Oath of the Oprichnik (\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisite</b>: Obfuscate \u2022<br /> <br /> <b>Effect: </b>Even beyond their supernatural repugnance, the Order of Sir Martin is hated and feared for its secret police services, and this Oath is the source of that reputation. With the Oath of the Oprichnik, the vassal swears to protect the Silence even at the cost of her identity.<br /> <br /> A high official of the Invictus (often a prince) serves as liege, representing a kind of stand-in for the Masquerade itself. The vampire becomes no one, gaining the Forgotten Condition. As long as this Condition lasts, she gains the rote quality on Perception, and any Investigation actions to track Masquerade breaches exceptionally succeed on three successes instead of five. Finally, since she is considered to have Face in the Crowd active at all times, she can treat Cloak of Night and The Familiar Stranger reflexive actions, as well as any other non-instant effects that rely on it.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s very rare for Leper Knights to swear this Oath for longer than a few weeks at the very most, or for the duration of a particular investigation, as such intense isolation invariably leads to\u2026 issues.<br /> <br /> <b>Forgotten (Persistent)</b><br /> <br /> [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>Oath of the Scapegoat (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Effect: </b>The vassal becomes a member of the Order of Sir Martin, with the Order itself serving as her feudal liege. This Oath is always administered as a Nosferatu is inducted into the bloodline.<br /> <br /> Oath of the Scapegoat effectively serves as Kindred Status for the bloodline and its knightly order. A character who swears it loses any Invictus Status (Sanctity of Merit apples), but her player can use dots in this Oath to purchase benefits that scale with Invictus Status or have it as a prerequisite.<br /> <br /> For each dot in this Merit, the character suffers a penalty on all actions with Invictus members where Covenant Status would normally apply, but she also [REDACTED GOOD THING].<br /> <br /> This Oath\u2019s duration is indefinite, but it breaks if the Leper ever gains a dot of Invictus Status.<br /> <br /> Oath of the Scapegoat is an exception to the drawback of the Oath of Penance (<b>Vampire</b>, p. 117); it cannot be obviated in any way by normal Invictus Oaths.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Rank is a commodity among the Lepers. Each time you want to increase your dots in this Oath, your character must have it renewed by a Notary with the permission of a superior in the Order.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 09-26-2022, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-26T15:02:10-07:00","id":1493779,"title":"","content":"For some reason, the phrase \u201cREDACTED GOOD THING\u201d makes me chuckle more than it should <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-26T17:02:53-07:00","id":1493784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1493779#post1493779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For some reason, the phrase \u201cREDACTED GOOD THING\u201d makes me chuckle more than it should <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Gotta have my fun where I can!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-27T12:10:52-07:00","id":1493843,"title":"","content":"Alright, let's have a look at the Iltani.<br /> <br /> This is one of the rare Mekhet bloodlines I didn't know that much about before we got writing. I think that may be because they have one of the sparser write-ups (only two pages), with most of their word count going toward their backstory (which is elaborated in <b>Ancient Mysteries</b>), followed by a long section on M\u00e9rges Sorcery. Ultimately, they end up coming off as a riff on the Banu Haqim from <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b>. There's not much to the original Iltani, so the big goal here was to elevate their concept beyond that of poisonous assassins, which was especially tricky given that that's what the Brothers of Ypres are. The Trenchers are slightly different poisonous assassins, but they're also much more <i>interesting </i>poisonous assassins.<br /> <br /> This is all to say that I think the author really nailed this one. The Iltani in Second Edition aren't assassins so much as &quot;cleaners&quot; for the gods. They aid the Kindred by guiding them to following the laws of the universe \u2014 the fundamental strictures of civilization \u2014 thus preventing creatures like the Strix and... other... agents of anarchy from taking advantage of any moral hiccups. They hesitate to kill, but when they have to, they're well equipped.<br /> <br /> Which brings us to M\u00e9rges Sorcery. In the original, this power was essentially Theban Sorcery with a poison twist. It's also the only case where a 1E bloodline had access to a form of sorcery that wasn't part of their Discipline spread, which is not important but I find interesting (I have a theory about that, but it's just wild guessing). Anyway, it's got some interesting enough powers, but we ultimately felt it was too narrow in concept for a Ritual Discipline, especially because I have a possibly-too-rigid rule about including new sorcery Disciplines in books: they've got to have 10 rituals. The way I see it, the whole point of a Ritual Discipline is that you have different options at each level, and to my mind, you have to have at least two for each dot to have any sort of meaningful choice.<br /> <br /> As you might imagine, that rule broke pretty hard against M\u00e9rges Sorcery. There are only so many ways to do poison, and ten was just too many. I believe I had the suggestion of turning it into a set of special rituals for Cr\u00faac or Theban Sorcery, but that also lacked the flavor of the original bloodline. So, the author decided to turn M\u00e9rges Sorcery into M\u00e9rges Admixture, a Merit, giving the bloodline Protean to represent that &quot;Viper&quot; aspect. in hindsight, I wish I'd thought to give them some snakey/spidery Protean powers in dev, but you can ultimately repurpose the ones in the core or <b>Wild Hunt</b>.<br /> <br /> The other big change was their bane. The original is actually not too bad, but it feels like something that would come up just a bit too often to be fun. Despite wanting them to be a less like the Banu Haqim, I actually think the bane they ended up with suits them really well.<br /> <br /> Not too much changed in development; I fussed with the Merit a bit, and I added another one (the animal ghoul one), and I swapped around their bloodline gift a bit to tie into their emotional removal a bit more strongly. The biggest changes I made were to the Edimmu, their associated horror; mostly that was just simplifying them a bit, though.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I could honestly go on about how great I think this update is and all the concepts that went into it, but I know the author lurks on the forums, and they had some really interesting background on the mythological and cultural elements this new version draws upon, so they're free to add some context to what I've said here.<br /> <br /> Anyway, here are the Iltani! As noted in an earlier post there's a discrepancy with the Discipline spread, which will be corrected in the errata. I also noticed their bane is slightly different from what I had in my final dev file, and combined with the Discipline mistake (and a couple of other discrepancies), I suspect that means I copied the wrong file somewhere along the line. So, that will also be fixed, but you'll have to wait for me to get through the previews, as those are helpful for me to catch typos and such. The bane below is the correct version.<br /> <br /> Tomorrow, I'll be back with the <b>Shepherds</b>!<br /> <br /> <b>Iltani: The Ones Who Despise You</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cDon\u2019t waste your words on me. I\u2019ve seen what\u2019s inside you.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Hatred is so stigmatized. We\u2019re taught to fear our anger and swallow it down from the time we\u2019re children. The truth is, hatred is a natural part of the human condition, and what\u2019s natural for humans is natural for vampires. As fortune would have it, the Kindred are especially attuned to hate.<br /> <br /> In Sumerian theology, the gods gifted humans with the <i>me</i>, the qualities necessary for civilization. More than just the ability to create architecture or laws, the <i>me </i>drove conflict: enmity, warfare, and fear. Without these, humans would never be forced to confront that which needs to change. They would lie indolent in the fields, doing only what was necessary to survive and provide comfort. Strife, too, is one of the <i>me</i>, and this is what the Iltani embody. Anger is useful. You just have to point it in the right direction, whether your own or someone else\u2019s. So go ahead. Give in \u2014 just this once. It\u2019s in your blood, and there\u2019s so <i>much </i>to rage against.<br /> <br /> The Iltani have always lurked at the corner of civilization\u2019s visions, and they claim to have been born at its very dawn. In the shadows of Babylon\u2019s walls, most lurked as ashipu, gods-blessed physicians who could banish evil spirits through magical concoctions. Rather than proper physicians one might visit in a temple, they were a last resort whose names and deeds were spread through rumor, and rather than the medicinal herbs a mortal ashipu might use, they used the powers of the Blood. They\u2019ve gone more underground since then, but spirits haven\u2019t gone anywhere in the past few millennia. Nothing will save you when one comes to pay a visit, and there are some that are very, very interested in the Kindred.<br /> <br /> This necessitates keeping up certain standards of behavior, and the Iltani expect their fellow Licks to do the same. Most of these protocols are enshrined within the modern-day Traditions, but one outweighs all others in terms of importance: There is no sin greater than the Amaranth. It opens the soul to things that should not be there. Alu. Edimmu. Strix. The Widows know just how dangerous the arrival of any one of these evil spirits might be, even if others don\u2019t. Best to never risk their appearance. Unwise Kindred must be guided on the proper path and become the right kind of monster.<br /> <br /> This has given them a slightly unwarranted reputation as venomous alchemists and dark sorcerers. They\u2019re happy to let these rumors remain in place, however; it helps that the distinction between magical practice and medicine was blurred in their earliest nights, when they worked as ashipu. Despite their repute, Vipers are unusually hesitant to kill, given that corpses tend not to make useful tools of the <i>me</i>. For the Iltani, frenzy and hatred have swallowed deep into their being and curdled into a very literal toxin. This means they have a shockingly long fuse for a bloodline so fixated on the power of hatred and fear. Falling to frenzy without being able to control it is a serious sign of weakness.<br /> <br /> It would be a mistake to think of the Widows as anything approaching merciful, though. Like most Shadows, they prefer not to get their hands dirty. They have ways of making sure their targets\u2019 sins are exposed, and those who can\u2019t channel their negative impulses for a righteous cause deserve whatever punishment\u2019s coming to them.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, just because the <i>me </i>are no longer inscribed on clay tablets for people to read doesn\u2019t mean they\u2019re not necessary. The veneer has changed \u2014 different faces, different names, different words \u2014 but the human mind remains the same, and the gifts the gods gave humanity abide. So do the Iltani. Younger Widows may no longer adhere to a specific list, and they might not teach it as a divine imperative, but the general philosophy remains. The modern concept of dialectics has provided a useful framework to explain and justify it, and this allows them to root out certain weaknesses and vices within the Kindred. They say there are terrible forces that might seize hold of the All Night Society. Civilization is built on certain cruelties\u2026 yet the alternative is far worse. But they would say that, wouldn\u2019t they?<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> Absolute control is within your grasp, and that\u2019s a rare thing for any Kindred: control over your anger, over others, over the very physical nature of your being. You just have to reach out and take it.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> But <i>you</i>, of course, are not so refined. It\u2019s so easy to push your buttons. Your weaknesses are written so clearly on your face and in your every action. And if you can\u2019t keep a grip on yourself? We\u2019ll be there.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> The truth is, absolute control is impossible. Human psychologists have managed to piece together that trying to bury your emotions is a lost cause. They\u2019re still there, and no matter how much your own twists of the blood alchemize them, you\u2019ll never, ever completely cage the Beast. And when you fail, and you\u2019re drained dry, there\u2019s something else that will step in to take your place.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan: </b>Mekhet<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Vipers, Widows<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Hemolytic Curse): </b>The hateful blood of the Iltani does not take well to intrusion. If a Viper ingests Kindred Vitae, whether willingly or otherwise, she suffers a bashing damage per point. Furthermore, the tendency of Mekhet blood to draw in strange secrets and occultic qualities exerts itself, and the Widow gains one acquired bane that the vampire she drank possesses until it inconveniences or harms her, at which point, it fades. This bane does not apply to drinking the Vitae of other Vipers.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b>Animalism, <i>Auspex</i>, Obfuscate, <i>Protean</i><br /> <br /> <b>In the Dark Eras (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> <b>One Thousand and One Nightmares \u2014 832 CE (DE2, p. 124): </b>The Iltani no longer hold a vice-grip over Middle Eastern civilization as their elders claim they once did, and to make matters worse, the secrets of the All Night Society leak out through the visions of mere mortals, and the Vipers\u2019 dreams are filled with fire coming to the domains of the Damned. It\u2019s clear they need to emerge from the shadows at last. They form strange alliances with the children of nightmares but fear that this might be the end of everything that the Iltani and lesser Kindred have fought for. Elders prepare for the worst in a massive upheaval that may tear away the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Gift: Focused Hatred</b><br /> <br /> An Iltani can focus her poisonous hate into a kind of Zen state to aid in her work. Once per night, when facing a provocation to rage frenzy, a Viper can spend a Willpower to take the Stoic Condition. She must still resist frenzy, but she immediately benefits from the effect of Stoic. Some Iltani only use this ability when facing dire situations, while others deliberately provoke themselves in order to attain calm.<br /> <br /> <b>Stoic</b><br /> <br /> Your emotions turn as cold as your dead heart and lifeless veins, and you find it difficult to open up or show any emotion at all. Gain a +2 on rolls to hide your emotions or resist rage frenzy, and do not take the Tempted Condition on a normal success. However, your Humanity is treated as though it were two dots lower for the purposes of relating to mortals. This Condition fades without resolving at the end of the night.<br /> Resolution: Fall to frenzy.<br /> <br /> <b>New Merit: M\u00e9rges Admixture (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Iltani, Medicine \u2022\u2022, Safe Place \u2022<br /> <br /> <b>Effect: </b>The line between magic and medicine was often blurred in ancient Mesopotamia. Some illnesses were said to be caused by evil spirits, and exorcisms were necessary to banish the offending creature. When the Iltani were still young, they practiced medicine following this principle, as though it were a religious ritual, and the end result is that their gift for alchemizing poisons is often mistaken for a primitive form of blood sorcery. While this isn\u2019t true \u2014 it\u2019s a natural process of their bodies rather than witchcraft \u2014 but it\u2019s a misconception the Iltani have let persist to keep up a more sinister reputation.<br /> <br /> The creation of a M\u00e9rges Admixture (from a Sumerian word meaning anger or poisonous) requires alchemizing the vampire\u2019s own Vitae. Many perform ritualistic actions as their blood transmutes to keep up traditions, whether it be invoking long-lost gods, consuming herbs they claim to have magical qualities, or making a sacrificial offering. The creation of a venom inflicts one level of bashing damage on the vampire per turn it takes to achieve the target successes. Unless noted otherwise, the venom must be injected to work. Nothing prevents the vampire from coating her own fangs to use them as makeshift syringes, but most Widows prefer to have greater control over when and where their venom is used.<br /> <br /> However, it\u2019s not unheard of for Iltani to turn their own poisons on themselves. Most have certain benefits, at a steep cost, but desperate times call for desperate measures, especially when facing off against their ancestral enemies.<br /> <br /> [REDACTED]<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-27T15:07:36-07:00","id":1493862,"title":"","content":"I guess the Iltani would have much to discuss with the Arisen\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-27T15:28:41-07:00","id":1493867,"title":"","content":"Iltani, risen again! Interesting. I wonder if their most ancient roots link with Ki-En-Gir.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-27T15:45:35-07:00","id":1493868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1493862#post1493862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess the Iltani would have much to discuss with the Arisen\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1493867#post1493867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iltani, risen again! Interesting. I wonder if their most ancient roots link with Ki-En-Gir.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's funny, we had a lot of <b>Mummy </b>references in this book, mostly because it's just the most natural connection for vampire stories with historical themes, but the Iltani are perhaps an obvious one where the Arisen <i>didn't </i>come up. I considered adding a plot hook for them for the Dark Era I added, but ultimately, I didn't want to skew too hard to that one gameline. That said, I think there's a <i>lot </i>you could do with them considering the details of their bloodline origin(s).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 09-28-2022, 01:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-27T15:50:19-07:00","id":1493869,"title":"","content":"I really hope future Mummy 2e books go into more detail about the Ki-En-Gir. What <i>does</i> 1/3rd divine even <i>mean</i>? How did they rival Irem? What magics were at their disposal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-27T19:36:02-07:00","id":1493879,"title":"","content":"And now that I remember my password...<br /> <br /> That one is mine! Yay! While I would have loved to bring in some connections to Mummy 2e, unfortunately I was already leaning in <i>hard</i> on it with one of my other bloodlines and I was worried about things getting same-y. Also, my regular gaming group would have teased me for being predictable given Mummy is one of my favorite games and I love crossover-friendly content. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Quick crosspost of some things I said on another forum and my Twitter for posterity:<br /> <br /> I'm a religious studies major (recently graduated as of a few months ago so I'm now allowed to call myself one, I guess) and by sheer coincidence my comparative mythology class did a unit on Mesopotamian (including Babylonian and Akkadian) mythology which is where about 80% of the inspiration for this came from. I'm pretty sure you could audibly hear the gears starting to grind back to life in my brain once I read that &quot;strife&quot; was one of the several dozen. The me are very dialectical in nature, and the concept of traits that we almost always think of as negative being a positive thing that helps with building civilization felt like it'd fit in with their M.O. really well. As for their practices, evil spirits are a major presence in Mesopotamian and Babylonian mythology...not to say that they aren't in most cultures, but as my professor put it, in ancient Mesopotamia your physician was likely your priest. Ailments were often blamed on wicked spirits. I decided to tie that back into the Iltani being less practitioners of magic and more early chemists and alchemists. And I like it when there's some flexibility with powers so I made it so that they have certain niche uses if you use them on yourself if you're willing to accept the drawbacks.<br /> <br /> Let's see, what else. Their earliest draft had them taking Vile Blood from Guide to the Night as a free Devotion. That got ditched because we didn't want to force people to buy non-core books, and honestly it wasn't as compelling as something wholly customized anyways. If anyone decides to use them, though, I'd say it'd be fair to allow them to buy it at a reduced cost, it is very them.<br /> <br /> And a side note entirely unrelated to my design process: their first creation myth does go back into an actual myth, the Atra-Hasis. According to that the gods created humans to tend to the land. I was having a fun time with reading Mesopotamian mythology so I kept going and decided to bring in one of my favorite mythological chimeras, the scorpion-men. The third one...well, all I can say is I can never resist a crossover concept.<br /> <br /> But yeah, the original one was a little sparse on the ground so I kind of just went wild with it. I'm happy it came together like it did! :&gt; It probably took the longest out of all of mine but I think it paid off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raziel MacPhereson, he/they | <a href=\"http://twitter.com/beastsoulfury\" target=\"_blank\">Twitter</a> | <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Raziel%20MacPhereson\" target=\"_blank\">STV Content</a> | <a href=\"https://huntunderironskies.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Tumblr</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23812-cherubic","name":"Cherubic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23812_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-27T20:08:37-07:00","id":1493882,"title":"","content":"Iltani, those guys really hit on memory lane. Curiously, the one time i used them was not as Mekhet but a Akhud bloodline instead (along with the branches of the Betrayed from VII).<br /> <br /> - Mashed up Ahranite and Merges Sorcery into one ritual system.<br /> - The ghosts that served as guides of the Betrayed became hollow-esque &quot;daughters of Shadad&quot; in the process.<br /> - Shadad became a Blood Mary/Red Jack kind of entity acting by proxy through his daughters and stealing the reflections of his descendants, mortal or kindred. Some of those would, through its blessing or theft from the morsels of wisdom peppered in rambling whispers, learn the secrets of the Maze of Mirrors (Ars Speculorum, that i did as a merit tweaking Obfuscate, much like Of Rose &amp; Thorn for Animalism).<br /> - The Maze of Mirrors <b>also </b>existed as a literal citadel of mirror-polished brass walls that existed in no certain place, disappearing and reappearing between fallen world, shadow and beyond (that i admit, stole from the Glass Mansion in pages 60-63 of Reliquary)<br /> - Ekkimu i turned into a sort of &quot;weaponized hollows&quot; created through rituals, potions or infusions. Though sometimes Lilitu (owls), vipers (kind of inspired in the chapter from Mythologies mixed in with the Zmai from Predators, i think) or scorpions would come out instead.<br /> <br /> And a bunch of other things, mostly riffing from <i>Mythologies</i> bits &amp; pieces i utterly fail to remember (and seem to have lost the notes for, unfortunately).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-28-2023, 08:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-27T23:45:25-07:00","id":1493889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1493867#post1493867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iltani, risen again! Interesting. I wonder if their most ancient roots link with Ki-En-Gir.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ki-En-Gir is another name for Sumer. Since Ancient Bloodlines/Mysteries features Iltani in Babylon, it's possible they could have Sumerian roots if they're just old enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-28T10:14:20-07:00","id":1493909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1493882#post1493882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iltani, those guys really hit on memory lane. Curiously, the one time i used them was not as Mekhet but a Akhud bloodline instead (along with the branches of the Betrayed from VII).<br /> <br /> - Mashed up Ahranite and Merges Sorcery into one ritual system.<br /> - The ghosts that served as guides of the Betrayed became hollow-esque &amp;quot;daughters of Shadad&amp;quot; in the process.<br /> - Shadad became a Blood Mary/Red Jack kind of entity acting by proxy through his daughters and stealing the reflections of his descendants, mortal or kindred. Some of those would, through its blessing or theft from the morsels of wisdom peppered in rambling whispers, the secrets of the Maze of Mirrors (Ars Speculorum, that i did as a merit tweaking Obfuscate, much like Of Rose &amp; Thorn for Animalism).<br /> - The Maze of Mirrors <b>also </b>existed as a literal citadel of mirror-polished brass walls that existed in no certain place, disappearing and reappearing between fallen world, shadow and beyond (that i admit, stole from the Glass Mansion in pages 60-63 of Reliquary)<br /> - Ekkimu i turned into a sort of &amp;quot;weaponized hollows&amp;quot; created through rituals, potions or infusions. Though sometimes Lilitu (owls), vipers (kind of inspired in the chapter from Mythologies mixed in with the Zmai from Predators, i think) or scorpions would come out instead.<br /> <br /> And a bunch of other things, mostly riffing from <i>Mythologies</i> bits &amp; pieces i utterly fail to remember (and seem to have lost the notes for, unfortunately).</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds <i>awesome</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-28T10:43:06-07:00","id":1493910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1493909#post1493909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This sounds <i>awesome</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks a lot. I do enjoy getting lots of bits and pieces from several books and having fun with putting them together in all kinds of bizarre ways to get the players by surprise when the crypto-lore rears its head, along with a fun homebrew trick or two for them to learn or steal too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-28T10:49:32-07:00","id":1493911,"title":"","content":"Baaldam:<br /> <br /> Did crossover ever enter your thoughts, while using the Iltani like that? That sounds like some serious Shadow shenanigans, right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-28T11:06:51-07:00","id":1493913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1493911#post1493911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Baaldam:<br /> <br /> Did crossover ever enter your thoughts, while using the Iltani like that? That sounds like some serious Shadow shenanigans, right now.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Somewhere in the middle, so to speak - my games and ideas tend to be overall very much Requiem-centric but that doesn't mean i can't add some elements more common to Forsaken, Awakening, Lost or others, like realms of existence outside the average person's keen, ephemeral beings and a variety of peculiar antagonists, rivals or potential allies.<br /> <br /> But overall for kindred it's mostly one of the many layers of the Underworld, dreams and sometimes one's Temenos through Torpor - yes, also meaning that there are kindred who are familiar with Goetian demons, to a degree that might surprise and bother a number of Awakened. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> With also some stuff that exists somewhere between such realms or actual physical places, like the Maze of Mirrors previously mentioned, or Yurema, an ancestor-realm connected to trees sprung from branches of a certain kind of south american wood when used to stake the undead. The sprout turns into a sarcophagus-tree of sorts engulfing the undead, the sap of these trees being usable as Lacrima or a component of a number of occult rituals done by families of ghoul-like shapechangers of supposed native american descent (though quite distant in some cases) that guard such trees as sacred and sometimes hunt kindred to &quot;return to sleep&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-28-2022, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-28T11:08:46-07:00","id":1493914,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t suppose this \u2018mirrored palace\u2019 has anything to do with Chur, does it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-28T11:20:23-07:00","id":1493916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1493914#post1493914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t suppose this \u2018mirrored palace\u2019 has anything to do with Chur, does it?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not familiar with. My main inspirations in devising the Maze of Mirrors were the chapter on Red Jack &amp; Blood Mary from Mythologies, the Mekhet clanbook's info on Hollows (that would inspire me ideas on update the previous) and the update &amp; expansion to Blood Mary (possibly connecting her to CtL's Hedge) given in Danse Macabre. Ah, and as previously mentioned, the Glass Mansion from Reliquary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-28T11:26:39-07:00","id":1493917,"title":"","content":"Ah. Well, Chur is the so-called \u2018Seventh Watchtower\u2019 the Tremere liches once held. \u2018Twas a thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-28T11:28:30-07:00","id":1493918,"title":"","content":"And Yurema sounds pretty effing cool. Probably a euphemism for very unique Avernian Gates, or <i>sonething</i> to do with the Underworld, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-28T13:07:20-07:00","id":1493928,"title":"","content":"Let's talk about the <b>Shepherds</b>! (I will second that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1147_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1147\" data-vbnamecard=\"1147\">Baaldam</a>'s remix of the Iltani sounds <i>awesome</i>, though).<br /> <br /> This is a bloodline that was very low on my radar; Gangrel bloodlines are not my expertise, and I actually forgot they were in the book before I started writing my outline. I actually think they have a really cool concept, especially for Gangrel, but they end up being outshone by the Sta-Au, who are by far the cooler of the two Montrose Party bloodlines.<br /> <br /> With that said, the big direction here wasn't radical change so much as adding more meat to the bone. I really liked the &quot;gray hat&quot; mood of their original write-up, and that they're very explicitly not made out to be the &quot;good guy&quot; vampires. As such, this was probably the most straightforward update in the book, with a few more plot hooks in their backstory (I'm a big fan of the Origins section on this one). The biggest change is their bane: Their original weakness pretty much went straight out the window; it wasn't bad in concept, but we really didn't feel it fit for this particular bloodline. So, the author added a little twist to the Bestial Curse, and I think it ties in much more strongly with their themes and their reputation. The author had a Twist in the first draft offering an alternate bane that conformed in spirit (if not mechanically) with the old bane, but I felt that the one we ended up with was leaps and bounds more interesting, and I didn't feel a need to retread the previous version.<br /> <br /> The other big adjustment was expanding their power set, giving them an inherent gift as well as some Merits and a new Devotion. Some of those are based on the original material, but we gave everything a 2E shine.<br /> <br /> Not too much else to say about the Shepherds. They're a solid bloodline in <b>Ancient Bloodlines</b>, so we didn't feel a need to rework them too much beyond giving players more options.<br /> <br /> So, here are the Shepherds. Tomorrow, let's look at a <i>new </i>bloodline: the <b>Vetala</b> of Clan Nhang.<br /> <br /> <b>Shepherds: The Ones Who Corral You</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Behave, or this'll get unpleasant right quick.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Many Kindred exist in abundance, which breeds recklessness. And when junkie bloodsuckers get reckless, this often leaves the sorts of messes behind that spook mortals. When the herd is spooked, all Kindred lose. Thus, the so-called Shepherds take on a responsibility akin to their namesakes among the kine, protecting human flocks as a herdsman might do with cattle and sheep. This isn\u2019t normally so literal; the Watchers don\u2019t keep pens of humans they occasionally let out to graze, but many of the same concepts apply when standing security in the city\u2019s hottest nightclub or directing a convenient flash mob \u2014 although some Shepherds <i>do </i>get involved in \u201canimal husbandry,\u201d but this isn\u2019t common.<br /> <br /> Just as with mortal shepherds, what these Savages do isn\u2019t out of kindness, but pragmatism. Shepherds (both mortal and dead) need their herds for sustenance, and it simply won\u2019t do to butcher your cattle when you can first take milk. Mortals have much more to offer than their blood. Of course, that doesn\u2019t keep the Watchers from developing deeper relationships with parts of their herd, just like farmers sometimes have prize heifers.<br /> <br /> The commonly accepted founder of this lineage is one Greta Devenpeck. She was the only vampire who escaped the destruction of the Montrose Party, a group of settlers traveling along the Oregon Trail that was accompanied by Kindred hoping to establish domains in the West. Great misfortune befell the Party, but Greta escaped, and with the lessons she learned and the change these challenges wrought in her blood, she soon gathered the first coterie of what would become the Shepherds.<br /> <br /> Being Savages, Watchers are both the shepherd and the sheepdog. While they typically make for gentle guides, they can lash out with shocking violence against any wolves who would threaten their herds \u2014 as well as at any disobedient \u201csheep.\u201d Corralling humans requires a special kind of social engineering that involves many tools. A little fear of the dark here; the comfort and safety under the Watcher\u2019s gaze there. But even when a Shepherd must be harsh, she must always appear as an anchor of safety to the kine. She must be able to gauge how any disturbance could impact her flock and how to counteract threatening influences. For some Shepherds, this turns into all-consuming obsessions as they manipulate relationships and even whole family trees.<br /> <br /> The attitude they bring to their work doesn\u2019t help their reputation, however. In many domains, other Licks ridicule the Herders as spoilsports and softies. This doesn\u2019t usually lead to any institutional harassment, but altercations between Shepherds and rowdy Kindred aren\u2019t unheard of. In some cases, these conflicts grow to encompass the domain as a whole, and the local Shepherds are forced to move on, sometimes taking their herds with them.<br /> <br /> For this and many other reasons, self-righteousness is common to Shepherds. Whether they feel they\u2019re the only ones capable of long-term thinking, or genuinely see themselves as heroic, Herders often have trouble leveling with their Kindred. Occasionally, a Watcher styles herself as an avenger of the kine, taking her sanctimoniousness too far for even other vampires to bear. Few domains will suffer vigilantes for long.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> Kindred rarely get to feel like they\u2019re saving lives and keeping order in the world, but we do. Yeah, the others talk shit about ulterior motives and pragmatism, but is it so bad to keep the apple cart running and the body count low? Didn\u2019t you ever wanna be the Good Guy going Savage on a bully? Well, guess what: There are a lot of bullies in the All Night Society.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> Livestock handling isn\u2019t just beer and massages, like you\u2019re some prime Kobe beef. The herd needs to be kept docile and oblivious. That\u2019s what we do, and we have to do it subtly. The only ones who should fear us are our shortsighted kin. It\u2019s all fun and games till you have to tear up some motherfucker who doesn\u2019t check himself. The kine are way quicker learners.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> Does the milk cow appreciate being slaughtered later than the steer? Maybe. Not like she gets much of a choice. Seeing mortals that way dehumanizes them more than the occasional \u201cfeeding accident,\u201d and being the designated killjoy in a world of dead yahoos doesn\u2019t always make for a great time either. Just all the more reason to let out the inner Savage after all.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Origins</b><ul><li>The Montrose Party were one of many groups of settlers traveling the Oregon Trail in the 19th century, and with them, a coterie of young Kindred. It quickly became clear that protecting every single mortal was vital for survival, as each life lost was a major cut in the blood supply. Ultimately, they failed. Like many migrants who took on the arduous journey, many died to hardships, and those who were left were picked off by the Sta-Au (p. 87), remarkably monstrous vampires native to the region who haunted the Party over its last few nights. At least one vampire survived, however: Greta Devenpeck. While sharing the adversity (and blood) of the Montrose Party, she developed a special link with her herd. This brought a deep understanding of how important it is for Kindred to not unduly harm or spook their food supply, and from there, she found likeminded Savages who would protect the kine for the long-term benefit of all Kindred.</li> <li>There never were any vampires in the Montrose Party. What an idiotic idea, that Kindred would cram themselves among just a handful of mortals over miles of wilderness! And even if some were stupid enough to try, they surely met Final Death in short order through accident or discovery. Maybe the reason why you can\u2019t find the Montrose Party in any history books is because it never existed at all. A Kindred fiction to teach an oblique lesson \u2014 or to hide a darker truth. Whether or not the Montrose Party existed, the Shepherds certainly do. As do the Sta-Au. The truth is, the Sta-Au call themselves \u201ctwice-dead\u201d for many reasons, both poetic and bloodcurdlingly real. The first Shepherds were what was left behind when a Wicked One decided to die her third death. This separated any human decency still left within her from her monstrosity, allowing the Sta-Au to become one with the Land of the Worms. The Shepherds are still monsters, but they\u2019re the better part of what was left behind.</li> <li>The Montrose Party <i>did </i>exist as the Kindred tell it, but the important thing is that the \u201cConquest of the West\u201d wasn\u2019t really a mortal project at all, nor even a Kindred one. The Great Will, in its immaculate calculations, determined that the settling and industrialization of the American continent were of vital importance. That adventurous bloodsuckers would try to hijack this project wasn\u2019t accounted for, but It understands how to fit an errant cog into Its Grand Design. Through Its agents and portents, It effected a bonding between mortal and immortal, and created servitors who would forever help maintain sublime stability and order among the unruly and erratic dead. Humans who selected to further Its design should not fall prey to the fickle variable of the dead, nor should they have reason to fearfully look at what\u2019s concealed around them. The Watchers fulfill an important role, but there aren\u2019t enough of them yet. They must spread. Carefully.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan:</b> Gangrel<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Watchers, Herders<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Vigilant Curse):</b> Shepherds protect their herds and, by extension, all mortals with a watchful ferocity, and their Beasts have adapted to protect this precious food source against any threat. Any overt violent action toward a mortal by another vampire or supernatural being is a frenzy trigger with a modifier commensurate with the severity of the transgression. This does not apply to self-defense or subtle feeding, but only if the act doesn\u2019t inflict the Drained Condition. If the victim is part of the Watcher\u2019s herd (e.g., represented by the Herd or Feeding Ground Merits or determined by domain law), [REDACTED].<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b>Animalism, Obfuscate, <i>Protean</i>, Resilience<br /> <br /> <b>In the Dark Eras (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> <b>The Great War \u2014 1914\u20131918 CE (DE2, p. 390): </b>It\u2019s only natural the Shepherds follow their herds wherever danger awaits them. While only a handful of Watchers (mostly from the Canadian prairies) make the journey across the Atlantic, that\u2019s vastly more than any other group of North American Kindred. They take on masquerades as medics and nurses, or even drill sergeants who wake their charges at night for \u201cspecial\u201d training. Many serve the war effort as hidden presences, angels of the battlefield who whisper in young men\u2019s ears to get out of the way just as the shelling starts. Some Embrace posthumously in order to bolster their numbers, and many of these neonates remain in Europe after the war, hoping to shepherd the herd into a lasting peace\u2026<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-28T14:31:35-07:00","id":1493933,"title":"","content":"I like how both the Shepherds and the Sta-Au's Gifts interact with Humanity. There's also some duality in the Banes: Violence in their surroundings also affects the Shepherds while violence caused by the Sta-Au bleed out into the surroundings. It's just a minor thing but I think it's neat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-28T15:10:54-07:00","id":1493935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1493933#post1493933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like how both the Shepherds and the Sta-Au's Gifts interact with Humanity. There's also some duality in the Banes: Violence in their surroundings also affects the Shepherds while violence caused by the Sta-Au bleed out into the surroundings. It's just a minor thing but I think it's neat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I really like that parallel too. There's a fun affinity between them, even beyond what was baked into the original versions. We actually talked about giving the Shepherds Auspex instead of Animalism, which would've given them the same Disciplines as the Sta-Au (and tied more concretely to that second origin), but I ended up feeling like it would've been too pat, and that their original combination was ultimately more thematic; a bloodline of herders pretty much <i>has </i>to have Animalism.<br /> <br /> I also really wanted to make an image incorporating the two bloodline illustrations (lasso vs. machete!), but time did not allow.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-28T16:55:19-07:00","id":1493939,"title":"","content":"I<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1493536#post1493536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, let's look at the Sta-Au. From a distance.<br /> <br /> This is one of the very, very few &quot;any/multi-clan&quot; bloodlines from First Edition, which for some reason was a thorny issue in early <b>Requiem</b>. Infamously, the Moroi bloodline write-up includes a sidebar that goes out of its way to declare that they're in fact two bloodlines that are exactly the same. To a lesser extent, then Mortifiers of the Flesh made you jump through several hoops if you wanted to play a non-Daeva. At any rate, that reluctance seems to have tapered off by the time <b>Ancient Bloodlines </b>came out, because there don't seem to be any caveats about who can join. At any rate, this is all to say that I like all-clan bloodlines. I feel like a future project might be to do a book of them, although I have to admit I'm a little bloodline'd out at this juncture.<br /> <br /> Anyway, my big directive for the Sta-Au was to make them more playable. Their original weakness was that they could never buy back Humanity which, uh, certainly scales with that trait, but is maaaaaaaybe a little harsh; direct quote from my outline: &quot;Boy their bane goes hard.&quot; It's a weakness that's interesting in concept but in practice (and with apologies to the sidebar on p. 35 of <b>Ancient Bloodlines</b>) mostly relegates them to Storyteller character territory, in which case that particular weakness doesn't really matter anymore. I'm sure one could play a Sta-Au with their original bane, but even ignoring how narrow it is, it's a tad boring. As such, I really like their new bane. We have a few more &quot;externality&quot; banes in this book (e.g., the Brothers of Ypres, the Nehebkau), in that they don't directly affect the character, but still influence behaviour. This bane also integrates the Land of the Worms more intimately with the bloodline, making them direct vectors for its spread.<br /> <br /> Speaking of the Land of the Worms, I'm really happy with how our version turned out. It's not too heavy mechanically, but it's a bit more modular than the original. I'm a big fan of Mysterious Places, so I'm always happy to fit them in where we can.<br /> <br /> I don't have much to say about the development process here, as not too much changed from the final draft apart from a couple of tweaks here and there. This was one of the bloodlines that was really solid right from the start. My only major addition was adding an additional Dark Era (the Lifting of the Veil one), as well as the &quot;Who We Are Tonight&quot; list. My biggest contribution was mostly the art.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I believe the author wanted to talk a bit about the writing process here, so I'll end on that note.<br /> <br /> So, here are the Sta-Au. As always, if you like the book, consider leaving us a review. Tomorrow, let's finish the week with the chilling <b>Caporetti</b>...<br /> <br /> <b>Sta-Au: The Ones Who Slaughter You</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Wolves to them; sheep to us.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Across the Great Plains, Kindred tell tales of the Sta-Au, ashen-skinned boogeymen with jagged teeth like rows of knives, covered in trinkets and trophies of human bone. This bloodline makes its home in the inhospitable badlands of the region, where all trespassers are dealt with accordingly. \u201cNormal\u201d vampires in the area cleave to humans as much as possible, spending their nights in cities and only traveling on heavily trafficked roads if possible; anything to avoid facing the Sta-Au and their hunting parties, or coming across the skull-adorned borders of the Land of the Worms.<br /> <br /> The Wicked Ones live up to their moniker. They have no regard for morality, instead celebrating depravity and cruelty as if they were virtues. The Sta-Au act as if they\u2019re the Beast incarnate, seemingly giving in to every dark urge and instinct with abandon. Yet unlike the draugr, they\u2019re not mindless monsters incapable of higher reasoning \u2014 which only serves to make them more insidious.<br /> <br /> The Sta-Au take their name from the ghosts of Blackfoot belief, the wicked dead who choose to harry the living instead of passing on to the Great Sand Hills. Unlike their incorporeal counterparts, the Wicked Ones believe all vampires have failed to properly die, reprobates eternally stuck in their corpses. To break free from these shackles, the Sta-Au die a second time, bringing themselves ever closer to a true death. After that, it\u2019s just a matter of finding the passage to an afterlife befitting such vile creatures as vampires and, finally, proving worthy of entrance.<br /> <br /> The Sta-Au\u2019s afterlife is said to link to the locations collectively known as the Land of the Worms (p. 91). It\u2019s within the Land of the Worms that Sta-Au traditionally dwell, reinforcing its ruinous resonance and preparing themselves for what lies beyond. By deliberately and carefully shedding each remaining scrap of his mortal life, a Wicked One shall become a pure monster, unfettered by any inhibitions yet not reduced to a simple animal. When he\u2019s freed from the limitations of his Humanity, the Twice-Dead sheds his human body and enters his new hunting grounds.<br /> <br /> True monsters don\u2019t abide by any rules, but until the Sta-Au can escape their immortal coils, rules serve a crucial purpose. As a group, the Sta-Au would\u2019ve self-destructed long ago were it not for the traditions and customs they developed centuries ago. One seeker\u2019s path to transcendence shall not interfere with another\u2019s, and a threat to one\u2019s road is a threat to all. While violence is the natural way to settle conflicts between Wicked Ones, it\u2019s ritualized, and the victor is expected to respect their opponent\u2019s defeat. Even bitter rivals cease their attacks once the other lies in torpor, and they even band together should another Twice-Dead break one of their few taboos, or fail their quest and fall to the Beast.<br /> <br /> However, not all Sta-Au are committed to anarcho-primitivist deaths in the wilderness. As the American frontier drew to a close, towns and cities boomed. During the Great Depression a few decades later, hunting parties discovered the Land of the Worms could manifest in built-up areas, such as derelict industries and abandoned residencies. Since then, more and more Wicked Ones have made their homes in urban environments, though not without adaptation. Rather than existing in bands separate from the All Night Society, they hide by intermingling with the uninitiated \u2014 joining mixed coteries and even participating in the covenants.<br /> <br /> This is not to say traditional Sta-Au are rigid and unchanging. Elders expect new blood to adapt to their brutal ways, with scarification and the filing of one\u2019s teeth being common ways to show dedication to the goal of transcendence, but individuality is otherwise encouraged. New ideas just mean new possibilities to explore \u2014 and ultimately, the goal is for <i>you </i>to become the best monster you can be.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> The first death cursed you. You\u2019re caught in the world of the living, unable to break free of your invisible bonds and move on. You play make-believe and hide behind petty schemes. It\u2019s pathetic. We discard all these meaningless pursuits, fetters that would keep us from reaching our true potential. We know what we\u2019ve become, and we\u2019ll show you how to become more.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> Your second death is a promise. The world is violent, and sooner or later, everyone dies for good. Sooner if you give us a reason. But we aren\u2019t beasts who attack on sight. We act deliberately. With reason. Just make sure to always treat us with respect, stay out of our way, and never, ever show weakness. If you can do that, you\u2019ll be fine.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> Our third death lies ahead of us. We know the path. We only need to reach beyond the Land of the Worms and grasp our reward\u2026 but the path is narrow and treacherous. Violence begets violence, and many of us perish before we ever reach our goal. We celebrate our dark desires and denounce our vestigial Humanity, but without restraint, they will surely destroy us, and only darkness will be our reward.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan: </b>Any<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Twice-Dead, the Wicked Ones<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Ruinous Curse):</b> The Sta-Au are creatures of defilement and destruction, both physical and moral, and wherever they go, they bring this nature with them. Whenever a Wicked One suffers a breaking point or causes another to suffer a breaking point against Humanity or Integrity, roll her Humanity. On a failure, the location around them suffers the Spiritual Infestation Tilt.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b><i>Auspex</i>, Obfuscate, <i>Protean</i>, Resilience<br /> <br /> <b>Spiritual Infestation (Environmental Tilt)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Description: </b>The curse of the Wicked Ones has infested the area. It eats through the spiritual foundation of the world, perforating its structure and leaving nothing but refuse behind.<br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> The area takes on the traits of the Land of the Worms. When this Tilt is applied, the area suffers the Spiritual Blight Aspect (p. 93). Additional breaking points suffered within the same area reset the Tilt\u2019s duration, and if a breaking point leads to the loss of Humanity or Integrity, the area gains an additional minor Aspect (Potency 1, if needed).<br /> <br /> If the area would gain a fourth Aspect, it\u2019s major. At this point, the area is at the cusp of deteriorating into a true Land of the Worms. Provided the location is not otherwise unfitting (such as being populated or heavily trafficked by humans or wildlife) a single significant push will end the Tilt and create a Land of the Worms at Potency 2.<br /> <br /> <b>Causing the Tilt: </b>A Sta-Au suffers or causes a breaking point.<br /> <br /> <b>Ending the Tilt:</b> The Tilt ends after a number of nights equal to the Sta-Au\u2019s Blood Potency times the number of Aspects that currently apply to the area.<br /> <br /> <b>In the Dark Eras (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> <b>A Handful of Dust \u2014 1933\u20131944 CE (DE1, p. 470):</b> Amid economic hardship and ecological disaster, the Sta-Au became yet another scourge afflicting the Midwest. Barren fields, abandoned factories, and storm-struck towns allow the Land of the Worms to grow at an unprecedented rate. The Sta-Au are quick to follow, and they find unlikely rivals. Animated piles of dust and detritus, also known as Dust Devils, have no aversion to the Land, and they stalk the same human victims as the Wicked Ones. They\u2019re also strangely drawn to the dead who dwell in Twilight\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Gift: A Path Between Worlds</b><br /> <br /> The Wicked Ones do not act as they do due to blind faith alone. No, they see clearly what lies ahead of them. Every step they take on their journey of transcendence is clear.<br /> <br /> The first step is as simple as opening your eyes. As soon as a Sta-Au joins her new siblings, she also starts perceiving the dead who were freed from their physical forms yet still linger in the world of the living. Ghosts in the state of Twilight (see <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b>, p. 124) appear as if physical to her \u2014 only their muted colors and lightly distorted voices betray their true insubstantiality. Other entities and phenomena of ghostly ephemera are similarly visible.<br /> <br /> As she sheds more and more of her chains, the Wicked One unlocks additional benefits along the path. As long as her Humanity does not exceed five dots, she can shift her body into Twilight as per the following systems:<br /> <br /> [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I consider this canon in my games. If it actually <i>is</i> canon, all the better. All the wonderful awfulness of 1e\u2019s Belial\u2019s Brood, yet heavily reflavored into something less overtly demonic.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> A thought just occurred to me. A while back, another poster here created a homebrew system for \u201cEmbracing\u201d Wyrm Nests, turning a room-sized area into a dark, twisted, cancerous version of reality. It was a <i>really</i> extensive writeup. I remember really loving the whole thing.<br /> <br /> Though that writeup was for the Ordo Dracul, the Tumors of Nowhere Cells can be reflavored for the Sta-Au, instead. It would certainly add to the lore presented here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 09-28-2022, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-29T12:34:42-07:00","id":1493987,"title":"","content":"Alright, today, let's talk about some new blood: the <b>Vetala</b>.<br /> <br /> All the new bloodlines went through a bit more development than the old ones; the major benefit of working from previous material is that a lot of the groundwork is already done for you, so making something <i>wholly </i>new is always a different beast, especially when we're talking about lost clans, who don't have the literal decades of background the standard-issue ones have. So, it took a bit more work to get these new bloodlines where we wanted in comparison with the &quot;Ancient&quot; bloodlines. The Vetala were no exception, mostly because the Nhang, while a really cool concept, are one of the weirder lost clans. &quot;Water vampire&quot; is definitely a trope, but it's just narrow enough that we had to work a bit harder to find a natural expansion of that concept.<br /> <br /> To that end, I think we ended up with something really cool and thematic with the Vetala. It's not a long walk from water vampire to swamp thing vampire, and the author had a really interesting idea in framing them as classic movie monsters. Unlike, say, the Nosferatu, where they represent your deepest personal fears and fundamental prejudices, the Troglodytes are the externalities of human hubris (like so many movie monsters), evolving with technology and pollution and culture. They're what happens when you dump toxic waste in the lake and it wakes up hungry for blood.<br /> <br /> Obviously, that steps a bit into Gangrel territory, but we thought of the Vetala as being a very modern phenomenon, whereas the Gangrel are more primordial and (in a sense) natural. That said, it's hard to escape the archetypes, and if you wanted to play them as a Savage bloodline, I don't think that would be a stretch. You could pretty easily map all the new bloodlines to the basic clans if the lost ones don't fit into your chronicle, which is partly why we did five; not <i>just </i>because there are five in <b>Spilled Blood</b>!<br /> <br /> The big dev changes were their mechanics. Making vampires hard to kill is a surprisingly delicate dance; you don't want things to just be unfair, but you don't want them to be only nominally tougher than regular vampires. Protean and Resilience also cover a lot of &quot;this isn't even my final form&quot; territory, so we had to get a bit creative. Their bane also went through a few versions. Originally, they had to take skins with the Nhang Flesh Form Devotion to prevent themselves from mutating, but I'm ultimately not a fan of having to harm your Humanity to fulfill your bane, and literally skinning people was just too much for a weakness. I also didn't want to make buying the Devotion a prerequisite to joining the bloodline at all, so we went with something that narratively suggests they're going to mutate no matter what, but mechanically that only affects them in certain circumstances.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'll let the Vetala do the rest of the talking. Tomorrow, let's have a look at the <b>Anvari</b>, the only First Edition bloodline not from <b>Ancient Bloodlines</b>, and the one I've literally been trying to figure out how to fit into a book for three years...<br /> <br /> <b>Vetala: The Ones Who Make You Shudder</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cPatience! Lurk in the dark, dank places. Nurse that hunger. Evolve.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <i>Drip, drip, drip goes the chemical drain. Toxic pools stink and burn and let off a gaseous odor that keeps even the rats away. NO TRESPASSING signs aboveground on the barbed wire gates seem almost comical by comparison. The corporation that keeps this place hidden from regulations and inquests turns a blind eye, pretending it doesn\u2019t exist. Suits you fine. It\u2019s home sweet home.</i><br /> <br /> <i>After the first decade down here, as your hair fell out to every last eyelash, as your teeth rotted and your lesions multiplied, you had moments of doubt. The silence was nice, but it left you starving for a morsel of fresh blood. No one comes around here except the rare inspector, and if too many of those go missing, you\u2019ll be attracting attention you don\u2019t want. But when your flesh sloughed off in ragged strips and you felt yourself becoming, you knew you had it made.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Then that tabloid reporter showed up about rumors of a mutant or a radioactive mongrel lurking in the slurry. You gave him a little glimpse. Just enough to piss his pants and write his story. Now the hunters come \u2014 not many, not enough to be dangerous, but enough to keep you fed. You play with them, stealing their forms and walking among them\u2026 for a while. It breaks up the monotony, right?</i><br /> <br /> <i>Say what you will about pollution; it\u2019s great for your neighborhood monster.</i><br /> <br /> The Nhang are the stuff of vampire nightmares, but that\u2019s because the Kindred forget to count the Vetala. Even the dead can evolve, and the Troglodytes are the glorious, grotesque proof of that, ever-shifting and ever mutable, sprouting whatever proto-organs their environments demand of them. \u201cHumanity\u201d is just another weakness to be expunged.<br /> <br /> The Strix think Kindred are abominations, walking corpses who pretend at being people that need the delusion excised by force. No such force is needed against the Troglodytes. Their very existence eats through Humanity like acid rain, eroding them into something inhuman at all times. Take on a human face and slow the distortion of the body \u2014 and hope your victim won\u2019t be missed. Perhaps because of this atrophy, the Vetala have an understanding with their Beasts. It boils against their flesh rather than lashing out, and an Extremophile\u2019s frenzy is not the messy rampaging of less-evolved Kindred, but a caustic boiling over. Watch in terror as their bodies swell and distort, jaws wrenching wide, many hands grasping: a nightmare risen from a watery grave. Just another cryptid to add to their urban mythology. The Nhang might be forgotten, but the Vetala are here to stay.<br /> <br /> The Troglodytes don\u2019t make a habit of hobnobbing with their Kindred. They surface only when they need something: a bylaw changed, a development project derailed, a fresh rumor to drive prey into their domain. But with their habit of wearing others\u2019 faces, you likely won\u2019t know you\u2019ve dealt with an Extremophile at all.<br /> <br /> The first substantiated sighting of a Vetala was during the industrial boom of the early 1900s, but it wasn\u2019t until the 50s with its ramp-up of space-age technologies that this bloodline really found its foothold. The Troglodytes have always been reclusive, but as industry expanded and the world shrank, these hideous Nhang were forced into ever more extreme conditions. Sulfuric hot springs, active volcanic craters, acid lakes \u2014 these are the places they make their lairs. They become customized to survive in the most inhospitable locations on Earth. And there, in places anathema to humanity, they wait for the Strix to show them the next step in evolution.<br /> <br /> The isolation means they remain largely unmolested, and perhaps this is how they\u2019ve managed to survive. However, it also means they\u2019re forced to venture out on forays to find their food, and their clan's ability to steal appearances becomes crucial. Behind these temporary masks, an Extremophile\u2019s true form is hideous and often plagued with spliced limbs, bulbous growths, and distorted features. They cannot pass as human, living or otherwise. But they can survive anything.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> You aren\u2019t human anymore, so stop pretending. Those old limits mean nothing to you now. Slip on human forms to lure them in, then discard their husks to tangle in the flotsam. With us, you need not sacrifice sunlight \u2014 just society.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> We\u2019ve got tricks you\u2019ve never even imagined needing to counter, and there\u2019s no one who can make us bend, no one who can challenge us for our domain. We\u2019re always hungry and we\u2019re <i>always </i>hunting \u2014 yes, even you. We drown the meat to steal its face, so you won\u2019t even know we\u2019re among you\u2026 until it\u2019s too late.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> Our flesh sloughs off, and we take a new face. We walk in it for a while until it flakes away, and we take another, and another\u2026 Each time, we\u2019re worn a little smoother, a little less. No matter, we\u2019ll take another! But soon, we see our reflection and don\u2019t know this boiled, cancerous, wriggling thing peering back, cold and lonely in the dark depths. All those myths about monsters reduced to their watery lairs, their ravenous hunger \u2014 they\u2019re all true.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan: </b>Nhang (<b>Night Horrors: Spilled Blood</b>, p. 94)<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Extremophiles, Troglodytes (derogatory)<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Contaminated Curse): </b>The Troglodyte Beast doesn\u2019t know when <i>not </i>to adapt, even when it\u2019s to nothing. As the Blood thickens and Humanity declines, a Vetala\u2019s body reacts by forcing a violent and disfiguring mutation: tumorous growths, new organs with dubious functions, etc. This degeneration is inevitable and worsens as the vampire ages, but sometimes the body overwhelms even itself. To keep this overgrowth in check, roll an Extremophile\u2019s Humanity penalized by Blood Potency when she rises for the night. On a success, nothing happens; on a failure, she gains the Maladaptation Condition. As long as this Condition lasts, her bane remains dormant.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b>Celerity, <i>Protean</i>, Resilience, Vigor<br /> <br /> <b>Maladaptation</b><br /> <br /> [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>In the Dark Eras (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Fear and the Golden Promise of Tomorrow \u2014 1938\u20131946 CE (DE2, p. 428): </b>The sudden surge in horror books, comics, and films makes \u201cthe monster\u201d a common feature of many science fiction works, and this fascinates the Troglodytes, who see in these creatures their own likeness, whether to be lampooned or made into tragic heroes \u2014 though never with a happy ending. As their faces fill movie posters around the world, some retreat back into the shadows, only for their evolutions to morph in new and extreme ways as they fight to adapt to the coming nuclear age. On the frozen ice floes of Severny Island and the dry wastes of New Mexico, a few Vetala get a dose of a very modern terror.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Gift: Adaptable Physiology</b><br /> <br /> Vicissitudinous flesh provides the Vetala greater protection against environmental factors. By default, the standard Nhang traits are no longer hindered by the purity of the water the vampire lives in. A Troglodyte\u2019s color-changing scales and underwater vision are unhampered by pollutants, alkalinity changes, chemicals, saltwater, etc. In an extreme environment [REDACTED]. However, this gift does not apply if the vampire is exposed to sunlight or the effect of her clan bane is in effect.<br /> <br /> <b>New Merit: Legend (\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisite: </b>Kindred, Fame \u2022<br /> <br /> <b>Effect: </b>Your character has acquired a local legend. This niche brings cryptid hunters and other looky-loos to her territory searching for proof of her existence, providing potential sources of food. Treat each dot of Fame as a level of Herd or Feeding Grounds, distributed as you see fit.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback: </b>Each bit of \u201cevidence\u201d your character allows into the hands of cryptid hunters risks the Masquerade. If she cares.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-29T12:45:58-07:00","id":1493988,"title":"","content":"my favorites right there,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-29T18:50:49-07:00","id":1494008,"title":"","content":"First off, thanks to <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian\">Yossarian</a></b> and <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast\">Demigod Beast</a></b> for their comments on my take of the Iltani, Yurema and other bits.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now back to bloodlines proper, must admit that is definitely not what i expected upon first seeing the name <span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">vetala </span></span></span>- but i really like them and can see some fascinating interpolation space with the Sta-Au's Spiritual Infestation Tilt and/or Wyrm Nests for some wicked, wicked permutations and dare say a Strix connection can be redudant or unnecessary in their case.<br /> <br /> Brackish, noxious swamps where individuals court death while seeking wisdom from strange fumes or guidance of will-o-wisps,.<br /> Marshes where animal &amp; human sacrifice for the sake of fortune in finding bog iron, verdigrised cooper and other ores to be forged amidst poison herbs, fat &amp; bones for fuel, quenched upon sulphurous waters hungry for its unclean morsels of slag and refuse.<br /> Deadly, ancient cenotes under the earth full of strange treasures and secrets of long forgotten people, living, dead or other.<br /> <br /> Yes, i can certainly see both Extremophile and walking corpses doing away with the middlebird in their path to spontaneous unholy awakening into ravening unlife.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-28-2023, 11:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-29T19:14:07-07:00","id":1494010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1494008#post1494008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Now back to bloodlines proper, must admit that is definitely not what i expected upon first seeing the name vetala</div> </div> </div> </div>That name went through fair bit of workshopping, funny enough. Originally, they were just the Troglodytes, but that felt a bit anodyne, and more like a nickname than a proper name. The second choice was <i>Vishap</i>, which is another kind of Armenian water dragon (similar to the Nhang), but I didn't want to be too geographically precise (the Nhang aren't just Armenian), and the bloodline's origin pointed more to India. Vetala are somewhat more generic vampire-like creatures, but a couple of interesting details really clicked. For one, vetala possess corpses, which fit with the skin-stealing aesthetic of both the clan and the bloodline, and for two, they live in charnel grounds, places where bodies are left to putrefy, which fit with their general nastiness and mutative qualities. The god Agni Vetal is also said to have controlled flame, which fit well with their alternate Extremophile nickname.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-29T21:07:24-07:00","id":1494016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1494010#post1494010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That name went through fair bit of workshopping, funny enough. Originally, they were just the Troglodytes, but that felt a bit anodyne, and more like a nickname than a proper name. The second choice was <i>Vishap</i>, which is another kind of Armenian water dragon (similar to the Nhang), but I didn't want to be too geographically precise (the Nhang aren't just Armenian), and the bloodline's origin pointed more to India. Vetala are somewhat more generic vampire-like creatures, but a couple of interesting details really clicked. For one, vetala possess corpses, which fit with the skin-stealing aesthetic of both the clan and the bloodline, and for two, they live in charnel grounds, places where bodies are left to putrefy, which fit with their general nastiness and mutative qualities. The god Agni Vetal is also said to have controlled flame, which fit well with their alternate Extremophile nickname.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can see what you're going for now.<br /> <br /> They take the kindred's ressonance with death, putrefation (or its absence), refuse of both the material &amp; spiritual sorts and take them a few steps further into a sort of stygian course of sorts, i guess. Or maybe that's just my head messing with those themes in another cultural framing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-30T10:07:00-07:00","id":1494044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1493987#post1493987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, today, let's talk about some new blood: the <b>Vetala</b>.<br /> <br /> All the new bloodlines went through a bit more development than the old ones; the major benefit of working from previous material is that a lot of the groundwork is already done for you, so making something <i>wholly </i>new is always a different beast, especially when we're talking about lost clans, who don't have the literal decades of background the standard-issue ones have. So, it took a bit more work to get these new bloodlines where we wanted in comparison with the &quot;Ancient&quot; bloodlines. The Vetala were no exception, mostly because the Nhang, while a really cool concept, are one of the weirder lost clans. &quot;Water vampire&quot; is definitely a trope, but it's just narrow enough that we had to work a bit harder to find a natural expansion of that concept.<br /> <br /> To that end, I think we ended up with something really cool and thematic with the Vetala. It's not a long walk from water vampire to swamp thing vampire, and the author had a really interesting idea in framing them as classic movie monsters. Unlike, say, the Nosferatu, where they represent your deepest personal fears and fundamental prejudices, the Troglodytes are the externalities of human hubris (like so many movie monsters), evolving with technology and pollution and culture. They're what happens when you dump toxic waste in the lake and it wakes up hungry for blood.<br /> <br /> Obviously, that steps a bit into Gangrel territory, but we thought of the Vetala as being a very modern phenomenon, whereas the Gangrel are more primordial and (in a sense) natural. That said, it's hard to escape the archetypes, and if you wanted to play them as a Savage bloodline, I don't think that would be a stretch. You could pretty easily map all the new bloodlines to the basic clans if the lost ones don't fit into your chronicle, which is partly why we did five; not <i>just </i>because there are five in <b>Spilled Blood</b>!<br /> <br /> The big dev changes were their mechanics. Making vampires hard to kill is a surprisingly delicate dance; you don't want things to just be unfair, but you don't want them to be only nominally tougher than regular vampires. Protean and Resilience also cover a lot of &quot;this isn't even my final form&quot; territory, so we had to get a bit creative. Their bane also went through a few versions. Originally, they had to take skins with the Nhang Flesh Form Devotion to prevent themselves from mutating, but I'm ultimately not a fan of having to harm your Humanity to fulfill your bane, and literally skinning people was just too much for a weakness. I also didn't want to make buying the Devotion a prerequisite to joining the bloodline at all, so we went with something that narratively suggests they're going to mutate no matter what, but mechanically that only affects them in certain circumstances.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'll let the Vetala do the rest of the talking. Tomorrow, let's have a look at the <b>Anvari</b>, the only First Edition bloodline not from <b>Ancient Bloodlines</b>, and the one I've literally been trying to figure out how to fit into a book for three years...<br /> <br /> <b>Vetala: The Ones Who Make You Shudder</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cPatience! Lurk in the dark, dank places. Nurse that hunger. Evolve.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <i>Drip, drip, drip goes the chemical drain. Toxic pools stink and burn and let off a gaseous odor that keeps even the rats away. NO TRESPASSING signs aboveground on the barbed wire gates seem almost comical by comparison. The corporation that keeps this place hidden from regulations and inquests turns a blind eye, pretending it doesn\u2019t exist. Suits you fine. It\u2019s home sweet home.</i><br /> <br /> <i>After the first decade down here, as your hair fell out to every last eyelash, as your teeth rotted and your lesions multiplied, you had moments of doubt. The silence was nice, but it left you starving for a morsel of fresh blood. No one comes around here except the rare inspector, and if too many of those go missing, you\u2019ll be attracting attention you don\u2019t want. But when your flesh sloughed off in ragged strips and you felt yourself becoming, you knew you had it made.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Then that tabloid reporter showed up about rumors of a mutant or a radioactive mongrel lurking in the slurry. You gave him a little glimpse. Just enough to piss his pants and write his story. Now the hunters come \u2014 not many, not enough to be dangerous, but enough to keep you fed. You play with them, stealing their forms and walking among them\u2026 for a while. It breaks up the monotony, right?</i><br /> <br /> <i>Say what you will about pollution; it\u2019s great for your neighborhood monster.</i><br /> <br /> The Nhang are the stuff of vampire nightmares, but that\u2019s because the Kindred forget to count the Vetala. Even the dead can evolve, and the Troglodytes are the glorious, grotesque proof of that, ever-shifting and ever mutable, sprouting whatever proto-organs their environments demand of them. \u201cHumanity\u201d is just another weakness to be expunged.<br /> <br /> The Strix think Kindred are abominations, walking corpses who pretend at being people that need the delusion excised by force. No such force is needed against the Troglodytes. Their very existence eats through Humanity like acid rain, eroding them into something inhuman at all times. Take on a human face and slow the distortion of the body \u2014 and hope your victim won\u2019t be missed. Perhaps because of this atrophy, the Vetala have an understanding with their Beasts. It boils against their flesh rather than lashing out, and an Extremophile\u2019s frenzy is not the messy rampaging of less-evolved Kindred, but a caustic boiling over. Watch in terror as their bodies swell and distort, jaws wrenching wide, many hands grasping: a nightmare risen from a watery grave. Just another cryptid to add to their urban mythology. The Nhang might be forgotten, but the Vetala are here to stay.<br /> <br /> The Troglodytes don\u2019t make a habit of hobnobbing with their Kindred. They surface only when they need something: a bylaw changed, a development project derailed, a fresh rumor to drive prey into their domain. But with their habit of wearing others\u2019 faces, you likely won\u2019t know you\u2019ve dealt with an Extremophile at all.<br /> <br /> The first substantiated sighting of a Vetala was during the industrial boom of the early 1900s, but it wasn\u2019t until the 50s with its ramp-up of space-age technologies that this bloodline really found its foothold. The Troglodytes have always been reclusive, but as industry expanded and the world shrank, these hideous Nhang were forced into ever more extreme conditions. Sulfuric hot springs, active volcanic craters, acid lakes \u2014 these are the places they make their lairs. They become customized to survive in the most inhospitable locations on Earth. And there, in places anathema to humanity, they wait for the Strix to show them the next step in evolution.<br /> <br /> The isolation means they remain largely unmolested, and perhaps this is how they\u2019ve managed to survive. However, it also means they\u2019re forced to venture out on forays to find their food, and their clan's ability to steal appearances becomes crucial. Behind these temporary masks, an Extremophile\u2019s true form is hideous and often plagued with spliced limbs, bulbous growths, and distorted features. They cannot pass as human, living or otherwise. But they can survive anything.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> You aren\u2019t human anymore, so stop pretending. Those old limits mean nothing to you now. Slip on human forms to lure them in, then discard their husks to tangle in the flotsam. With us, you need not sacrifice sunlight \u2014 just society.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> We\u2019ve got tricks you\u2019ve never even imagined needing to counter, and there\u2019s no one who can make us bend, no one who can challenge us for our domain. We\u2019re always hungry and we\u2019re <i>always </i>hunting \u2014 yes, even you. We drown the meat to steal its face, so you won\u2019t even know we\u2019re among you\u2026 until it\u2019s too late.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> Our flesh sloughs off, and we take a new face. We walk in it for a while until it flakes away, and we take another, and another\u2026 Each time, we\u2019re worn a little smoother, a little less. No matter, we\u2019ll take another! But soon, we see our reflection and don\u2019t know this boiled, cancerous, wriggling thing peering back, cold and lonely in the dark depths. All those myths about monsters reduced to their watery lairs, their ravenous hunger \u2014 they\u2019re all true.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan: </b>Nhang (<b>Night Horrors: Spilled Blood</b>, p. 94)<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Extremophiles, Troglodytes (derogatory)<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Contaminated Curse): </b>The Troglodyte Beast doesn\u2019t know when <i>not </i>to adapt, even when it\u2019s to nothing. As the Blood thickens and Humanity declines, a Vetala\u2019s body reacts by forcing a violent and disfiguring mutation: tumorous growths, new organs with dubious functions, etc. This degeneration is inevitable and worsens as the vampire ages, but sometimes the body overwhelms even itself. To keep this overgrowth in check, roll an Extremophile\u2019s Humanity penalized by Blood Potency when she rises for the night. On a success, nothing happens; on a failure, she gains the Maladaptation Condition. As long as this Condition lasts, her bane remains dormant.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b>Celerity, <i>Protean</i>, Resilience, Vigor<br /> <br /> <b>Maladaptation</b><br /> <br /> [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>In the Dark Eras (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Fear and the Golden Promise of Tomorrow \u2014 1938\u20131946 CE (DE2, p. 428): </b>The sudden surge in horror books, comics, and films makes \u201cthe monster\u201d a common feature of many science fiction works, and this fascinates the Troglodytes, who see in these creatures their own likeness, whether to be lampooned or made into tragic heroes \u2014 though never with a happy ending. As their faces fill movie posters around the world, some retreat back into the shadows, only for their evolutions to morph in new and extreme ways as they fight to adapt to the coming nuclear age. On the frozen ice floes of Severny Island and the dry wastes of New Mexico, a few Vetala get a dose of a very modern terror.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Gift: Adaptable Physiology</b><br /> <br /> Vicissitudinous flesh provides the Vetala greater protection against environmental factors. By default, the standard Nhang traits are no longer hindered by the purity of the water the vampire lives in. A Troglodyte\u2019s color-changing scales and underwater vision are unhampered by pollutants, alkalinity changes, chemicals, saltwater, etc. In an extreme environment [REDACTED]. However, this gift does not apply if the vampire is exposed to sunlight or the effect of her clan bane is in effect.<br /> <br /> <b>New Merit: Legend (\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisite: </b>Kindred, Fame \u2022<br /> <br /> <b>Effect: </b>Your character has acquired a local legend. This niche brings cryptid hunters and other looky-loos to her territory searching for proof of her existence, providing potential sources of food. Treat each dot of Fame as a level of Herd or Feeding Grounds, distributed as you see fit.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback: </b>Each bit of \u201cevidence\u201d your character allows into the hands of cryptid hunters risks the Masquerade. If she cares.</div> </div> </div> </div>What\u2019s that Tzimisce-like dead-or-dying clan from Eastern Europe? I can never remember how to spell (or even pronounce!) their name. These guys could be one of <i>their</i> bloodlines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-30T11:10:16-07:00","id":1494047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1494044#post1494044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What\u2019s that Tzimisce-like dead-or-dying clan from Eastern Europe? I can never remember how to spell (or even pronounce!) their name. These guys could be one of <i>their</i> bloodlines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pijavica, I believe. Which is interesting, because we were very close to including a bloodline each for them and the Akhud, but we wanted to save them for... something else.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-30T12:57:47-07:00","id":1494050,"title":"","content":"So, the <b>Anvari</b>. Here's how the sausage gets made.<br /> <br /> It's not an exaggeration to say that we've been circling the drain on this bloodline for quite some time. I briefly considered them for <b>Bloodlines: The Resurrected</b>, but I didn't really have a hook for them, so they just ended up in the quick conversion appendix. I <i>also </i>considered them for <b>Bloodlines: The Devoted</b>, but there were a few too many Daeva bloodlines in that book already. Then, they were absolutely, positively going to be in <b>Bloodlines: The Ageless</b>... which, obviously, they are, but that was back when <b>BTA </b>was going to be, like, an omnibus of all the remaining bloodlines, including those from the 1E clan books <i>and </i><b>Ancient Bloodlines</b>. My original outline for this book was kind of a beast, and it quickly became evident that it was Too Much. I also had some authors drop off for scheduling reasons, so that original, chunky version evolved into the 2E clan books; keen observers may note that <b>Bloodlines: The Devoted </b>had a &quot;coming next&quot; teaser for <b>Ageless</b> in the early version, which I sheepishly removed eventually. If I recall correctly, someone wrote a few bits and bobs for the Anvari in that proto-version of the book, but I didn't ever see the drafts. I believe it was something about them having toxic blood, which, in hindsight, I don't think would've really fit.<br /> <br /> Anyway, when the first version of <b>Ageless </b>collapsed into the clan books, the Anvari were absolutely, positively, <i>definitely </i>going to be in <b>Sin Again: Daeva</b>. And then, I finally took a good long look at their original write-up and kinda got turned off, lol. I didn't find them as icky as the Children of Judas, but I found the idea of opium-addict vampires deeply inessential. I also felt we had enough old bloodlines in the book, and I wanted at least a couple of new ones. So, they got the chop.<br /> <br /> However, when we decided to take another crack at <b>Ageless</b>, I gave them one last chance. I still didn't particularly like them, but I also really wanted to have full translations of all the 1E bloodlines with unique Disciplines, and they were the only ones we hadn't in some form or another. But, I was really stuck on their concept, which was so monofocused on opium, and I didn't know how to make opium powers interesting or pointful. That got me talking to one of the other authors, because I was getting close to just writing them off completely. Fortunately, that conversation led to a much more interesting take on them, one that fits with the original concept but expands it beyond the very narrow niche it was stuck in.<br /> <br /> In Second Edition, the Anvari are addicted to addiction, not just opioid-tainted blood. Sex addicts, gamblers, alcoholics, Vitae fiends \u2014 all these and more can fulfill an Anvari's appetites, though, in the case of that last one, they can't get high on their own supply. So to speak. The Pushers use their special Kiss effect to temporarily relieve addiction, forcing human junkies to rely on them to get their fixes. They're like walking, talking, omni-methadone, and by purveying vices, they ensure a steady food source. They also, rather infamously, use this ability to &quot;help&quot; ghouls and blood addicts escape Kindred (read: their rivals), weaning them off blood addiction. Of course, they can <i>also </i>help you out if you're jonesing for diablerie, so the rest of the dead haven't <i>quite </i>got around to dealing with them. Yet.<br /> <br /> All that said, this is probably one of the nastier bloodlines we've done. They spread human misery and then lap it up for good measure. I think there are some really interesting stories you can tell with them, but they're not something everyone's going to want to bring to the table. Of course, I could also see someone playing them very altruistically (speaking of the Salubri), serving as harm-reduction specialists.<br /> <br /> So, here are the Anvari, with a brand new drug. Tomorrow, let's end the week with a Nosferatu bloodline: the <b>Adroanzi</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Anvari: The Ones You Crave</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cI can take the pain away. Just takes a little pinch...\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Addiction is everywhere. From opioids blighting the streets to the smartphone in your pocket, the monkeys clinging to our backs bear many masks \u2014 vampires among them. The Blood is more addictive than heroin, and the dead are habit-forming in their own awful right. The Daeva call that quality \u201cMajesty,\u201d but it\u2019s not a stretch to say all Kindred possess a certain allure that\u2019s difficult to resist. Some more than others.<br /> <br /> The Anvari have product to move, and that product is themselves. Any Lick can make a junkie, but the Lotus-Eaters supply a more specialized service. Rather than creating legions of Vitae fiends and blood dolls, they can fulfill any habit with nothing but a nip, and in the nights of the Persian Empire, the Anvari Kiss was a thing of legend, a panacea for all addictions physical and mental.<br /> <br /> Traditionally, they cultivated poppies (<i>hal gil</i>, the joy flower) or any other substance they could use to lure customers \u2014 but no one\u2019s got time for that these nights. Drugs have too much overhead, whether financial or legal. But you know what the pigs don\u2019t give a shit about? Gambling. Porn. Social media. Hell, booze is way worse for you than smack, and the government will sell it to you in ABC stores. Some Pushers run wineries for the rich and permanently soused, while others are sex workers with <i>very </i>loyal clientele, and others still deal habit-forming cure-alls for whatever makes you tick.<br /> <br /> They\u2019ve smoked hash with the Assassins and supplied the Romantics with laudanum; they\u2019ve cultivated harems for emperors and run casinos on behalf of riverboat barons \u2014 and they\u2019ve ruined them all. Anvari require the disgraced, destitute, and doomed to feed their addiction to addiction. People who are comfortable in their habits tend not to see a vampire\u2019s bite as an appealing alternative, so a Pusher makes sure her customers reach rock bottom before she takes her first drink, replacing addiction with an altogether more constructive habit in a perfect closed loop of parasitism. Any Serpent can make you want her, but an Anvari makes you need her.<br /> <br /> For the All Night Society, the Anvari are simultaneously a necessary evil and a source of conflict. A Lotus-Eater\u2019s bite can relieve the addiction of even the most strung-out ghoul or blood groupie, and while it can\u2019t break the Vinculum, it goes a long way toward clearing heads. Of course, in the same way, Pushers can also provide therapy for Kindred Vitae addicts, providing a rehab program that\u2019s exactly as sinister (and effective) as it sounds. A few princes employ Lotus-Eaters as personal physicians, whether to treat their cravings or to punish those who fall to wanton cannibalism. Some mistake their gifts for altruism, but that\u2019s a dangerous mistake. It\u2019s not like methadone wants to drink your blood.<br /> <br /> One would think relieving their subjects of the very thing that sustains their bloodline would be self-defeating, and one would also be incorrect. Sure, maybe an Anvari can untangle your brain from its psychological or chemical dependencies, but addiction isn\u2019t about the hit. It\u2019s <i>never </i>about the hit. It\u2019s about whatever circumstances brought you to a goddamn vampire\u2019s doorstep for help. She can\u2019t fix your life for you (not unless she wants to), and nine times out of ten, you\u2019ll be back again within a week. Month, tops.<br /> <br /> Then, the Anvari will really have you hooked.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> I mean, look at us. We make bank like Scarface and get to live forever. You don\u2019t get into the life because you want to be a dealer: You want to be a kingpin.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> Everyone has something they can\u2019t live without, something that gets them through the night or pushes them over the line in the dull day-to-day. If you think you don\u2019t have one, well, we already know what it is, and don\u2019t think for a <i>second </i>we can\u2019t take it away.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> I mean, look at us. All vampires are junkies in some fashion, and if we aren\u2019t on the cutting edge of that particular flaw, we don\u2019t know what is. All highs dull in the end. The satisfaction pops like a soap bubble on your tongue, and that\u2019s when the Beast decides it needs a bigger taste. Ain\u2019t no rehab for that.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Origins (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> Once upon a midnight darkly, a lost little girl in gingham came upon a wonderful field of poppies. Because she was pure of heart, she marveled at the rich crimson of their petals, the scent so sweet she couldn\u2019t help but breathe in every bloom. However, these were no ordinary flowers, but the prized poppies of a wicked witch, and those who sniffed their pollen would fall to endless sleep. Yet the girl had great courage too, and she fought the lure of slumber as she soldiered on through the field. At the edge of the clearing, the witch awaited, and the sorceress offered to open a golden road back home if the child would only give up her heart and courage. However, the little girl had brains above all, and she blew a flowerful of pollen in the hag\u2019s face, then ran down the golden road to Kansas. They say the witch lies among the poppies still, dreaming dead dreams of the things she can never have \u2014 addictively ever after.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan:</b> Daeva<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Lotus-Eaters, Pushers<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Curse of Hal Gil): </b>Doesn\u2019t matter what you\u2019re hooked on \u2014 coke, sex, the red stuff \u2014 the Anvari have a jones for your dependence. If a Pusher fails to feed from a character with the Addicted Condition at least once every (Humanity) nights, [REDACTED]. A Lotus-Eater can\u2019t get high on her own supply: Vitae addicts she creates with her blood do not count, nor do any created by other members of her bloodline.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b>Celerity, <i>Dominate</i>, <i>Majesty</i>, Vigor<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Gift: Nepenthe</b><br /> <br /> Named for the potion Helen of Troy imbibed to relieve the suffering of her captivity, <i>Nepenthe </i>is the ability Anvari use to keep their herds coming back for more.<br /> When a Pusher uses the Kiss on a character with the Addicted/Deprived Condition, the vampire can spend a Vitae to fulfill whatever her subject\u2019s craving may be, whether for Vitae, alcohol, opioids, or even behavioral addictions like gambling and sex. However, she must know what the addiction is first.<br /> <br /> The only habit that offers some resistance is the Amaranth. To repress a diablerist\u2019s addiction, [REDACTED].<br /> <br /> If a Pusher uses this effect on a vampire, she does not need to resist blood addiction or the Vinculum if she takes only one Vitae and immediately spends it on Nepenthe. However, this does fulfill the constraints of her bloodline bane.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 10-01-2022, 02:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-30T13:00:03-07:00","id":1494051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1494044#post1494044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What\u2019s that Tzimisce-like dead-or-dying clan from Eastern Europe? I can never remember how to spell (or even pronounce!) their name. These guys could be one of <i>their</i> bloodlines.</div> </div> </div> </div> Just like Tzimisce, Pijavica require a pronunciation aid. It's PEE-YA-VEE-TSA. In multiple languages it means &quot;leech&quot; (the animal) which in turn is derived from &quot;to drink&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-30T13:12:01-07:00","id":1494052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1494051#post1494051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Just like Tzimisce, Pijavica require a pronunciation aid. It's PEE-YA-VEE-TSA. In multiple languages it means &amp;quot;leech&amp;quot; (the animal) which in turn is derived from &amp;quot;to drink&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always pronounce it the (roughly) accurate way, and people look at me like I\u2019ve had a stroke. I dated a Serbian girl in university, so I roughly know how to sorta kinda read South Slavic words, oddly enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 09-30-2022, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-30T13:20:29-07:00","id":1494054,"title":"","content":"The curse of knowledge. My condolences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-30T15:54:29-07:00","id":1494061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1494047#post1494047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pijavica, I believe. Which is interesting, because we were very close to including a bloodline each for them and the Akhud, but we wanted to save them for... something else.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Damn, and now i can't unsee the possibility of a Pijavica-Nhang connection, on their own or through the Vetala - information mismatch, twice-cursed or something else altogether, who knows?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-01T13:35:32-07:00","id":1494109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1494061#post1494061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Damn, and now i can't unsee the possibility of a Pijavica-Nhang connection, on their own or through the Vetala - information mismatch, twice-cursed or something else altogether, who knows?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be an interesting combo. Animalism, Celerity, Resilience and probably Vigor, since they have a fair bit of overlap power-wise. That would be a pretty nasty pair of banes, too.<br /> <br /> Now, let's take a stroll and sniff roses with the <b>Adroanzi</b>.<br /> <br /> So, I had a longer post planned, but I foolishly was writing it in the forum text box and then accidentally used the same window to Google something, losing everything a wrote. I'm kind of crunched for time right now, so I can't rewrite all of it, sadly.<br /> <br /> The long and short is that we really liked this bloodline in the original book, but felt their Discipline wasn't worth preserving. So, we gave them Animalism instead and added some Merits so it could apply to plants. In addition to a special Mandragora Merit, that necessitated reprinting Of Rose and Thorn from <b>Wild Hunt</b>; I felt it was better to provide readers with easy access to that Merit, especially if they didn't have access to the Gangrel book. We also made their superiority complex weakness a bit more concrete, rather than dealing double damage.<br /> <br /> One other small detail worth noting is that, while we wanted to keep their cultural heritage, we also wanted to hint that there may be other such Nosferatu in a bit of convergent evolution (very much like certain plants), which ties into what we were talking about above with respect to bloodlines showing up in various different times and places through history. To that end, one of their origins is very much not African.<br /> <br /> Anyway, enjoy the excerpt! Sorry for the short post, but feel free to ask questions. Also, the name of the Merit excerpt below is different in the book due to a research SNAFU that I thought I'd fixed; I suspect it was another case of me mixing up files (there are a lot of moving parts to these things). So, that will be fixed in errata.<br /> <br /> I'll be back Monday with lots to say about the <b>Kinnaree</b>. Bring your dancing shoes.<br /> <br /> <b>Adroanzi: The Ones Who Answer Your Prayers</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Miracles aren't free.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> There are many gods in Africa. From well-known fixtures of mythology such as Anansi the Spider to all but forgotten deities who watch over single villages or lonely crossroads. The spiritual ecology of the continent and its peoples is rich and vibrant\u2026 but not all gods are good. Some prayers whispered in the night are not made in the hopes of health and fortune, but rather for old and hungry things to pass the supplicant by and feast upon their neighbors instead. Some prayers are made not in awe and wonder, but in bitterness and rage, blood spilled upon black earth while wishing death and ruin upon those who <i>deserve </i>to suffer. For prayers like that, many things in the dark still listen \u2014 and answer. But when they do, you may regret ever asking at all.<br /> <br /> The Adroanzi are an old bloodline in an ancient land, but one that has lost much of its power over the centuries. Once, these Nosferatu ruled openly over living tribes, their divine lineage granting them domain over the plants and beasts the people needed to survive. They tended their vast human herds as Gardeners tending to a grove: planting new seeds, pruning problem growths, and harvesting a price in blood for their \u201cbenevolent\u201d guidance. Times change, however. Colonization eroded, and then finally collapsed, the Adroanzi\u2019s powerbase, just as invasive Christianity dismantled their herd\u2019s faith and fear in their old gods.<br /> <br /> Modern Adroanzi are much diminished from the heights of their power, but they can\u2019t forget they were once as gods to their mortal thralls, and their bitterness over having their rightful role stolen away drives them to recreate it. Indeed, the bloodline\u2019s stubborn clinging to their faded glory has earned them the unfortunate moniker \u201cPretenders\u201d in modern nights. Unlike most Haunts, many Gardeners surround themselves with cults of mortal followers, enforcing loyalty with Vitae, fear, and brute force. They become urban legends in the domains they lair in, lurking within old shrines and cursed groves, answering prayers in exchange for blood and other favors.<br /> <br /> The Adroanzi are far from divine, however, and the miracles they grant to those foolish enough to seek them are harsh and terrifying in equal measure. A young man desiring success in business witnesses his competitors and their customers swarmed by hissing, biting snakes, leading to dozens of hospitalizations and an entire building condemned due to infestation. A jilted lover wanting retribution on the woman who spurned her is horrified to discover her drained corpse hanging from the washing lines the next evening. A father wishing for a more obedient son finds his child now terrified of him, convinced \u201cthe pale-eyed man\u201d will take him away for horrible punishments if he so much as looks his parent in the eye.<br /> <br /> Despite their methods, there are always desperate people willing to accept the help of monsters if it gets them what they think they want. However, these interactions strain the Masquerade, which is why Adroanzi usually operate on the fringes of domains, far from the prying eyes of Kindred courts. One might wonder, then, why any prince would suffer this arrogant and troublesome bloodline to operate anywhere near their domain, and the answer lies in why the Adroanzi are called \u201cGardeners.\u201d<br /> <br /> The bloodline has a unique affinity for producing a rare substance known as lacrima. This ocher sap is a delicacy among the Kindred, one of the only substances besides blood they can consume for pleasure. It can only be harvested from the vines of mandragora, twisted, Vitae-fed plants that crave blood like other flora crave light. Mandragora, also called \u201cmandrakes,\u201d are difficult to grow and cultivate, with most attempts ending in piles of fetid rot. Not so for the Gardeners. Where other Kindred might struggle to create a single viable mandrake, a lone Adroanzi can make an entire garden flourish with relative ease.<br /> <br /> The lacrima produced from such gardens fetch a high price, and holding the keys to the supply is what buys the bloodline tolerance for their more problematic behavior. Some Gardeners devote themselves wholly to the creation of lacrima, preferring to withdraw from a world that no longer recognizes their divine heritage. Hidden away in vine-choked havens, they emerge only to feed or sell their little black bottles.<br /> <br /> However, for most Adroanzi, lacrima is simply a means to an end. The sap gets them money and favors, which they use to cultivate worshippers for their (no doubt inevitable!) rise back to their proper place as divine rulers. One garden feeding another.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> Let the other Haunts crawl in the sewers, too cowed to raise their heads. We walk unseen because others aren\u2019t worthy to look upon us. We have the blood of gods within us, and our gardens drip with ruby ambrosia. To be one of us is to know your place in this world, and it\u2019s upon a throne of thorns and blood.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> We command the fears of men, we command the beasts of the land, we command the very grass beneath your feet and branches over your head. We are the descendants of divinity, and if you cross us, your body shall serve as fertilizer in our gardens.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> The worst fate for a god is to be forgotten, and it\u2019s been a long time since we were truly known. We scavenge fearful prayers like jackals and drip lacrima in the eyes of our detractors so they don\u2019t see how deep our sins run. It\u2019s a poor Gardener who needs his plants more than they need him.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan: </b>Nosferatu<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Gardeners, Pretenders<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Sanctimonious Curse): </b>The Adroanzi are either no longer gods or never were, but something deep in their blood still compels them to assert their assumed divine superiority over their victims. Pretenders all suffer a variation of the Blood of the Unwilling bane (<b>Vampire</b>, p. 108). However, instead of consent, the vessel must pay respect to the vampire without direct supernatural coercion, whether recognizing her as a deity or at least some form of superior. The Sanctimonious Curse does not apply to Kindred until Blood Potency 6, but it always applies to ghouls.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Animalism, <i>Nightmare</i>, Obfuscate, Vigor<br /> <br /> <b>In the Dark Eras (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Princes of the Conquered Land \u2014 1501\u20131568 CE (DEC, p. 116): </b>As the Gr\u00e9mio dos Corajosos (p. 45) spreads its influence across the world, the bizarre Tenth Choir covenant (Dark Eras 2, p. 352) sends a coterie to travel through Central Africa to sabotage the Christian and Sanctified missionary work spreading across the continent. There, they find unexpected but eager allies in the Adroanzi, especially those who wish to make inroads into Mutapan territory to the south. While only a small number of Gardeners formally join the covenant, they take on the mission of destroying God with a zeal only those who felt personally wronged by Him could. The Gardeners turn the land itself against the missionaries, planting hungry mandragora in newly founded church grounds and summoning hordes of savage wildlife to torment priests and converts alike. It\u2019s rumored that one Adroanzi even learns to wield Therion, and when she finally awakens from torpor, she intends to spread its power to the rest of her bloodline\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>New Merit: Mandrake Cultivation (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Adroanzi, Gardening Specialty in Crafts<br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> The creation of mandragora is what the Adroanzi are primarily known for in modern nights, and their affinity for these thirsty plants is astounding in the eyes of anyone who knows how difficult their creation usually is, at least if they survive the encounter. With this Merit, an Adroanzi can grow quite a little garden.<br /> <br /> <b>Red Fertilizer (\u2022): </b>Something in the Gardener\u2019s Vitae causes mandrakes to flourish unnaturally. All Vitae requirements for mandragora creation and maintenance are halved (rounding up) so long as the plants are fed only Adroanzi Vitae.<br /> <br /> <b>Strange Growth (\u2022\u2022):</b> [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>Sweet Sap (\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>Thorn Whispers (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): </b>[REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>Blood-Soaked Grove (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): </b>[REDACTED]<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-02T07:06:09-07:00","id":1494135,"title":"","content":"The Adroanzi sound wonderful and their Mandrake Merit is interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-03T12:25:39-07:00","id":1494248,"title":"","content":"Welcome back! Let\u2019s talk about the <s>Kinarree</s> <s>Kinnarree</s> <b>Kinnaree</b>.<br /> <br /> This was another bloodline that had a strong hook in the original that mostly needed a bit of finessing to fit in 2E. In general, that involved giving their dancing/fighting abilities more heft mechanically. In the original, they had a couple of Cr\u00faac rites and a Devotion. The rituals weren't much to write home about, and the Devotion is more or less just basic Auspex in 2E, so we focused on giving them movement-based powers. We <i>considered </i>updating the Muay Thai Merit in the sidebar on p. 119 of <b>Ancient Bloodlines</b>, but we felt it was pretty thoroughly covered by various Fighting Style Merits in <b>CofD </b>and <b>Hurt Locker</b>. We also wanted to give a bit more systems for them to actually hunt &quot;demons&quot; (i.e., ephemeral beings).<br /> <br /> The other big change was their bane. I actually find that their old weakness (i.e., riding the wave is a Vice) ties well into the First Edition Daeva weakness, though it occurs to me now that it may have inadvertently let you ride the wave without spending Willpower if you played your cards right. I might be missing something in that analysis, as it's been a while since I really engaged with the First Ed. system. I digress. We still liked the <i>idea </i>of frenzy as addictive, and I think the author did a great job of expressing that mechanically.<br /> <br /> This bloodline had some refocusing in development. Mostly, I asked the author for a better sense that they were karma assassins rather than just warriors; they have some overlap with the Amara Havana, who are also fighty Daeva with a Hindu mythos, and I wanted to make sure there was a stronger distinction between the two. I'll talk about that overlap a bit when I get to the Amara Havana, as it's a developmental problem I found quite thorny (and one I don't think I <i>quite </i>solved to my satisfaction, but that's a conversation for another day). I really like this bloodline, though. The origin section in particular is a highlight.<br /> <br /> The art for this one was also a lot of fun to do. I think the skull looks pretty metal, if nothing else. That said, convincing myself that I could elegantly fit that character within the text in layout was pure hubris on my part, but I <i>feel </i>like it was worth it for the strikingness of her pose.<br /> <br /> Alright, time to fill your dance card. Tomorrow, I'll be back with another new bloodline: the <b>Kanaim</b> of Clan Bekaak.<br /> <br /> <b>Kinnaree: The Ones Who End You</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Mind if I cut in?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Everything ends. This is not only true, but <i>necessary</i>. Without endings, there can be no beginnings, and this cycle is vital for the Wheel of Creation to keep turning and balance the world. Most things meet their end naturally and are sent back to the Wheel to be made ready for their next life according to their karma, as intended. Some things, however, need a little help.<br /> <br /> Kindred are static by nature. Beyond immortality, their forms are restored to the moment of death each night, their blood forcing the body to reset itself. Left to their own devices, vampires will stagnate for centuries, and the schemes they spin catch and hold everything around them in a never-changing web of influence and blood. Or, they would, but the Kinnaree are here to cut the threads.<br /> <br /> Claiming to be the descendants of asura, the demons of Hindu mythology, Kinnaree believe they have a sacred duty to bring an end to beings who are due one. Most commonly, these are ancient vampires who\u2019ve grown bloated with power, but the Dancers also target more exotic creatures such as lingering spirits, patchwork immortal men, and human sorcerers determined to cheat death. \u201cKinnaree\u201d is a name taken from the half-bird women of the Himmapan forest; they were said to have protected and succored Shurpanakha, the line\u2019s founder, after she received Durga\u2019s blessing.<br /> <br /> Obviously, the Kinnaree\u2019s practices make them rather unpopular among elders, who\u2019ve called several blood hunts upon the bloodline in a variety of Thai domains throughout history. Among their many detractors, Kinnaree are called Kin-Slayers, and most princes will not suffer them to operate in their courts, which means they\u2019re rarely open about their lineage. They\u2019re not so easily rooted out, however. The Dancers are a truly ancient bloodline, one that\u2019s woven itself deeply into Thai culture, including the ritual dances so important to national holidays. The bloodline draws many of its childer from traditional performers, as they believe a master dancer physically experiences the history of the people of the land.<br /> <br /> Despite the heavy opposition they face, the Dancers aren\u2019t without supporters. Many traditional festivals and superstitions involve humans aiding asura, a role that the Kinnaree enjoy taking on in order to manipulate kine into serving them. What\u2019s more, many young Kindred \u2014 particularly among the Carthian Movement \u2014 celebrate the Dancer\u2019s mission as justified and necessary, all too eager to have the Kin-Slayers topple a local tyrant so they can race to fill the ensuing power vacuum.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the most terrifying aspect of the Kinnaree, if you\u2019re a potential target, is their beautiful, violent dances. A sensuous sweep of the leg enthralls the watcher so they never see the dagger descend. Steps so graceful the audience weeps tears of blood even after their hearts stop beating. Victims begging not for their lives, but to be allowed to see the dance to its completion before they die. Based on Thai ritual dances (or perhaps the Thai people modeled their dances after the Kinnaree), to watch a Dancer perform is a sight that stirs even the oldest hearts. To witness such a sight and live is a gift rarely bestowed.<br /> <br /> Despite their grisly work, Dancers are far from being grim executioners, or even righteous crusaders. Rather, the Kinnaree are as affable and charming as the rest of their Daeva cousins, which allows them to walk within domains largely undetected for what they are. They take joy in their work \u2014 not from the killing, but from the new beginnings they enable by removing that which is static and unchanging. When possible, the Kin-Slayers offer their targets a quick and painless end, with assurances that they shall have a better next life for having accepted the end of their current one.<br /> <br /> They are inevitably disappointed that so few take them up on their compassionate offers.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> Of course you want to dance with us! Each step keeps the Wheel turning and preserves this wonderful world. You\u2019ve seen what happens to our kind when we exist too long and forget what it was to live. Help free your kin from that existence, knowing that they\u2019ll accept your help with gratitude \u2014 in the next life.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> The last thing you see before your end is beauty. Accept that gift and die with dignity, or deny it and meet your maker in terror and agony. Your choice.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> Ours is an ancient dance taught by holy demons, and we\u2019ve been dancing a very, very long time. Does that make us as old and unchanging as the things we hunt? One night, <i>we </i>must end, as all things must, but then who will do our holy work? These questions fester in our blood, but we dare not speak them aloud. Easier to dance on\u2026 as we always have.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Origins</b><ul><li>In times of myth, when demons still walked among men, Shurpanakha was a demon created by the All-Mother to slay others of her kind. She was also a young girl, and the paradox of her existence as both an innocent and a weapon caused her great pain and loneliness. One night, after more asura died from her actions, she called out in grief to Lady Durga, scourging herself fiercely as she begged for answers. Moved by the girl\u2019s suffering, the goddess answered her, explaining for the first time the girl\u2019s purpose and gifts. Shurpanakha was necessary; she needed to serve as an ending to creatures who required one in order to foster new beginnings. In her mercy, however, Durga decreed that Shurpanakha would no longer need to bear her burden alone. From the half-god, half-demon blood that the girl had shed, Durga created beautiful, joyful children for her, ones that would never age so their mother would never grow lonely again. The Kinnaree claim Shurpanakha still watches over her children, and when one of them requires an ending, it is she who appears to deliver it with all the warmth and tenderness of a mother\u2019s love.</li> <li>The Kinnaree are liars. They don\u2019t kill their targets; they sell them. Chaiyo Palathai was an old diablerist who managed to kick the addiction just in time to stop herself from becoming a draugr, but by the time she mastered herself, her thirst had already cost her all her worldly wealth and connections \u2014 her skills at hunting Kindred were all she had left. Having learned many strange abilities from the souls she devoured, Palathai searched for others like she had been, and offered them a deal. She would capture and deliver Kindred to them to feed their black hunger in return for money and influence. She became a dealer to a very select set of addicts, but not just them: mortal sorcerers, powerful in-the-know, corporate interests\u2026 There are many different parties who would pay a fortune for giftwrapped elder Kindred. As Palathai sired childer to keep up with an ever-expanding client-list (addiction is such a dependable business model) she invented her bloodline\u2019s mythology as a smokescreen. Kin-Slayers actually go after tyrants and monsters because no one really misses those sorts of vampires when they\u2019re gone. Much younger than they claim, the Kinnaree have been in business for only a couple centuries now, outlasting the disappearance of their founder and continuing to sell torpid Kindred to the highest bidder.</li> <li>The Kinnaree are one of the Owl\u2019s greatest triumphs. Durga ignored Shurpanakha\u2019s prayers in the woods that night, as gods often do, but the Strix heard her. They came drifting out on the branches to watch this wailing, powerful thing, and in her, they saw an opportunity. Slipping into the corpses of women buried in the soft earth, they came to Shurpanakha\u2019s side. They comforted her with words of smoke and held her in dead arms. They whispered to her a new purpose, that she was to kill monsters, old and terrible things that cause suffering wherever they go, ancient and powerful monsters stubbornly resistant to the Owls\u2019 meddling. They showed Shurpanakha how to spread her blood so she wouldn\u2019t be alone anymore, and ensured she taught her children as well. How the Strix laugh now, to watch the Dancers so dedicated to carrying out their will, removing the greatest threats to their schemes without so much as a nudge from the Birds. Indeed, by shadowy agreement, no Strix who knows of the grand joke will ever claim a Kinnaree. They don\u2019t want to risk a Kin-Slayer being seen with yellow eyes and spoiling their lovely game.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Parent Clan: </b>Daeva<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Dancers, Kin-Slayers<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Avenging Curse): </b>While the Kinnaree do their best to harness their monstrous nature toward a righteous cause, they\u2019re still begotten of demons, and sometimes their instinct to revel in destruction can\u2019t be controlled. When resisting frenzy triggered by violence, a Kin-Slayer\u2019s resistance pool is limited by Humanity. This cap does not apply to riding the wave. Once a Kinnaree has met the goal of the frenzy, her player must roll Resolve + Composure again with the same cap. Success ends the frenzy, but failure results in her attacking a new target. If there are no obvious targets, the Kinnaree will stalk the night for another, and the vampire will continue to hunt until the roll succeeds or the daysleep takes her.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> <i>Auspex</i>, Celerity, <i>Majesty</i>, Vigor<br /> <br /> <b>In the Dark Eras (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> <b>The Year Without a Summer \u2014 1816 CE (DEC, p. 204):</b> The eruption of Mount Tambura brings more than poor crops. As cholera spread by migrants infects Southeast Asia, a strange bloodline of Mekhet follows the disease\u2019s trail to Thailand. These Jvarasura \u2014 known as the Morbus in the West \u2014 have developed their own apocalyptic (and heretical) Hindu sect, believing they can hasten the return of Vishnu by exacerbating the current age of Kali Yuga. The Kinnaree are dutybound to destroy these vile Shadows, but between the ravages of cholera and the kine\u2019s endless wars with Vietnam, the Kin-Slayers find themselves on their back foot for once. However distasteful it may be, some Dancers wonder if the Maiyarap could be of help in balancing the Wheel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-04T06:29:17-07:00","id":1494307,"title":"","content":"The 3 possible backstories are interestin and the Bane fits them well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-04T15:15:26-07:00","id":1494352,"title":"","content":"Hello again! Let's discuss the <b>Kanai\u200bm</b>.<br /> <br /> The Kanaim are a bloodline of the Bekaak clan, a lineage of Sanctified age-vampires who may or may not have held a similar social position to the Julii and Ventrue in pre-contact North America. Due to a curse from some... manner... of entity, their bodies seem to decay over time, and eventually, their minds <i>actually </i>do. Their clan curse (as opposed to their &quot;fucked around and found out&quot; curse) is that they find it difficult to lie to high-Integrity mortals. The Kanaim are doubly screwed in that regard, in that they have a bit of a Cassandra problem: their prophecies aren't believable. Worst of all, most of those fortunes have to do with their subjects' impending dooms.<br /> <br /> Conceptually, the first draft for this bloodline wasn't too different from what we ended up with, but they didn't really have a goal or a default to fall back on. In development, we gave them an apocalyptic bent/heresy, in that they believe the &quot;proper&quot; apocalypse of Revelation has been averted by a manmade one, and that it's their duty to get things back on track, or else the Kindred are more damned than even Longinus said. We also did a lot of workshopping on the name; originally, it explicitly referenced Cassandra, and I felt that was both too on the nose and not really fitting for a Lancea et Sanctum-associated bloodline.<br /> <br /> Their powers also went through some retooling. Prophetic powers are always kind of a pain, so we ended up repurposing what amounts to Dream Visions, but linking it intrinsically to the bloodline's bane.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'll give the Kanaim the pulpit. Tomorrow, let's look at our other Gangrel bloodline: <b>Les Gens Libres</b>!<br /> <br /> <b>Kanaim: The Ones Who Undeceive You</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;The end is here.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <i>Armageddon is not a prophecy.</i><br /> <br /> <i>It\u2019s a fact, my children, one that you can touch if you don\u2019t believe the truth before your eyes. The boiling seas, the rise of tyrants, the worship of false idols: they\u2019re all here.</i><br /> <i>But this is not the lifting of the veil that was foretold. This is not holy revelation. No, my children, there are no trumpets or beasts from the sea or horsemen a-riding. Merely the rot of sin.</i><br /> <br /> <i>And if that\u2019s true \u2014 and we all know it to be, my children \u2014 then the covenant is broken, and the Lord has abandoned the world of men. Therefore, we are a doubly damned race, for if there is no redemption for humanity, no grace for the elect in the Kingdom of Heaven, then the Kindred are even more wretched than the Dark Father told us.</i><br /> <br /> <i>But do not despair! Do not let the Devil win because he tells you he already has! There is yet work to be done, my children, and the Lord has blessed you with one final chance. No, they won\u2019t listen to you \u2014 that\u2019s the cross we must bear for righteousness, but oh how sweet the victory shall be when we open their eyes. You\u2019ll force them to see, my children, and in this, you shall not be silent.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Then, on that glorious night, when God\u2019s green earth is in its right place\u2026 He can end things the right way.</i><br /> <br /> When the Bekaak fell from grace, cursed to age yet never die, the Kanaim fell further.<br /> <br /> Derided as Babblers by their kin, this bloodline believes it\u2019s been tasked with averting the apocalypse. Not just averting: reverting. Humanity has pushed the world past the tipping point, and as punishment, God has vacated His throne, the Second Coming canceled because, no, in fact, not one was righteous. For centuries, the Diviners spent their Requiems guiding the kine and Kindred alike through other apocalypses \u2014 from the Thirty Years\u2019 War to the Spanish flu \u2014 but this one is different: They foresee no end. Without the cleansing wrath of God, the current, sinful age will only fester, and when all is said and done, none will escape its Hellish maw.<br /> <br /> The problem is, nobody fucking believes them. Not in the sense that they\u2019re dismissed, but because nobody <i>can </i>believe them. Like her kin, a Kanai must speak truth to the worthy, but she\u2019s also cursed to never be heeded. Some say the bloodline\u2019s progenitor earned this punishment for speaking truth to power, or that the first of their lineage lied to the Devil Himself and has yet to make reparations. Some just say they\u2019re nuts.<br /> <br /> To say this maddeningly contradictory curse has left the Kanaim eccentric would be an understatement, even among a lineage of eccentrics. Like other Bekaak, the Diviners can stay the withering hand of time, but they frequently don\u2019t. Those who choose this bloodline aren\u2019t seduced by the glamor or romance of vampirism, but by a deep and unshakable desire to redeem humanity. They see themselves as shepherds of the meek, as lighthouses against the coming storm and as warders of doom. To remain pure and do the Lord\u2019s work, they allow their clan\u2019s strange withering to run its course as long as possible, desiccating their bodies but keeping their souls free from depravity. They wear their mortal masks for decades or even lifetimes, growing old with their adherents, ensuring the Masquerade tightly cloaks them against sinful suspicions.<br /> <br /> Yet it would be sanctimonious to claim all Kanaim are selfless warriors of truth. While they may not be believed, their prophecies have a nasty habit of coming true, and some Prophets join this bloodline simply because they want access to the universe\u2019s secrets, even if they think the whole Armageddon thing is a tad overblown.<br /> <br /> Tonight, the Diviners settle into niches. The nature of their bane means their circles must remain small, from schismatic church boards to heretical Bible study groups, as they need a constant supply of blood bonds in order to have anyone to share their visions with and effect change, always looking for new ways to draw in those they deem worthy; they\u2019re (literally) purveyors of hidden knowledge, and that can be attractive to the unwise. Judgment, then, often comes from their fellow Kindred. If they are decrepit in body, most would posit, they must also be decrepit in mind. Indeed, the most fanatical Kanaim freely invite bouts of senility in exchange for keeping the Devil at bay. They may not have the visages of angels, but they hold themselves above the degradation of their brethren. <br /> <br /> Yet for all their talk of piety, there\u2019s something insidious about the sacred truth the Kanaim have lashed themselves to. One cannot gaze into coming destruction without being changed by it\u2026 But the Babblers believe it\u2019s revocable. Judge not by appearances, for God has sent His messengers. You will have to make a choice: Let the truth be told, or be damned.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> You want to be prepared for what\u2019s coming. We stand highest and lowest among God\u2019s holy monsters, able to live and feel and <i>know </i>beyond the capacity of any mortal or Lick. We have been blessed by the undiluted Word of God with a glorious responsibility. We speak with His mouth, we act with His hands, and all who ignore our warnings do so at their own peril.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> Truth is incorruptible. We cannot be bought off or swayed or silenced. In the end, our proclamations always come true, and if you deny us, you will have wrought your own doom. We alone can save you \u2014 from damnation, from Final Death\u2026 from yourself. Be bound to us. Submit to God. Yes, you shall be beholden\u2026 but hey, at least you\u2019ll be in on the secret.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> We see it coming. We\u2019ve howled ourselves raw with warnings. Yes, we once scoffed at those who ignored our doomsaying; if they didn\u2019t heed us, to Hell with them. But now? Even our siblings call us fools, too wrapped up in our self-righteousness. Maybe they\u2019re right. What\u2019s the use of surviving the terrors to come if we lose all we love in the process? We see it coming, yes, and we broke ourselves trying to stop it. We watch the world burn, alone, knowing the final, horrible truth: <i>We </i>are the damned.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan: </b>Bekaak (<b>Night Horrors: Spilled Blood</b>, p. 86)<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames:</b> Diviners, Children of Kanatase (historical), Kanai (singular), Babblers (derogatory)<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Unheeded Curse): </b>While all Bekaak must speak truth to the worthy, the Kanaim are doubly damned. When a Kanai experiences her bloodline gift (p. 108), any attempt to communicate her prophecy directly requires a [REDACTED]. This bane applies to Kindred, but does not apply to other Kanaim, Touchstones, or characters with a third-stage blood bond to her.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b>Animalism, <i>Auspex</i>, Obfuscate, <i>Vitiate</i><br /> <br /> <b>In the Dark Eras</b><br /> <br /> <b>Lifting the Veil \u2014 (DEC, p. 252): </b>With the founding of the Society for Psychical Research, the Diviners are finally heeded. For the first time since crying their truths to deaf ears, their audiences are eager to experiment. They have ghouls beyond count, Embrace new childer, and even Princes sit at their s\u00e9ance tables. It seems they might finally be able to reach the masses with their prophecies. Unfortunately, more is prowling in the ether than just spirits. Only the fool believes he can hold the reins of the universe, but for this brief, open-minded period, the Kanaim certainly try.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Gift: The Awful Word of God</b><br /> <br /> The Lord talks, and the Kanaim listen. No one else does, but they\u2019re working on that.<br /> <br /> Once a chapter, the Storyteller can reveal a prophecy to a Diviner in a moment of great stress, import, or danger. Her player can also take a Beat to invoke this effect at any point in the chapter if it hasn\u2019t gone off. The vampire experiences a vision of the future, typically an impending misfortune or doom relating to another character present in the scene, gaining [REDACTED]. Her player can then ask a question about the vision as long as it fits within a yes/no/maybe answer.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T11:16:51-07:00","id":1494427,"title":"","content":"Alright, let's take a look at <b>Les Gens Libres</b>.<br /> <br /> This was a tricky one.<br /> <br /> To start, I wasn't that familiar with the original version. I had some assumptions about what they were based on their name, but I didn't know anything <i>beyond </i>those assumptions, and the fact that they were Gangrel who didn't have Protean. As I've mentioned above, I wasn't originally the writer on most of the bloodlines I ultimately ended up doing, and I was in for an unpleasant surprise when I finally sat down to update them.<br /> <br /> For those of you aren't familiar with the old version, they were anarchistic Gangrel who emerged from the Haitian revolution...except that's a lie. They were <i>actually </i>feeding stock for colonial elders who had their clan Discipline bred out of them so they're more docile and easy to trap. They're the descendants of slaves whose true purpose is to be fed upon by high-Blood Potency vampires because they can't create blood bonds. There's even an artifact that you can use to track them for that purpose.<br /> <br /> So! Our version of Les Gens Libres has a murkier background; there's still a connection to Haiti (a very different one!), but there's also one to witches' sabbats in medieval Europe...and one to Aulus Julius Senex in Rome. Members of our version are still Gangrel, but the bloodline has partly removed the normal restriction on clan, and can induct other Kindred into their movement. They discard many of the trappings of lineage, including their signature Disciplines, to exist in a truly egalitarian All Night Society. First, however, they'll need to fight for it. Les Gens Libres are too radical for most Carthian Movements, and it's written in their very blood that all authority is illegitimate.<br /> <br /> Apart from reworking the background, the big change was opening them up to all clans. Because we already had the Sta-Au, and because we already jacked the Mystikoi for <b>Wild Hunt</b>, I wanted to keep them as default Gangrel. As such, I made the barrier of entry for other clans <i>slightly </i>higher (ironic given my complaints a few pages ago, I know, but I contain multitudes). That said, if you want to lift that restriction and make them truly open to all clans, that definitely won't hurt anything.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'll let the write-up do the rest of the talking. Tomorrow, let's have a look at the <b>Bak-Ra</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Les Gens Libres: The Ones Who Set You Free</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cFreedom has a price, friend, and you\u2019re about to pay it.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Burn it all down. Traditions, princes, covenants \u2014 toss them in the flame and paint a new world with the ashes. Even the sire\u2013childe bond is just another imposition of power, an artifice as hollow as a vampire\u2019s soul. All the structures and customs and moves of the Danse Macabre are designed for one thing: keeping you down and all the other fuckers up, and Les Gens Libres aren\u2019t going to take it anymore. No, it won\u2019t be easy. True freedom means dispensing with things like mercy for those who have none, and even for \u201cbystanders\u201d content to sit back and accept the status quo. No one is innocent, and these Libertaires are ready to show you how deep the rot really goes. With a flamethrower.<br /> <br /> Les Gens Libres are anarchists in the purest sense. No power is legitimate according to their philosophy, and even groups like the Carthians are too authoritarian for their sensibilities. Community is the only structure worth preserving in the All Night Society, and anything that places one Lick above another is just asking for a good toppling, to the point that they shun the Vinculum as the ultimate taboo, a precept that\u2019s enforced by the curse of their blood. Hierarchy is anti-freedom, and anti-freedom is fascism, so anyone who would perpetuate it is worthy of death until proven otherwise.<br /> <br /> The cause isn\u2019t limited to vampires, either. Les Gens Libres see no distinction between Kindred and kine artifices of power, and while they\u2019re careful not to antagonize mortal governments, they have plans. <i>Permanent revolution </i>is the name of the game, a quasi-millenarian belief that they have the right and obligation to change the world. They\u2019re not ready to discard the Masquerade just yet, but human oppressors are the next target once they\u2019re done with the Kindred, and they don\u2019t care if that makes them pariahs and criminals. Though some exist on the margins of the Cacophony, content to carve out their communes as long as the dead keep their corruptions out, many are guerrillas, freedom fighters, and even terrorists. \u201cBy any means\u201d is both theory and praxis, and more than a few Licks have learned that the hard way.<br /> <br /> Near the top of the Libertaires\u2019 shitlist, the worst of the All Night Society\u2019s oppressions, are clans. Clans are a line in the sand based on a load of bigotry dressed up as supernatural pageantry. Vampires aren\u2019t Daeva or Gangrel or Mekhet or Nosferatu or Ventrue: They\u2019re <i>Kindred</i>. Even the so-called \u201cgifts\u201d of the blood perpetuate more inequality. Dominate, Majesty, Nightmare \u2014 these are just different names for the jackboot. Thus, the first thing a new Libertaire does is dispose of her clan; with the new blood coursing through her veins, she becomes part of a universal fraternity, one where each member of the whole is as worthy as the next.<br /> <br /> If murdering anyone who sniffs in the direction of hierarchies in order to achieve an egalitarian utopia sounds like a paradox, well, you\u2019ll probably be next against the wall. Force in the hands of the oppressed against the powerful is acceptable as long as it doesn\u2019t become institutional, and the Clanless are still figuring out just where that line might lie. In the meantime, they\u2019ve developed a reputation that rivals Belial\u2019s Brood for violence, and some Kindred whisper they\u2019re one and the same as the Worthless. In truth, the Libertaires consider the Brood a perversion of their cause, all the more as they carefully study their tactics. Waste not, want not, after all.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, Les Gens Libres are a marginal presence in the All Night Society, a problem that surfaces every once and a while to be crushed all over again. Where they keep coming from is another question altogether, as is why they always return in greater and greater numbers\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> You want justice. You want to live in this midnight world as a true equal. You want to take your despair at the nature of death and forge it into a sword to wield against those who would claim to be your betters. You want to destroy them all.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> We\u2019ll die for our cause, and we\u2019ll take every last one of you with us. It\u2019s a simple calculation: Give us what we want or die. <i>Now </i>you want to talk it out? I\u2019d sooner cut out your fascist tongue and feed it to my dog to shit out. Negotiations are over; now comes the pyre.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> You\u2019ll pave the road to Hell with every one of your good intentions. A time will come when you\u2019re not strong enough, when convenience trumps purity, and that\u2019s when you\u2019ll learn the cost of bearing these ideals is very steep indeed.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Origins</b><ul><li>Most origin stories place the Libertaires as clawing their way out of the crucible of the Haitian Revolution. As the people of Saint-Domingue overthrew their European oppressors, the island\u2019s All Night Society experienced a similar tumult. At the vanguard of this conflict was a group of Gangrel who had been freed from bondage before their Embraces, and it\u2019s said they fought well into the daylight hours to win their liberty once more. Eventually, these revolutionaries and their followers managed to take most of Port-au-Prince for their own, purging colonists both living and dead. Their movement rejected authority of all kinds, making a pact to never suffer tyranny as long as Vitae flowed through their veins. Soon, members of all Kindred lineages made the same promise, calling themselves <i>les sans-clans</i>. Few of the original Libertaires survive tonight, having either fallen to the fangs of their enemies or factional infighting, but their legacy sparked a fire in the Danse Macabre that might never burn out.</li> <li>As the Inquisition made its way through Europe, a sabbat of witches came together to hold a great rite. They were, one and all, the children of those shunned and abused by society, or those who had escaped the flames with nothing but char left for flesh. They beseeched the old gods of the land \u2014 themselves discarded for the Christ and his saints \u2014 to make them strong against their abusers, to answer for the oceans of blood they had lost. Reaching through the rage and sorrow in their hearts, the gods answered back, but in their diminished state, they required great sacrifice. And so, each witch cut her own throat and drank from her sisters, their many deaths feeding the gods to make manifest their dreams of revenge. When they woke the next night, they were sisters in both blood and deed, blessed and cursed to walk the world to lay low the powerful.</li> <li>When Julius Senex conquered the night, he brought forth the dead of Rome to legitimize his twilight republic, asking each of the Kindred <i>gens </i>to swear an oath to his rule. Each paterfamilias pledged their loyalty \u2014 all but one, a freedwoman of the blood clan I must not name. She made the manu fica at the dread lord and declared she would not be ruled by any nation of corpses, nor any nation at all. She called on the gathered Propinqui to rise and become truly free, but the groveling masses feared Senex more than they loved liberty. They jeered the freedwoman and she cursed them in turn, saying they were no Kindred of hers. The Old Man laughed and laughed, for never before had one dared defy him so, and as reward and punishment, he used the awful powers of his blood to decree her free, burning away all bonds that held her to the Propinqui but denying her the ability to form any of her own. It is said she laughed right along with Senex, promising she would return to thank him for his gift.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Parent Clan: </b>Gangrel, but non-Savages can join if they have Blood Potency one level higher than the usual relevant prerequisite. At Blood Potency 5, a member of the bloodline rather than a member of the inductee\u2019s clan can act as Avus.<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames:</b> Libertaires, the Clanless, the Free People (in the local language)<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Curse of Liberty):</b> Freedom isn\u2019t passive. It\u2019s a quality one must uphold actively, and Libertaires who would enslave others aren\u2019t worthy of the name. In addition to her \u201cformer\u201d clan\u2019s curse, whenever a Clanless vampire deliberately inflicts a blood bond on a sapient character (i.e., not an animal), she [REDACTED].<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b>Animalism, Celerity, Obfuscate, Resilience<br /> <br /> <b>In the Dark Eras (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> <b>The Master\u2019s Tools \u2014 1917 CE (DEC, p. 290): </b>Despite the eventual victory of Marxism (and, ultimately, Stalinism), anarchists have a significant impact on the Russian Revolution, and many of the ones who end up dead are chosen for the Libertaire cause. <i>Svobodnye Lyudi </i>aren\u2019t numerous in Russia, but they\u2019re adept at using the revolution and subsequent civil war as cover to strike at Kindred who they deem insufficiently supportive of the mortal cause. Many of these targets are Yagnatia (<b>Better Feared: Nosferatu</b>, p. 60), a family of Haunts who ruled a midnight fiefdom for the same space of time as the tsars. Even tonight, these Boyars still remember the Clanless, and it\u2019s a matter of personal honor for them to eliminate any Libertaire cells they happen across.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Gift: Fraternit\u00e9</b><br /> <br /> Les Gens Libres don\u2019t belong to clans, at least as far as properties of the Blood are concerned. As such, Taste of Blood rolls cannot identify a Libertaire\u2019s parent clan.<br /> Furthermore, having no clan is a little like belonging to all of them. Les Gens Libres can ignore clan prerequisites when purchasing Merits, but doing so costs an additional dot if the Merit comes from a lineage that isn\u2019t her original clan. For example, if a Gangrel Libertaire wants to purchase Kiss of the Succubus, her player treats it as a two-dot Merit. As such, Libertaires cannot purchase five-dot clan Merits this way.<br /> <br /> This gift does not obviate a character\u2019s clan curse, whether it was active before she joined or not, and this is one of the few ways one might guess a Libertaire\u2019s \u201ctrue\u201d nature.<br /> <br /> <b>New Merit: Vaulderie (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Les Gens Libres Status \u2022\u2022, Occult \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> <b>Effect: </b>Hierarchies are a nonstarter for the Clanless, but the bloodline does require some form of organization, or else anarchism quickly becomes anarchy. This odd ritual, rumored to have been passed down from the original Haitian Clanless when they swore their oath, makes a coterie more than a gang of Licks: It turns them into comrades.<br /> To perform the Vaulderie, the pack passes around a receptacle containing a point of Vitae from each member of the coterie, and your character spends a Willpower. This does not add to Vitae pools or inflict blood bonds, but it does cause Vitae addiction as usual. Once complete, for weeks equal to the highest Blood Potency in the group, participants gain the following benefits:<ul><li>Each character gains access to one dot of another packmate\u2019s highest Discipline (or second highest, and so forth, if they have equal levels level); the players choose which characters to draw dots from.</li> <li>The participating vampires treat the pack as a collective Touchstone. These Touchstones do not attach at a specific Humanity level, but characters count as having multiple Touchstones if they have attached ones already.</li> <li>Blood sympathy is [REDACTED].</li> <li>All Vincula the participants are bound to are [REDACTED].</li> </ul><br /> <b>Drawback: </b>Betraying the Vaulderie is a Humanity 1 breaking point, even involuntarily, and the detachment roll gains no bonus from Touchstones of any kind.<br /> <br /> <b>Story Seed: Synchronicities</b><br /> <br /> During the Terror, Les Gens Libres set their knives and fangs on the ruling class with such abandon that Kindred accused them of Devil worship, a claim that follows them to this night. However, the Libertaires took it as a badge of honor, referring to their main communal practice as <i>la vaulderie </i>after the apocryphal rites of medieval witches.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s peculiar though \u2014 perhaps suspicious \u2014 that the Therion bloodline (<b>Bloodlines: The Devoted</b>, p. 56), a group of gnostic Satanists who claim members from all clans and who might have ties to Belial\u2019s Brood, also practice a ritual called the vaulderie, with a rather similar effect.<br /> <br /> Wait \u2014 <i>Therion</i>? Isn\u2019t that the magic of the Tenth Choir, yet another faction active during the Terror, whose goal was nothing less than murdering God on His throne?<br /> <br /> Funny, that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-06T14:00:42-07:00","id":1494463,"title":"","content":"Good afternoon! Let\u2019s have a look at the <b>Bak-Ra</b>.<br /> <br /> This was always a cool bloodline. Mekhet who claim to have been sunwalkers is just the right level of audacity; it\u2019s a concept you can do a lot with in ways that are both typical and atypical of the Mekhet.<br /> <br /> The big changes were largely mechanical. Their bane, in particular, is completely different; the old version had them paying an extra Vitae per night to wake, which is not that interesting, nor particularly meaningful at higher Blood Potency levels. We felt it was more thematic if they had to \u201ccommune\u201d with their god, Ra. That is, the sun. In first drafts, this required them to take damage, but I felt that wasn\u2019t necessary. Now, they just need to view it live, taking whatever measures they desire to prevent too much, uh, rapture. Rather than making life hard for Bak-Ra players, we wanted their bane to be more about the ways you avoid it rather than being &quot;die, lol&quot;. It's also something you can shirk <i>if </i>you don't mind your supernatural powers being a little duller, though at low Humanity, that's very dull indeed.<br /> <br /> The other mechanical shift was their Discipline spread. Normally, we avoid shifting out more than one power, but Resilience and Vigor fit very well for their Devotions, and they\u2019re an oddly un-sneaky manifestation of Shadow blood (are the Bak-Ra are so overt they\u2019re covert?), so we didn\u2019t feel they lost much without Obfuscate. We also wanted just a smaaaaaall hint that <i>maybe </i>their sunwalking claims aren't complete BS; see the Merit below.<br /> <br /> You\u2019ll notice that their powerset forms something of a parallel with the Usiri, who also possess a pretty atypical spread (three signature Disciplines), and I\u2019ll let everyone draw their own conclusions on that, given our discussions about the\u2026 mutability of the Blood over the course of history.<br /> <br /> The other change was giving them a bit more to do. The original version focuses rather narrowly on their obsession with uncovering their history, and while that\u2019s still there, we felt it was limited on its own. So, now the Bak-Ra are (for lack of a better term) try-hards. They need to prove to their god that they\u2019re worthy of walking in his light again, so they do\u2026 good\u2026 in the All Night Society. Each time they do\u2026 good\u2026 they hope they make up for whatever sin they may (or may not) have committed. Good doesn\u2019t just have to be morally correct things; maybe a Bak-Ra becomes the master of a sport or the greatest scholar in the city \u2014 above all, they strive to shine. That ties into their Shadow Cult a bit, too.<br /> <br /> On a side note, the third Bloodline Origin for this one is probably my favourite in the book, and is a perfect example of how you get <i>weird </i>in <b>Vampire </b>in a thematic way.<br /> <br /> The art on this one was (I believe) the first I did. It's a little more (overtly) cheese-cakey than we'd normally go for, but I wanted the &quot;sun-bathing vampire&quot; image to be as explicit as possible. I also wanted a wee reference to one of the original illustrations.<br /> <br /> So, don your sunglasses and take in the Bak-Ra in all their glory. Tomorrow, let\u2019s check out another new bloodline: the <b>Nehebkau</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Bak-Ra: The Ones Who Shine for You</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cThe only deluded one is you. Trust the proof before your eyes and see the light.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> The Bak-Ra must stalk the night beside lesser kin, but they know they belong to the light. Once, these Children of the Sun were leaders among the Great Covenant of the Kindred of Egypt. In this power structure, each clan and bloodline had a distinct role and was associated with one of the many gods of this land. The Bak-Ra (\u201cServants of Ra\u201d) are Shadows who had the responsibility of guiding all Kindred of Kemet according to Ra\u2019s will.<br /> <br /> But those times are long gone. The elder Bak-Ra of tonight must learn how to play the All Night Society not from a position of leadership, but as senile ancients, delusional and out-of-touch. Those unable to adapt prove their enemies right. They build Shadow Cults to Ra and other ancient divinities; they may dazzle mortal cultists with ancient secrets, but trap themselves as much as the kine. Ignorant mortals won\u2019t return them to the glories of the past, when they reigned from the top of the Kindred pile, so their neonates and ghouls are vital links to the current age.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s bizarre enough that any group of vampires would have ever been associated with a sun god, but that even doesn\u2019t scratch the surface of the bloodline\u2019s outrageous claims: According to them, they were once able to walk the daylit world without blistering their skin, without burning to ash \u2014 able to enjoy the sun\u2019s rays like mortals. However, if this ever was the case, it\u2019s no longer true. A Bak-Ra burns away in the light like any Shadow. What changed? They don\u2019t know for sure, but they blame a curse. Most Children of the Sun only recently awoke from millennia of torpor, but they remember how hateful Roman vampires drove them underground and left them no choice but to escape into history. The Romans envied the Great Covenant and the blessings its members received from the gods, and so they destroyed it in the name of their One God.<br /> <br /> Through the ages, only a handful of Sun-Stroked have awoken early from what the bloodline refers to as the \u201cLong Night,\u201d the period the world had to endure without Ra\u2019s chosen, as well as the void of seemingly endless torpor these chosen suffered (the irony that vampires bemoan an endless night is largely lost on the Bak-Ra). The most common theory is that the Roman vampires cursed the bloodline with their vicious rites out of spite. However, the suspicious blame their fellow Kindred of Kemet instead, and even those who don\u2019t blame their compatriots find their lack of support suspicious. Where are the Usiri with their wisdom? Where are the Khaibit with their blades? Not only are the Bak-Ra left without allies after centuries of guidance, the others outright deny their claims. Indeed, only their own histories back their version of events, and this only bolsters the ridicule they receive from modern Damned \u2014 not even their former pawns play along with their \u201cdaydreams.\u201d This ridicule strengthens the Bak-Ra\u2019s resolve to prove their detractors wrong \u2014 and perhaps even rebuild the Great Covenant while they\u2019re at it. Forcefully, if necessary.<br /> <br /> To this end, the Servants of Ra take up an odd niche in the All Night Society: doing good. As one might expect, the definition of \u201cgood\u201d is\u2026 different for an ancient blood cult in comparison with modern morality, but it\u2019s an ethos all the same. The Sun-Blessed have no illusions about the dead things they are, but they believe they must, in some way, prove themselves to their god so he might deem them worthy once again. Perhaps this is through personal achievement, becoming the master of a craft or the fairest in the land, or maybe it\u2019s just community service, like, say, throwing some reprobate Lick into an oubliette with no roof. This redemption-through-good-works philosophy wins even fewer friends among the Kindred than their sun-walking claims, and it\u2019s earned them a deserved reputation for sanctimony and overachievement.<br /> <br /> Most Bak-Ra fit into two groups: The ancients who were long dead before Rome fell, and recently Embraced neonates created to help their sires make sense of the modern world. Those who rose early from the Long Night and their childer are a small but important minority, and currently, they\u2019re the Bak-Ra with the most potent blood and connections in the All Night Society. Nonetheless, both factions, ultimately, have the same two objectives: Break the curse and return to a position of leadership in the All Night Society.<br /> <br /> They\u2019ll not be denied, no matter how many have to meet the sun.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> We are diminished, true. Any Servant of Ra must bear a great burden. However, think of the future that awaits us! We will regain ancient glories and take our rightful place above all Kindred. Ra himself will once again welcome us with his warm embrace while the others suffer in eternal darkness. Accept this struggle now and reap eternal reward.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> We refuse to be confined to the night. We <i>know </i>our memories are true; so many wise Kindred could not err. It\u2019s a long way still, but eventually, we will rule both Day and Night again, and when that time comes, we will remember those who paid us respect \u2014 and those who did not. We will introduce them to our god.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> What did we do to deserve such a curse? And what terrible things will we do to get rid of it? We could be wrong. What sins will we commit in pursuit of a lie? Some truths are too terrible to accept. Perhaps it would be better to burn everything down than find out\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Origins (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> The Sun-Stroked aren\u2019t vampires as this world knows them. These poor wretches come from a parallel universe in which, among other things, the rules of vampirism are reversed: They\u2019re welcome to the sun, but darkness swallows them, body and soul. What they now remember as the Long Night was actually their minds being catapulted through spacetime. <i>Of course </i>their memories are jumbled. That\u2019s only natural after such a traumatic event, but the real mind-bender is that their Blood (incompletely) adjusted to the Curse of our world. They speak the truth, but they and other Kindred simply aren\u2019t talking about the same thing. They should be returned to their world as soon as possible, before the tear in spacetime causes a catastrophic collapse of reality.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan: </b>Mekhet<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>The Sun-Blessed, Servants of Ra, Children of the Sun, the Sun-Stroked (derogatory)<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Sun-Kissed Curse): </b>Even as they\u2019re cast into darkness by the \u201ctrue Curse,\u201d the Servants of Ra can\u2019t escape the draw of the sunlit world, though none of them would ever refer to this as a <i>bane</i>. A Bak-Ra must witness the sun in person (not remotely) every (11 \u2013 Blood Potency) days. If she fails to do so, [REDACTED].<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b><i>Auspex</i>, <i>Majesty</i>, Resilience, Vigor<br /> <br /> <b>In the Dark Eras (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> <b>One Thousand and One Nightmares \u2014 832 CE (DE2, p. 124):</b> Perhaps the strange dreams and nightmares that come over the kine during this era are what shake the first Bak-Ra out of the Long Night. This is the first time a significant number of Sun-Blessed rise, and they find a world very unlike the one they left behind. Shunned by the other bloodlines of Kemet and the \u201cMohammedan\u201d covenants, these few struggle for every scrap. Their only advantage is the connections these elders have with the other ancient supernatural creatures of their land. Despite the animosity they face from their former peers and servants, the hope of recreating the Great Covenant does not die, and many Bak-Ra commit themselves to creating a united front against the Kindred of the One God. In the end, it will be the lack of sway among the mortals of this age that will doom their ambitions \u2014 a lesson the survivors learn well.<br /> <br /> <b>New Merit: </b><b>Enduring Ra\u2019s Kiss (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Bak-Ra, Resilience \u2022<br /> <br /> <b>Effect: </b>Despite their reputation as charlatans and fools, some Bak-Ra really can suffer the sun better than other Kindred. This Merit lifts some of the limitations of Resilience against sunlight (<b>Vampire</b>, p. 141). Your character can spend Vitae to reduce damage from sunlight like any other damage from a bane, as per the second active effect of Resilience. However, she still cannot passively downgrade aggravated damage from sunlight.<br /> <br /> Some Dragons react to this ability with dry amusement and a knowing smile. Whether this effect is also available to Ascendant Dragons or could be replicated with a Scale is up to the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-06T20:20:10-07:00","id":1494490,"title":"","content":"That one bloodline origin is hilariously intriguing. Let\u2019s call it the Contagion of the Sun or something <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-06T20:40:29-07:00","id":1494491,"title":"","content":"Just bought pdf todaay<br /> <br /> <br /> geheim one i looked at most<br /> <br /> blut alchemie would work well enough as a sorcery<br /> <br /> <br /> am pleassed that it breaks a trend last few years of alchemical effects being temporary","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-06T22:10:05-07:00","id":1494495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1494490#post1494490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That one bloodline origin is hilariously intriguing. Let\u2019s call it the Contagion of the Sun or something <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds like a vacation package. Maybe the Bak-Ra got screwed on a timeshare and things just snowballed from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-06T23:34:43-07:00","id":1494498,"title":"","content":"I was curious about the Maiyarap, I saw that their non-favored Treasures were limited by their bloodline status, so is bloodline status a thing similar to clan status so you'd need like five dots of maiyarap status or was that a more informal &quot;if people in the bloodline like them enough to teach them&quot; kind of status.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T00:11:23-07:00","id":1494502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1494490#post1494490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That one bloodline origin is hilariously intriguing. Let\u2019s call it the Contagion of the Sun or something <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You could certainly make a full Chronicle of this and similar &quot;transpositions&quot; messing up your Chronicles of Darkness. What would bizarro uratha or Lost be like?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T01:17:25-07:00","id":1494505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1494502#post1494502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could certainly make a full Chronicle of this and similar &amp;quot;transpositions&amp;quot; messing up your Chronicles of Darkness. What would bizarro uratha or Lost be like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves who are wolves changing into human(oid)s. They desperately scour the world in search of their sapient lupine kin, raging after reaching the false conclusion that they have been driven to extinction\u2026<br /> <br /> Fairies whose powers are not based on promises, but lies. Cold iron still hurts them, because it\u2019s cold hard truth. Their \u2018pledges\u2019 and \u2018Contracts\u2019 are befuddling to any Fae on this side of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T01:32:38-07:00","id":1494506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1494498#post1494498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was curious about the Maiyarap, I saw that their non-favored Treasures were limited by their bloodline status, so is bloodline status a thing similar to clan status so you'd need like five dots of maiyarap status or was that a more informal &quot;if people in the bloodline like them enough to teach them&quot; kind of status.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd need dots in a &quot;Bloodline Status&quot; Merit, yeah. That's not a form of Kindred Status explicitly defined in the core, but we've used it to key into a few things for bloodlines in other books, and since you can pretty much have Status in anything, we didn't feel the idea that bloodlines have their own form of Kindred Status was too much of a stretch. Basically, it works the same way as Clan/Covenant/City Status, albeit more niche. Because the Treasures are kind of a BIG gift for a single bloodline, we wanted the barrier of entry to be a little bit higher than usual, so we used the same Status limitation the Ordo uses, but without a cost break.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T02:50:39-07:00","id":1494509,"title":"","content":"There seems to be a paralell between elder Bak-Ra and their alleged patron, in the sense that they're all senile and out of touch, as depicted through myth. Was that intentional?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T03:23:16-07:00","id":1494510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1494509#post1494509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There seems to be a paralell between elder Bak-Ra and their alleged patron, in the sense that they're all senile and out of touch, as depicted through myth. Was that intentional?</div> </div> </div> </div>More a lucky coincidence (though it may have inspired the original Ancient Bloodlines version, I cannot say). The idea of elder Bak-Ra coming of as deranged (by elder vampire standards) to the rest of the All Night Society was a very obvious setup to build from the initial hook of &quot;vampires who believe they belong into the sun.&quot; After this initial setup was clear, the idea of making it a bit of a simile to senility or dementia in humans was an obvious followup, which then also introduced the concept of the generational conflict, which I found out a neat contrast to how generations in a bloodline are usually portrayed. Personally, I find the idea of playing a young Bak-Ra who navigates their elder-sire's weird whims and claims and their regular modern Requiem rather intruiging.<br /> On a more meta level, I also found it a good way to get some of those old Fog of Ages plot hook back into 2e while leaving the Fog as a universal thing (rightfully) in the coffin.<br /> <br /> There are some more Ra-specific aspects in some of the unspoilered content though.<br /> <br /> Trying to balance the idea of the Sun-Stroked being obviously confused on one hand and &quot;maybe there is something to their claims after all&quot; on the other was the biggest challenge. I find that ambiguity serves ancient mysteries well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","user":"saibot","date":". 10-07-2022, 06:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T05:02:51-07:00","id":1494516,"title":"","content":"Honestly I expected to see a bit more emphasize on proto-Theban Sorcery in context to them, considering that it felt important in their original writeup. Like, it is still there, but I'm surprised there was nothing more in that respect, like special Theban Sorcery rituals only the Bloodline knows about or something along those lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T05:52:15-07:00","id":1494518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1494516#post1494516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I expected to see a bit more emphasize on proto-Theban Sorcery in context to them, considering that it felt important in their original writeup. Like, it is still there, but I'm surprised there was nothing more in that respect, like special Theban Sorcery rituals only the Bloodline knows about or something along those lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>While the idea that Theban Sorcery is really just a misappropriated &quot;pagan&quot; sorcery is something the line has occasionally played with, giving a bloodline 100% For Real True Bloodline Theban Sorcery would be too clear a confirmation that Theban Miracles are *not* the work of the Almighty (or angels, etc.). I prefer to leave as much ambiguity and subjectivity in the Chronicles of Darkness as possible. That being said, using the idea in your own games is certainly worthwhile and you can always use their jumbled memories as an excuse. What if that elder Bak-Ra with those impressive Miracles is actually an early convert to the nascent Spear \u2014 but doesn't remember that at all. Doesn't change the fact that she uses her command of Theban Sorcery to discredit the Sanctified. Neat narrative irony there.<br /> Theban Sorcery would have also been a perhaps too-straightforward &quot;rational&quot; explanation for their supposed past sun-walking, given that their are some Miracles that go into that direction too.<br /> <br /> I suppose one way how you could have your cake and eat it too is to imply that the Bak-Ra were actually the ones that misappropriated Theban Sorcery and that this is indeed the cause of their delusions and Long Night: They were cursed by the One True God for their hubris when they took His tools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T12:24:22-07:00","id":1494543,"title":"","content":"Happy Friday, everyone! Today, we're taking a look at the Nehebkau bloodline of the Twice-Cursed...clan? But first, a programming note. This weekend is Canadian Thanksgiving, and due to travel, I <i>probably </i>won't have an update for Saturday. I should be back Monday, though I'll tease which bloodline we'll be looking at next (regardless of date) below.<br /> <br /> To talk about the Nehebkau, we first have to talk about the creation of the Twice-Cursed. When I wrote them for <b>Spilled Blood</b>, I honestly thought people wouldn't grok them. They're one of the stranger concepts, and while they don't really rock the boat mechanically, they're probably some of the most screwed vampires in the game: two clan curses (Daeva and Nosferatu, the two that play worst together), have to pay five Experiences for Majesty and Nightmare, can only Embrace Touchstones, etc. Don't get me wrong; I was happy with what I came up with, and they fill a vampire archetype that exists in a lot of folklore and media, but I fretted that people would find them a bit half-baked, or unplayable. They were one of the last things I came up with during first drafts, and I kind of thought my reach had exceeded my grasp.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, as I often am, people seem to really dig the Twice-Cursed, and they're probably the thing I wrote from that book that I see most discussed on forums and whatnot. Not to say that just any player can pick up a Twice-Cursed character; definitely more of an advanced class protagonist choice, but there's always someone who likes the play on hard mode.<br /> <br /> This is all a rambling way of saying that I really wanted to make sure the Stalkers got a bloodline. In <b>SB</b>, you can optionally allow them to join both Nosferatu and Daeva bloodlines with some finessing of Discipline spreads, but I really wanted to see what kind of bizarre mutations this already bizarre clan* could produce.<br /> <br /> In that, I think the author filled the brief. The Nehebkau can slough off one of their clan curses onto a doppelganger, letting the creature go out and have its way with the world while the Twice-Cursed pretends to be a Daeva for a while (or a Nosferatu; no judgments!) I'll let the write-up below go into greater depth on that concept, but one thing I want to touch on a bit is the historical aspect of this bloodline. Something the author and I talked about during development was where to place this bloodline in the Dark Eras. The vanilla Twice-Cursed are &quot;modern&quot;, in that the paper trail starts in the US during the New England vampire panic. Of course, there are some alternate theories about that in the write-up, but nothing too concrete.<br /> <br /> So, you know how we were talking about clans/bloodlines appearing in different places and points in history? This is one of the few bloodlines where we pretty much state that that happens explicitly. The Nehebkau contradict the Twice-Cursed origin story; whether you believe their founder and her claims about lost divinity is another matter... This isn't really a contradiction, of course; it's something I was obviously hinting about in <b>Spilled Blood</b>, and that I wanted to elaborate on here. It's a contradiction in the world of <b>Vampire</b>, which is just a fancy way of saying it's a plot hook.<br /> <br /> Alright, that's it for me. Here are the Nehebkau! Next time, let's look at the <b>Amara Havana</b>!<br /> <br /> <b>Nehebkau: The Ones Who Disgust You</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cOh, my dear, you don\u2019t want to see us. You aren\u2019t </i>ready <i>to see us.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <i>It was too good to be true.</i><br /> <br /> <i>I\u2019ll admit, I was desperate. It\u2019s not like I had any good options in front of me, so being once-cursed instead of Twice-Cursed seemed like a great deal.</i><br /> <br /> <i>They just left out the part where that thing won\u2019t shut the fuck up.</i><br /> <br /> <i>I can feel it trying to move now, trying to wrench out of my back\u2026</i><br /> <br /> <i>Once in a while, it has something useful to say. The only reason I\u2019m not a smear of ash on the pavement right now is that it figured out that the guy I was hitting on at the bar was a hunter. But right now? It\u2019s hungry. Hungry enough that it\u2019s gone past the point of words to just growling and screeching.</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cFucking fine.\u201d I stand up, making sure to bump it against the back of the chair, hard, to get it to stop making noise for a second. I hold my breath, grit my teeth, stretch my arm behind me to grab its skin, and pull.</i><br /> <br /> <i>No matter how many times I do this, the feeling of flesh and bone tearing away from me always feels awful. It staggers out, blinking in the moonlight, looking just like me. Like always. It sniffs the air\u2026 then runs off without a second glance.</i><br /> <br /> <i>It\u2019s going to leave a mess.</i><br /> <br /> We all have a dark side. The acidic part of the mind that craves violence and revenge for a slight; the self-serving voice that knows \u201cwhat\u2019s mine is mine\u201d is the only sensible philosophy; the voracious thing that wants to sever all the bonds holding back the id. Vampires call it the Beast, but not even a saint lacks for vices. Nor can everyone tame that primal urge, and many turn to all sorts of remedies to keep the monster in check, whether spiritual or chemical or both. But we can never really excise our demons.<br /> We shouldn\u2019t, in point of fact.<br /> <br /> Who knows what they would get up to on their own.<br /> <br /> The Twice-Cursed are problem enough for the Kindred, but a recent development has provided even more cause for concern. The so-called Stalkers have grown populous enough to foster the creation of a bloodline: the Nehebkau. These Twice-Cursed are perhaps the most literal manifestation of that name, with each Two-Face having, as the name suggests, a second face located somewhere on their body, something horrible and rotting, with pieces of bone and sinew exposed. It whispers secrets to its host, warns them of threats and, in return, only demands a little\u2026 extra for its assistance. For the lucky ones, inasmuch as any Twice-Cursed can be lucky, it\u2019s somewhere easy to hide, usually on their back.<br /> <br /> But even for those who aren\u2019t so fortunate, there\u2019s a little moment of reprieve. That Second Self can be split away into a clone of the vampire, leaving only the beautiful (or, at least, presentable) half behind while a shambling horror wanders about the night, following the worst impulses of its host. Just don\u2019t think too hard about what it\u2019s doing or why you feel fuller when you have to become one again. Ignorance is bliss, and what\u2019s dead probably won\u2019t return. Just keep an eye out for the ones who do.<br /> <br /> But where does this ability come from? It\u2019s awfully specific, and to those few Kindred who know of this bloodline (and don\u2019t attempt to exterminate it), it far more closely resembles black magic and strange curses than a lineage. If you buy into the stories presented by its probable founder, the self-titled Enheduanna, they aren\u2019t Twice-Cursed at all. The story she tells the revenants and childer she\u2019s gathered over the years is that she\u2019s an ancient deity of life and death, the two-faced divinity of the ancients. Hathor\u2013Sekhmet, Mitra\u2013Varuna, Hel; whatever you wish to call her. Her legacy is older than any name. Enheduanna claims \u2014 believes \u2014 she once walked among the pillars of the First City, convening with immortal beings far greater than the Kindred and witnessing the faces of gods even the hoariest elders would not recognize.<br /> <br /> This clashes with what most Kindred know of the Stalkers. The Twice-Cursed are supposed to be a contemporary problem for the All Night Society, a relatively modern twist of the blood that no one\u2019s yet managed to untwist. It\u2019s easy to dismiss the claims of Enheduanna and her cultists as comforting lies to lure in wayward Stalkers, but the problem is, the more one looks through history\u2019s tapestry, the more one finds threads about \u201cvampires\u201d disconcertingly similar to these Amphisbaenas. This calls the entire narrative surrounding the Twice-Cursed into question. The Nehebkau vehemently insist they\u2019ve been around for centuries \u2014 and, by proxy, so have the Twice-Cursed.<br /> <br /> Does this mean all Kindred were once like the Stalkers, dead wretches caught between the duality of lust and repugnance? If so, perhaps there\u2019s a voice waiting to wrench out of the flesh of every Lick\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> So, you\u2019ve had enough of being a \u201cStalker.\u201d Of course you have. Well, you don\u2019t have to be Twice-Cursed anymore: We\u2019ll elevate you to the status of your peers in the All Night Society. Which ain\u2019t much, no, but it\u2019s the closest you\u2019ll ever get to normalcy, and the cost isn\u2019t even as bad as it sounds!<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> You don\u2019t need to be scared of us. You can trust us. We\u2019ve fixed ourselves. We\u2019re just like you now. Don\u2019t mind that shadow \u2014 it\u2019s just your imagination.<i> Don\u2019t look at it</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> You can divide yourself in half, but when you get right down to it, that\u2019s still you out there. It\u2019s the worst part of you, and that\u2019s\u2026 pretty fucking bad, honestly. You can\u2019t keep it away forever.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan: </b>Twice-Cursed (<b>Night Horrors: Spilled Blood</b>, p. 102)<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames:</b> Two-Faces, Amphisbaenas<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Curse of Duality): </b>Unlike the Twice-Cursed, the Nehebkau can technically create childer from mortals who aren\u2019t a vampire\u2019s Touchstone. The result, however, isn\u2019t pretty. If a Two-Face\u2019s Second Self (p. 113) drains a mortal to the point of death, the vampire\u2019s player must roll Humanity as though a spontaneous Embrace were occurring (<b>Vampire</b>, p. 94). On a failure, [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b>Animalism, Celerity, <i>Protean</i>, Vigor<br /> <br /> <b>In the Dark Eras</b><br /> <br /> <b>Arthur\u2019s Britannia \u2014 400\u2013500 CE (DE2, p. 86): </b>It\u2019s a time of promise for the Nehebkau, or so they believe. The Camarilla has collapsed, and they\u2019re able to run free without the threat of their nature exposing them to Kindred repression. Unfortunately, some would tame this glorious anarchy, from mortals who hunt the supernatural to would-be kings to those who bow before unworthy gods like the Parliament of Owls \u2014 or, for that matter, the capital-G God. Amphisbaenas form their own little domains far away from larger cities, positioning themselves as the two-faced deities of prehistoric civilizations once again. The more paranoid among them fear this will soon come to an end, but most are too content with this rare moment of acceptance that they refuse to worry about any encroaching forces.<br /> <br /> <b>Doubting Souls \u2014 1690\u20131695 CE (DE1, p. 358): </b>A hundred years before Frederick Ransom and Mercy Brown and the horrors that rise from their sad tale, a strange creature stalks the colonists of New England. The nature of the beast is unknown to even the Scarlet Watch, the local experts on vampires, and they speculate that the thing may not be one of the dead at all, but a demon that feasts on the living and takes blood as tribute to an infernal master. In truth, it is the Second Self of a torpid Nehebkau, a refugee from Europe who made the journey to the New World many centuries ago. Somehow, the symbiote is able to leave its host without their consent. The creature finds the mortals in disarray over witches and devils, and it uses the brewing social chaos to mask its feedings as the work of Satan\u2019s servants.<br /> <br /> <b>The Reign of Terror \u2014 1793\u20131794 CE (DE2, p. 316): </b>While there are no written records of the Nehebkau before the modern era (at least not under that name), Enheduanna <i>claims </i>she bore witness to the Terror when she first woke from torpor, and that she and a handful of childer posing as Daeva helped guide the Tenth Choir covenant, teaching them to refine their bizarre blood sorcery with secrets from Lost Irem. The Chorists made a good fit. There\u2019s nothing more natural for a Nehebkau than walking the line between the divine and infernal. To those who buy into the idea of being personally divine themselves, it\u2019s only natural that lesser servants of the divine should either bow before them or be destroyed. And destroying a rival God is an activity they\u2019re more than happy to go along with. The vainest of the Amphisbaenas believe overthrowing the old order will bring back the world Enheduanna was born into, one where they will be revered either out of terror or love. They\u2019re not particularly concerned with which of those it might be\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Gift: The Second Self</b><br /> <br /> To cope with her nature, a Nehebkau can literally split off one-half of her double curse.<br /> <br /> In addition to the following ability, all Two-Faces gain the Dark Passenger Merit upon joining the bloodline. <br /> <br /> <b>Cost: </b>1 Willpower<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Duration: </b>Nights equal to Blood Potency<br /> <br /> The vampire literally splits in half, with its doppelganger gaining either the Lonely Curse or the Wanton Curse, while the Nehebkau loses it for the duration. Should the Nehebkau have any dots in Protean, they may offload further banes onto the Second Self, one per Discipline dot. This does not affect her detachment dice pools, however.<br /> <br /> The Second Self has [REDACTED]<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T12:28:05-07:00","id":1494544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1494518#post1494518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While the idea that Theban Sorcery is really just a misappropriated &quot;pagan&quot; sorcery is something the line has occasionally played with, giving a bloodline 100% For Real True Bloodline Theban Sorcery would be too clear a confirmation that Theban Miracles are *not* the work of the Almighty (or angels, etc.). I prefer to leave as much ambiguity and subjectivity in the Chronicles of Darkness as possible. That being said, using the idea in your own games is certainly worthwhile and you can always use their jumbled memories as an excuse. What if that elder Bak-Ra with those impressive Miracles is actually an early convert to the nascent Spear \u2014 but doesn't remember that at all. Doesn't change the fact that she uses her command of Theban Sorcery to discredit the Sanctified. Neat narrative irony there.<br /> Theban Sorcery would have also been a perhaps too-straightforward &quot;rational&quot; explanation for their supposed past sun-walking, given that their are some Miracles that go into that direction too.<br /> <br /> I suppose one way how you could have your cake and eat it too is to imply that the Bak-Ra were actually the ones that misappropriated Theban Sorcery and that this is indeed the cause of their delusions and Long Night: They were cursed by the One True God for their hubris when they took His tools.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this was my reasoning as well. I remembered this was an element of their backstory in development, but I shared Saibot's opinion that it made things too explicit about the nature of Theban Sorcery. All I added was the line about them &quot;remembering&quot; something about it, which I think sets up the plot hook without defining it too precisely.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T09:35:37-07:00","id":1494737,"title":"","content":"W00t! A direct Irem reference! Plus, a reference to the gods and Judges of Duat! I iz now happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T13:11:41-07:00","id":1494750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1494737#post1494737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">W00t! A direct Irem reference! Plus, a reference to the gods and Judges of Duat! I iz now happy.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are quite a few little Mummy references in the book, but that\u2019s probably the most explicit one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T13:55:40-07:00","id":1494751,"title":"","content":"Would other Twice-Cursed, assuming they exist, also have bloodlines of their own? Like a Twice-Curse amalgam of Gangrel and Ventrue? Would it essentially be the same as the one mentioned above, or should each be a unique form of monstrosity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T15:32:49-07:00","id":1494753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1494751#post1494751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would other Twice-Cursed, assuming they exist, also have bloodlines of their own? Like a Twice-Curse amalgam of Gangrel and Ventrue? Would it essentially be the same as the one mentioned above, or should each be a unique form of monstrosity?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m always in favor of unique monstrosities. The Twice-Cursed are mostly the seemingly Daeva/Nosferatu ones, but it would not surprise me if there were other combos, with their own weird and horrible bloodlines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T16:17:29-07:00","id":1494755,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking that the Hollow Mekhet might have some things to talk with the Nehebkau about unruly malicious other selves that go ah wandering on their own....<br /> <br /> Also, Tenth Choir messing with secrets from Lost Irem? Ikes.<br /> <br /> That beggars the question of what Enheduanna might actually be - some form greater <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Amkhat_(MTC)\" target=\"_blank\">Amkhat</a> or lifeless, the mad remant of a <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Shuankhsen_(MTC)\" target=\"_blank\">Shuankhsen</a>, actually a <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Shan%27iatu\" target=\"_blank\">Shan'iatu</a> in fallen form as she seems claim to be, or just a pile of arcane refuse &amp; detritus grown fertile in its own spoiling?<br /> <br /> (Goddamn, she could be something spontaneously risen from the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Azar\" target=\"_blank\">ritually sacrificed carcass</a> of Aset....)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-27-2023, 10:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T17:23:35-07:00","id":1494757,"title":"","content":"Making her the equivalent of a spontaneously Embraced Aset would be <i>amazing</i>. Her beauty must\u2019ve been a thing of legend for Azar to shack up with her, while her special status as Azar\u2019s girlfriend made the Shani\u2019atu <i>very</i> uneasy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T18:01:05-07:00","id":1494758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1494757#post1494757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making her the equivalent of a spontaneously Embraced Aset would be <i>amazing</i>. Her beauty must\u2019ve been a thing of legend for Azar to shack up with her, while her special status as Azar\u2019s girlfriend made the Shani\u2019atu <i>very</i> uneasy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, if the Deceived's texts can be trusted, she was kind of a pawn of the Shan'iatu in arranging Azar's ascension and unintentional usurpation of Anpu, so it's kind of questionable how much agency or merit she actually had. But yeah, i'd imagine finding their offering arisen and shambling out and about should be <b>quite</b> bothersome for the Shan\u2019iatu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T18:07:12-07:00","id":1494760,"title":"","content":"Maybe she\u2019s Twice-Cursed due to her spontaneous Embrace, as her body remained but her soul fell to Duat. Over time, this division festered then bore unholy fruit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T18:37:45-07:00","id":1494763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1494760#post1494760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe she\u2019s Twice-Cursed due to her spontaneous Embrace, as her body remained but her soul fell to Duat. Over time, this division festered then bore unholy fruit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Have to give Mummy the Curse a longer, deeper read one of those days to look into potential cosmological bits to crossover with Requiem games.<br /> <br /> Though truth be told Requiem's kindred are hilarious easy to connect to <i><b>anything</b></i> no matter how improbable, considering how they basically are just corpses reanimated through a critical mass of all kinds of magical fallout and arcane refuse festering/infusing them that develop sapience as immediate colateral or later on through sheer luck or dogged persistence in avoiding destruction.<br /> <br /> Uratha, awakened, fae, abyssal, maejlin or other - pretty much <b>anything </b>esoteric in pure form or some debased combination can spawn some undead horror if the remains and right/wrong associations are available that, given time and happenstance may or not evolve into something akin to kindred of some kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-11-2022, 05:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T18:45:12-07:00","id":1494764,"title":"","content":"Prometheans are similarly versatile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T19:23:21-07:00","id":1494767,"title":"","content":"As an aside, anyone else gets vibes that <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ammut\" target=\"_blank\">Ammut</a> might &quot;just&quot; be the Nameless Empire's personification of the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Abyss_(MTAw)\" target=\"_blank\">Abyss</a>?<br /> <br /> Also, maybe it's just my imagination, but the way the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Temakh_(MTC)\" target=\"_blank\">Temakhs</a> of the Deceived are described reminds me in some aspects of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Goetia\" target=\"_blank\">goetic</a> demons too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T19:33:02-07:00","id":1494768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1494767#post1494767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an aside, anyone else gets vibes that <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ammut\" target=\"_blank\">Ammut</a> might &quot;just&quot; be the Nameless Empire's personification of the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Abyss_(MTAw)\" target=\"_blank\">Abyss</a>?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Abyss is Nu, the formless not-waters of primordial creation, which Ammut's jaws contain along with the world. Ammut is entropy/oblivion/destruction, marshaled most strongly in the parts of the cosmology that want to supplant the bits of existence that aren't a living contradiction or the parts so starved of reality that they twist the world around them if they aren't eating it wholesale. She's got her teeth in a lot of pies, but Mummy's closest thematic neighbors to the Abyss aren't the mummies who serve her directly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T19:52:47-07:00","id":1494770,"title":"","content":"Are the Ki-En-Gir still tied to the Scelesti?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T19:58:07-07:00","id":1494771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1494768#post1494768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Abyss is Nu, the formless not-waters of primordial creation, which Ammut's jaws contain along with the world. Ammut is entropy/oblivion/destruction, marshaled most strongly in the parts of the cosmology that want to supplant the bits of existence that aren't a living contradiction or the parts so starved of reality that they twist the world around them if they aren't eating it wholesale. She's got her teeth in a lot of pies, but Mummy's closest thematic neighbors to the Abyss aren't the mummies who serve her directly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So a force of entropy, that among other things, reels in those things intruding from the Abyss by gobbling them back into its maw, incidentally preserving the borders between worlds that it contains and defines, so to speak?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T20:03:24-07:00","id":1494773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1494770#post1494770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the Ki-En-Gir still tied to the Scelesti?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ubar is still described as a place where the veil between worlds was thin and its army was aided by wizards, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1494771#post1494771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a force of entropy, that among other things, reels in those things intruding from the Abyss by gobbling them back into its maw, incidentally preserving the borders between worlds that it contains and defines, so to speak?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more that the Abyss in aggregate destroys meaning and the Lower Depths consume almost everything else they can collectively get their hands on and the Devourer has a stake in both as the force that attempts to bring everything that exists to an end state of silence and stillness. The Judges the Arisen serve are hellish creatures of Duat, but the Rite of Return was devised after gaining an audience with Ammut through torturing Abyss-worshipping sorceror-kings.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is probably a line of questioning better continued in the Mummy forums rather than in a thread for a Vampire STV product that obliquely references Mummy for fun story hooks, y'all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 10-10-2022, 11:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T21:34:29-07:00","id":1494776,"title":"","content":"Hello again! A very late update today, but I thought I'd get it in just in case my COVID booster knocks me out of commission tomorrow. Today/tonight, we're looking at the <b>Amara Havana</b>.<br /> <br /> The original version is quite backstory heavy, in a way that I didn't find contributed a lot to actually playing one of these characters. We liked their being the apex warriors of clan Daeva, and their origins as the offspring of gods and demons. So, we tried to deemphasize some of that lore in favour of a more practical sense of what they do. For the most part, that just meant making their history more ambiguous, particularly in their first &quot;In the Dark Eras&quot; entry. Much like the Chandabhanu, we also wanted to divorce them a bit from the caste system, making them a bit less dependent on real-life cultural practices.<br /> <br /> Another big change had to do with their Discipline. Sakti Pati has a lot of interesting effects, but collectively, they don't really come together well enough to fit into a 2E-style Discipline. I made the suggestion of turning them into rituals in my outline, but I think the writer's choice to give them Protean with Devotions ultimately fit a lot better. We also swapped out Celerity for Resilience in their favoured powers, which fit a bit better thematically/mechanically.<br /> <br /> We also change up their bloodline bane. The original is actually really cool aesthetically, but mechanically nil, so we wanted to preserve the concept but give it some teeth.<br /> <br /> As noted in a previous post, there's some overlap with the Kinnaree here. That's partly due to the source material, but in hindsight, I wish I'd distinguished them a <i>bit </i>more cleanly in development. They <i>are </i>different (maximalist warlords vs. karma police), but I can see why one might read the two entries and find similarities, especially considering they're both Hindu-mythology-adjacent Daeva. This is always a tricky thing in development; it's sometimes hard to see the forest for the trees when you're trying to get each piece to fit on its own terms. Plus, overlap is just kind of inevitable with 22 bloodlines! I'm happy with what we ended up with on both fronts, but the perfectionist in me fusses about this sort of thing. And hey, if you do feel they're too similar, use whichever one you like best, or cannibalize their Devotions if you want the best of both worlds.<br /> <br /> So, here are the Amara Havana. Tomorrow (assuming I'm not convalescing), let's take a look at the <b>Usiri</b>.<br /> <br /> (Also, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23812-cherubic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23812_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23812\" data-vbnamecard=\"23812\">Cherubic</a> may want to add some thoughts, as this was one of their bloodlines!)<br /> <br /> <b>Amara Havana: The Ones You Fall Before</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cFight me here and die well \u2014 or the Prince\u2019s assassins can set you ablaze. Your choice.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Vampires are the ultimate nocturnal predators. This is a truism that\u2019s been passed down from sire to childe since time immemorial. To survive, the Kindred must be devious and underhanded, forever lurking in the dark. That\u2019s just what predators do to survive. A tiger has no concept of fighting fair. A tiger who abides by a code of honor \u2014 who refuses to stalk and hide from its prey \u2014 will die.<br /> <br /> Lesser Kindred tell themselves such things to soothe the pain of their existences in the twilight hours before daysleep claims them, but it\u2019s a coward\u2019s way of looking at their condition. Look at the might of the All Night Society. See how frail a human is before it, how their minds collapse under the slightest psychic push, how their ribs crack from a mere brush of a dead hand, how one can turn their world against them with a word. You are not meant to be some lesser beast lurking in the shadows of the city; you are blessed\u2026 if you\u2019re willing to accept it.<br /> <br /> This is the way of the Amara Havana, Guardians who, by their own billing, were created by a goddess and a demon to be neither. They are both the left and right hand of the Damned. Ostensibly, they defer to the prince of their domain; they\u2019re warriors, after all, and their place is to lead on the battlefield, not in thrones\u2026 but in practice? Well, Daeva will be Daeva. At the peak of their power in the halls of India\u2019s All Night Society, they were perhaps too influential in for anyone\u2019s comfort but their own, Embracing almost exclusively within the <i>kshatriya </i>caste in their heyday. They were to be both wise and mighty, to mingle within the courts and dazzle with beauty and wit, then to lead the charge on the battlefield and leave trails of broken bodies in their wake as a warning to those who might oppose their domains.<br /> <br /> Those nights are long gone, but the Asura remain. They still teach the same stories and nudge their childer into the same roles, to be warriors and protectors of the night and, at times, of mortals who are sufficiently\u2026 valuable to Kindred causes, eschewing the usual underhanded tactics other vampires prefer: An assassination would reflect poorly on them, but an outright duel gives their doomed target a chance to prove their worth. More importantly, it gives the Guardian a chance to prove her power \u2014 preferably with witnesses. Skulking around in the dark picking off kine to feed upon is dishonorable; better to gather mortals with the good sense to respect her and make her nature clear. Only the best of the herd are worthy of this, of course, but all kine need to eventually acknowledge they\u2019re in the presence of the divine. The especially lucky might even get to fight alongside her.<br /> <br /> This, at least, is the theory, one that rarely pans out in practice these nights. The mightiest elders of the Amara Havana have either met Final Death or lie in torpor to avoid facing the modern world, and the youngest scions are left to try and make their way, reconciling what they\u2019ve been trained to do and think with the practical reality around them. After all, the nights when the common man would readily accept the presence of a god are never coming back, and the preening arrogance and lack of subtlety the Amara Havana cultivated are now far out of favor \u2014 if not outright dangerous \u2014 for the Kindred around them. The neonates of the bloodline have begun to quietly move away from traditional practices as the few remaining elders sleep the ages away in the hopes of some night waking to a better age.<br /> <br /> Their remaining childer are often locked into roles as bloody-handed enforcers for whatever faction in the city gives them the best offer. The most idealistic yearn for the nights of openly claiming to be half-gods, or playing vigilante and protecting certain human communities for the low, low price of their unquestioning devotion. This behavior never tends to last long; a Requiem of constant violence and danger brings the Beast too far to the forefront. But, given the reputation that\u2019s trailed them for millennia, it\u2019s not as if they have many other choices.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> Power, beauty, influence, the blood of gods and demons alike \u2014 it\u2019s the best of all possible worlds, if you can shoulder the burden of divine heritage. Everyone will revere you, fear you, or envy you. Either way, you\u2019re taking center stage.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> You know what happens to those who stand up against holy power, don\u2019t you? Look at the deeds of Mother Kali, the one who birthed us. Legions of demons turned to a messy pulp of gristle and sinew before her. Even Shiva the Destroyer, in all his terrible glory, couldn\u2019t stand against her might. Move out of our way or you will be the ash on the ground we walk.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> All the chest-beating honor is nothing more than smoke and mirrors when you get right down to it. Dress up the tiger in gold to hide his stripes, but they\u2019re still there. He\u2019ll still eat you if he\u2019s hungry enough\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Guardians, Asuras, Vyaghra (\u201cTigers\u201d)<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Bloodstained Curse): </b>The world recognizes the blood-soaked nature of the Amara Havana, whether they want it to or not. Unless her player succeeds a Humanity roll or spends a Willpower, whenever an Asura feeds on someone for the first time, the victim begins to see phantasmal visions of blood that trail wherever the Asura goes, granting him the Obsession Condition with regard to tracking her down. This usually manifests as bloody handprints and footprints, but sometimes may include more fanciful ones that hint at past violent encounters the vampire has inevitably entangled herself in. Whether this makes the Asura an awe-inspiring god of war or a monster necessary to put down is a matter of perspective, but it certainly makes her hard to miss.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b><i>Majesty</i>, <i>Protean</i>, Resilience, Vigor<br /> <br /> <b>In the Dark Eras (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> <b>To the Strongest \u2014 330\u2013320 BCE (DE1, p. 68): </b>As Alexander\u2019s empire expands, so does the body count, and thus, as they always do, the dead rise. Creatures called daeva follow in the wake of the invader Greeks, often the corpses of those they slaughter, soldiers and innocents alike. They sup upon the carnage, and some take a great liking to battles where death is meaningless. A few believe the Goddess Kali favors them, and that they have been tasked with hindering her enemy, the demon Alakshendra. The forms they take from the shifting earth befit her brutal magnificence. They say they are different from the other dead, and perhaps they are right.<br /> <br /> <b>New Devotions (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> The Amara Havana have many ways to conquer. Called Shaktipata after the Hindu concept of conferring spiritual energy upon a person \u2014 it\u2019s unclear if the irony is intentional or not, even among Asuras \u2014 these Devotions made the Amara Havana the fiercest Kindred warriors in ancient (and modern) India.<br /> <br /> <b>Gift of Indra</b><br /> <b>(Protean \u2022\u2022, Vigor \u2022, Resilience \u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Someone too clever by half might assume the best way to take out a warrior is to catch them unaware and away from their panoply. The unfortunate truth is that a Guardian is never unarmed.<br /> <br /> This Devotion costs 2 Experiences to learn.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost: </b>1 Vitae<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <br /> <b>Action: </b>Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Duration: </b>Scene<br /> <br /> The Amara Havana extrudes his dead flesh, blood, and bone from his body to fashion a terrible weapon. The exact form of it varies based on the personal preferences of the Guardian himself, but most commonly it will resemble a sword or a trident, which were the weapons of choice for Durga herself. This weapon has a Durability and weapon modifier rating equal to the Guardian\u2019s Protean dots, and its Size cannot exceed 2.<br /> <br /> If she has not created the weapon already, once per scene, the vampire can use this Devotion reflexively and for free upon taking lethal damage, which will cause the weapon to blunt some of the impact of the blow. The Asura may choose to reduce either the weapon\u2019s damage modifier or Durability on a one-for-one basis to reduce damage from the attack.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T17:10:12-07:00","id":1494821,"title":"","content":"Well, the booster doesn't seem to have hit (yet?), so let's take a look at the Usiri while we have the chance.<br /> <br /> So, I pretty much knew what we were going to do with Hypnagogia from the get-go. Like so many bloodline sleep/hypnosis/memory powers before it, it was just Dominate with a different coat of paint \u2014 much of it is covered by The Lying Mind \u2014 so that was an easy switch, one which the author made without my prompting; always nice to be on the same wavelength. The big changes had more to do with the Fog of Eternity, or the lack thereof. Since that's a setting element that's much more ambiguous in the current edition, we had to make sure this bloodline was still relevant. Like the Agonistes (who are referenced in the write-up) we tweaked what the Usiri are doing with all those sleep powers, though we didn't have to adjust as much as I'd first assumed when looking over their write-up. The author of this one also did the Mnemosyne in <b>Strange Shades</b>, so he also had to be careful not to step too far into their thematic realm (they also get a reference!)<br /> <br /> No big lore changes here beyond the Fog-adjacent issues. The original Usiri serve is a fun counterpart to the Bak-Ra: the latter are convinced they aren't charlatans but everyone believes otherwise, and the former are the opposite.<br /> <br /> Nothing big changed in development. I don't remember if I mentioned this above, but the initial plan for these bloodlines was to include one of the historical covenants in each of the &quot;In the Covenants&quot; sections. That idea ended up not working very well; there weren't quite enough covenants, and later periods didn't really have any, which either meant including a <i>lot </i>of Gallows Post entries* or stretching what little we had to draw on very thin. However, many/most of those covenant descriptions survive as &quot;In the Dark Eras&quot; entries or story seed sidebars. In this particular case, the One Thousand and One Nightmares entry was about the Fir'awn specifically, so I just adjusted that to be more general.<br /> <br /> So, take a nice rest with the Usiri. Tomorrow, let's look at our last (!) old bloodline: The <b>Geheimen</b>!<br /> <br /> <b>Usiri: The Ones Who Make Your Dreams Come True</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;</i>Shh<i>. Go back to sleep...&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Torpor is a reality for all Kindred, should they survive long enough to experience it. The Sleep of Ages is a daunting prospect, if not downright terrifying: to slumber for years or even centuries as plans crumble from neglect and rivals prosper in your absence. Then there are other, less-understood dangers. Some Kindred awaken with missing memories, others with past events warped beyond recognition, and still others with entirely new personalities to better adapt them to the modern nights. No one knows why these afflictions occur, or how to prevent them, which makes entering a long stretch of torpor something even ancient vampires dread.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, the Usiri have returned to protect and guide their Kindred safely through torpor and back into wakefulness\u2026 for a modest fee. <br /> <br /> The Guides say their traditions date back to the heights of the Egyptian Kingdom, though their reappearance in the All Night Society is a relatively recent phenomenon. According to the Usiri, Kindred who fall into torpor experience a spiritual journey through the Underworld, one where they must battle dark entities and their own inner demons for the right to return to the waking world. Trauma from these encounters is what causes the personality changes some Kindred experience upon waking, and the Usiri, Chosen of Osiris, can shield the mind from these dangers with their rituals.<br /> <br /> As to be expected, most domains greet these claims with a healthy dose of skepticism, but the number of compelling testimonials from the Guides\u2019 clients are only increasing. An immaculately dressed woman with gold-rimmed pince-nez guides Invictus knights back from violence-induced torpor with their minds sharper than ever. A skeptical Acolyte experiences her calmest night in decades after an Usiri priest in soft gray robes soothes her Beast while she sleeps. A Guide with a loud shirt and sonorous voice watches over a beleaguered Carthian lobbyist during a monthlong torpor, and the Firebrand awakens with the zeal of a youth that\u2019s centuries past.<br /> <br /> The fact that all these Kindred only began to have troubles after the Usiri appeared in their domains is, of course, a coincidence. The bloodline\u2019s apparent ability to provide succor to troubled Kindred minds has earned them the somewhat sarcastic moniker \u201cTherapists,\u201d but it\u2019s taken the label in stride. Indeed, some progressive Usiri make a point of modernizing their methods, adopting the trappings of current psychological practices and minimizing the Egyptian mysticism. For all their soothing words and kind smiles, however, the Usiri are still Haunts, and they feed on fear. They prey upon the insecurities of their Kindred, using words of caution to plant seeds of doubt that bloom into a creeping dread of the unknown. That they really believe it\u2019s for their client\u2019s own good doesn\u2019t change the fact that, very often, the terrors the Guides calm are ones of their own making. <br /> <br /> So, are the Usiri wise spirit guides dedicated to shepherding Kindred through difficult times, or are they sly hucksters preying upon the paranoia of vulnerable vampires?<br /> Why not both?<br /> <br /> The Usiri bloodline truly is ancient, and they were known among the old Kindred of Egypt as Warriors of the Dead, respected far and wide for their ability to protect slumbering minds. They were also complete charlatans. These clever Haunts developed unprecedented powers of mental manipulation and used them to construct elaborate horrors within victims\u2019 minds, working them into a state of panicked terror. Only at the peak of this fear would the Usiri relent, appearing in their victim\u2019s dreams as saviors, claiming to have interceded on their behalf against the torments of the Underworld. At the height of their power, every court had at least one Usiri advisor, and no Egyptian elder would think of entering torpor without the Warriors of the Dead at their side. <br /> <br /> Everything changed for the Usiri upon the Roman invasion of Egypt. A flood of foreign Kindred arrived, dismissing the Egyptian gods as masks for their own, and the \u201cWarriors of the Dead\u201d as tricksters and liars. Now, the words of invaders would not be so easily believed, but with the forces of Rome and Greece also came the Mnemosyne and Agonistes, Shadows whose unique abilities objectively revealed Usiri\u2019s rituals were all lies, their role as \u201cguardians\u201d a total sham. Exposed, the deposed Warriors of the Dead were hunted down or exiled, and within a century or two, they were largely thought to be extinct. <br /> <br /> Not all the Usiri met Final Death, however. A handful survived by, ironically, retreating into deep torpor, intending to emerge only when the world had forgotten their lies. When they awoke many centuries later, these weakened elders sought to rebuild their power, but this time, they would add an extra layer to their deception by having their childer <i>believe </i>in what they were doing. All Therapists Embraced in the modern era have had faith in their \u201cmission\u201d installed in them by their elders, who are the only ones who remember the truth. Those same elders hope to raise their bloodline up to a place of power again, by stealing secrets from sleeping Kindred just as they did millennia ago. This time, however, there will be no fall.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> You feel the call of the Underworld every night, and you want to better understand its mysteries. You want security from torpor and its dangers. You want an understanding of your nature that few ever receive. You want others to look to you for deliverance from their fears, along with the power to grant or deny it as you see fit.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> We are the Chosen of Osiris, He who governs the dead. Including you. Do not interfere in the sacred duties of His Guides \u2014 it\u2019s only by His grace that you return from the Underworld each night with your mind intact. A Guide can lead you out of peril just as easily as into it. Choose wisely.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> We know we shouldn\u2019t question; it\u2019s not our place. And yet\u2026 if we\u2019re so beloved by Osiris, why did He let us fall? Why are we met with suspicion and disbelief? We think we knew the answers to these questions once, but those memories slip through our fingers like sand. We claim to be Guides, but have we been lost all along?<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan:</b> Nosferatu<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Guides, Chosen of Osiris, Therapists, Warriors of the Dead (historical)<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Curse of Osiris): </b>For a bloodline that sells its ability to provide other Kindred peaceful journeys through torpor, the Guides don\u2019t rest so easy themselves. Every time an Usiri sleeps, her player must roll her Humanity, or else she experiences intense visions of the Underworld and the souls trapped there. If she fails, she is tormented by horrifying, yet compelling, chthonic images and [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> <i>Auspex</i>, <i>Dominate</i>, <i>Nightmare</i>, Obfuscate<br /> <br /> <b>In the Dark Eras</b><br /> <br /> <b>To the Strongest \u2014 330\u2013320 BCE (DE1, p.68): </b>The Chosen of Osiris cult is among the most powerful factions of the dead in Egypt, even rivaling the Followers of Ra. Trusted advisors to pharaohs both living and lifeless, the Warriors of the Dead ruthlessly crush and discredit any who doubt their wisdom, but they grow more arrogant and careless with each passing night, so certain of their invulnerability. They don\u2019t know it yet, but the meeting of lands and cultures brought about by Alexander will be their doom. Culture shock brought on by an influx of foreign Kindred will shatter the mystery of the Warriors\u2019 abilities, and they will begin to be questioned for the first time in centuries. Also arriving with the young king are mages, whose arcane insight and influence will begin to erode that of the Warriors of the Dead. For the Chosen of Osiris, it is the beginning of the end.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Gift: Hypnagogia</b><br /> <br /> Whether other Kindred believe in the Usiri\u2019s mysticism or not, there\u2019s no denying the Guides have some peculiar abilities. Chief among these is <i>Hypnagogia</i>, a way to touch the minds of sleeping or torpid Kindred. The Usiri claim their patron god allows them to follow the spirits of these vampires into the Underworld in order to shepherd them safely through its many challenges. While most other Kindred scoff at this, they don\u2019t have another ready explanation for how the Guides do what they do.<br /> <br /> By anointing or feeding a subject, an Usiri can [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>Story Seed: Scholars, Guides, and Thieves</b><br /> <br /> Both the Mnemosyne and Agonistes have survived the intervening centuries from their initial confrontation with the Usiri, and it\u2019s likely both or either groups of Shadows have intact records of the Guides. The Agonistes are, and remain, guardians of knowledge, and they opposed the Warriors of the Dead because of how they twisted the truth of events to suit their own ends. If the bloodline\u2019s elders were to become aware that the Usiri are up to their old tricks, they would almost certainly take steps to thwart them once again, and with their own insights into torpor, they\u2019re in a unique position to do so.<br /> <br /> The Mnemosyne, on the other hand, are nearly unrecognizable compared with when they first encountered the Guides. Now they\u2019re the Mind-Thieves, using stolen memories to extort and blackmail other Kindred. With most of their elders long gone, it\u2019s unlikely that any waking Mnemosyne know of their bloodline\u2019s connection to the Guides, but Usiri elders certainly remember them. Currently, they\u2019re divided as to whether they should simply conceal themselves from their old rivals or attempt to strike a deal. The current incarnation of the Mnemosyne is much more likely to try and work with the Usiri (for a cut of the profits) rather than expose them, but could there ever be enough trust between the two lines for an alliance to work? For more on the Agonistes, see <b>Bloodlines: The Devoted</b>, p. 7; for the Mnemosyne, see <b>Strange Shades: Mekhet</b>, p. 43.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T17:25:01-07:00","id":1494822,"title":"","content":"So the demons Usiri claim to combat are false. But even lies and falsehoods and masks can come to life in the broader world of the Chronicles\u2026 cue [insert your favorite psychic-chthonic-infernal horror from gameline A here]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T17:39:02-07:00","id":1494824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1494822#post1494822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the demons Usiri claim to combat are false. But even lies and falsehoods and masks can come to life in the broader world of the Chronicles\u2026 cue [insert your favorite psychic-chthonic-infernal horror from gameline A here]</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bloodlines: The Ageless, p. 99</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>But It\u2019s All Fake... Right?</b><br /> <br /> The Usiri are charlatans; always have been. They have no divine patronage or mission from Osiris, if that god ever even existed. Everything they do can be explained by their Disciplines and some clever tricks of the blood.<br /> <br /> And yet\u2026<br /> <br /> The Underworld is very real, and the Guides do seem to have ties to it. Most modern Usiri believe in their mission, and while that faith is largely the product of mental conditioning, it still holds power. It may very well be that while the rituals of the Guides began as pageantry, they\u2019ve since made a connection to something with real power in the Realms Below that\u2019s providing them with guidance and patronage. If that\u2019s the case, what is this entity\u2019s goal, and why is it so interested in torpid Kindred?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:8px\">tencharacters</span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-12T16:23:46-07:00","id":1494889,"title":"","content":"Alright, let's get alchemical with the <b>Geihemen</b>.<br /> <br /> The first thing you'll notice is the name change. For that, I'll quote the author, who's a native German speaker:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One issue the Geheim have is that their very Bloodline name is really silly. It literally translates into &quot;(be) secret&quot; (as an adjective, not as noun; if we were being generous we could assume they were going for an adjectival noun, but the spelling does not really fit that, but it is hard to tell when you mix in a German name into English text). </div> </div> </div>Basically, we wanted to make the name linguistically coherent. We considered doing a more extensive change, but I felt it was better to keep some continuity with the original. We split the difference a tad, suggesting that their name in English-speaking countries is something of a misnomer, whereas in Germany and other European nations, they're known as the Loge der Geheimnisse.<br /> <br /> The other big change was their Discipline. The Geheimen are one of only two bloodlines with unique Disciplines in the book, and we had a lot of discussion about how we should do that. Blutalchemie is famously a riff on the old Tremere path of blood from <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b>, and while we've kept some of the DNA from that, we felt the effect would be better served as something more modular. That said, we didn't want to go with a full-on Ritual Discipline, though we certainly took some notes from that system. The closest comparison is probably the update we did of Ortam for the Gulikan in <b>Sin Again</b> \u2014 not quite a straight Discipline, but not quite a blood sorcery either. We also changed their bane completely. The original just wasn't that thematic, and we felt their hedonistic qualities could be a bit more to the forefront.<br /> <br /> The other bit of housecleaning we did was removing the Thule Society and Nazis from their backstory. It feels like a half-baked afterthought in the original write-up, and it left a bad taste in our mouths. Those connections didn't add anything to the bloodline, and there was no attempt to grapple with the implications at all. For these reasons, we also changed their logo, which is now the Ventrue scepter and crown superimposed over the alchemical symbol for gold (FYI).<br /> <br /> <i>Anyway</i>, I really like this new take on the Geheimen. They're a little different from the other two Ventrue bloodlines in the book while still fitting into the Lord archetype really nicely.<br /> <br /> Before I conclude, a small correction: Apparently, we actually have one more old bloodline to do: the Corajosos, who I convinced myself I did early on. However, rather than having two Ventrue bloodlines in a row, tomorrow, let's look at our last new bloodline: the <b>Higalit </b>of Clan Amari.<br /> <br /> <b>Geheimen: The Ones Who Squeeze Every Drop from You</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Progress comes hand in hand with breakage.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Dead seekers with inquisitive minds, insatiable urges, and Vitae especially suited to transformation, the Geheimen are a study in contrasts. The Geheimen (actually the \u201cLodge of Secrets\u201d or \u201cLoge der Geheimnise\u201d in the original German) are a bloodline of Lords who have perfected a form of Vitae-based alchemy. These Dilettantes are also prone to bouts of hedonism that contrast and complement their scientific curiosity, a trait they\u2019re said to have inherited from their mercurial creator. Sybaritic soir\u00e9es seeking extremes of sensation, manipulations of the nobility, and wild experiments into the nature of the Blood \u2014 these are the hallmarks of the Dilettantes.<br /> <br /> Most Ventrue content themselves with control over man and beast, but the Blood Alchemists have power over inert matter \u2014 and, even more so, power over the Blood. However, even in their research approach, they\u2019re unusual. Far from stodgy scholasticism, Dilettantes practice a DIY method of mystical study. Many build their own laboratories covering a dizzying array of designs. Philosophical exchanges and disagreements on the nature of alchemy, sensation, and the soul are common, but few Dilettantes are so gauche as to get involved in personal vendettas over matters of perspective. Better to focus one\u2019s time on further study and the wisdom of one\u2019s own body.<br /> <br /> Far removed from the stereotypical stoicism and aloofness of most Ventrue, the Geheimen throw themselves with great fervor into physical and mental experimentation, and for many of them, you can\u2019t separate the two \u2014 mind and body are one. <i>Experience </i>is important to these Blood Alchemists as the science behind their work; alchemy isn\u2019t just about the transformation of substances, but the evolution of the very soul. What transformations is the Kindred soul capable of? That remains to be seen.<br /> <br /> A Dilettante\u2019s night-to-night existence is much less high-minded, however. Geheimen are very practical when it comes to using both their unique gift of Blutalchemie: The riches they create from Vitae have provided them a great deal of soft power, something the Lord\u2019s word alone just can\u2019t match. They supply their allies, buy their rivals, and destroy their enemies with blood-soaked treasures and alchemical traps.<br /> <br /> While often shunned as Vitae junkies, sometimes a true connoisseur of Vitae is exactly what a domain needs to identify an obscure heritage, a rare vintage, or some other conundrum of the Blood. Indeed, the bloodline\u2019s limitless curiosity and glorious past have equipped them with connections among the other shadow-folk of the world. Various schools of alchemy exist within many uncanny societies, and the Dilettantes are always eager to learn about other approaches, perhaps even getting a chance to taste the blood and flesh of those creatures too. Few of their new \u201cfriends\u201d say no to the material comforts that they can provide.<br /> <br /> Yet despite these many gifts and appetites, in the modern nights, the bloodline has fallen far. The Graf, the bloodline\u2019s founder, has disappeared, and the influence of the Geheimen on Kindred politics has commensurately waned. Jealous rivals have driven them out of many European domains, and Blutalchemie breakthroughs are now rare without the Graf\u2019s guiding hand. All too many Dilettantes have ended up lost to debauchery or Vincula in search of new delights and mysteries; as it turns out, balancing a lust for life and a thirst for knowledge isn\u2019t so simple. Still, their advantages are many and no one knows better the transformations even the basest of substances are capable of than the Blood Alchemists. <br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> We\u2019ve got both the Apollonian and the Dionysian down pat. Whether you\u2019re a natural-born researcher looking for a big payday or a mature libertine with a good head on your shoulders, with us, you make the most of your gifts.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> The red in your veins is the gold in our palms. How\u2019s that for a theory of value? And when our sins do get the better of us, working in the lab on our next breakthrough does wonders for getting our minds off what we had to do to you.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> It\u2019s never enough. More Vitae. More discoveries. More transformations. We like to stand aloof like other Lords, but our needs always pull us back in. Transformation is not creation, but to devour <i>is </i>to destroy. We are alchemists who leave behind less of the world where we pass: nigredo without albedo.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan: </b>Ventrue<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Dilettantes, the Lodge of Secrets, Blood Alchemists, Habsburgs (derogatory)<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Insatiable Curse): </b>The bane of the Blood Alchemists is born of the cravings of their founder and his wild experiments. Geheimen cannot resist Vitae addiction when they taste the blood other vampires; the addiction is automatic no matter how much Vitae a Dilettante takes. This bane obviates the usual immunity to Vitae addiction that elders gain. Furthermore, when a Hapsburg imbibes Vitae from a vampire she hasn\u2019t fed from before, [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b>Animalism, <i>Blutalchemie</i>, <i>Dominate</i>, Resilience<br /> <br /> <b>In the Dark Eras (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> <b>A Grimm Dark Era \u2014 1812\u20131820 CE (DE1, p. 396): </b>The Napoleonic Wars aren\u2019t kind to the Geheimen. The Holy Roman Empire dissolves, the Habsburgs are a shadow of their former glory, and ascendant French Carthians ravage the Blood Alchemist domains with their infectious ideology. Ultimately, this is the age when the Geheimen lose the preeminent position in the Austrian and German domains they held for so long. Now they must scramble for every scrap of power. Soon, they\u2019ll be just another gang of Lords with their glory nights behind them.<br /> <br /> <b>Blutalchemie</b><br /> <br /> All Vitae contains the power of transformation, but the ichor of the Blood Alchemists offers greater potential for vicissitude than most. A Dilettante's Beast aligns with the principles of alchemy to force such changes upon the world \u2014 the Beast is a universal catalyst, after all.<br /> <br /> The Vitae spent as part of this Discipline is used both as a metaphysical currency to \u201cpay\u201d for the exchange taking place and also as a catalyst. Only Geheimen Vitae will suffice, so all Processes require at least 1 Vitae to be paid by the Blood Alchemist. Remaining costs may be paid by other sources.<br /> <br /> In addition, the Geheimen possess supremely honed senses for the intricacies of blood. Upon learning the first dot of Blutalchemie, they gain the Distinguished Palate Merit (<b>Vampire</b>, p. 111) without the drawback. If a character already has this Merit, she instead gains two Experiences but doesn\u2019t ignore the drawback.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Intelligence + Science + Blutalchemie<br /> <br /> <b>Action: </b>Extended (target number depends on the Process; each roll represents a half hour of work)<br /> <br /> <b>Duration: </b>The products of Processes are normally permanent; exceptions are noted.<br /> <br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <br /> <b>Success: </b>The vampire makes progress toward the completion of the Process. If the target number of successes is reached, the Process is complete.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>The vampire works the alchemy with astounding speed. Choose one of the usual effects of exceptionally succeeding an extended action, or temporarily resolve any Vitae Addiction she might be suffering for a week, as she\u2019s been fulfilled by scientific achievement.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure: </b>The vampire faces a setback. The Storyteller chooses a Condition to represent this, which can be even Deprived (Vampire, p. 302), as her addiction rears its ugly head. If the vampire fails to accumulate the necessary successes within the allotted rolls, the Process fails and leaves behind a bloody mess of aborted transmutation.<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Process fails spectacularly. The exact results vary based on the intended outcome, but examples include additional Vitae loss when using her Internal Athanor, damage from the release of gases or liquids harmful to Kindred, or the creation of something that is outwardly the intended product but is anything but. Harm scales with the relative ambition of the Process.<br /> <br /> <b>Blutalchemie Processes (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> Most Processes the Geheimen have developed are flexible, allowing for a great variety of end products based on common procedures. Teachers (when Dilettantes are lucky enough to have them) only instruct their students in basic principles and let them find the best way to achieve specific results through experimentation, which suits most Dilettantes fine.<br /> <br /> For each dot in Blutalchemie, the vampire gains a free Process. Some Processes also require others as prerequisites. Storytellers and players are encouraged to invent new Processes.<br /> <br /> Once a Dilettante character has five dots of Blutalchemie, her player may purchase additional Processes for 2 Experiences each.<br /> <br /> <b>Blood Stone</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost: </b>Varies<br /> <br /> <b>Target Successes: </b>(Vitae stored \u00d7 2) + 5<br /> <br /> This Process creates a crimson stone that can serve as a receptacle for Vitae. The Blood Alchemist transfers the desired number of Vitae (hers or another vampire\u2019s) into the stone. Later, this Vitae can be retrieved by consuming the stone. The Process costs 1 Vitae on top of the amount transferred.<br /> <br /> At the cost of an additional five target successes, the Dilettante can also choose to make this Vitae harmful to other vampires. Any vampire who consumes the stone takes lethal damage equal to the creator\u2019s Blutalchemie rating or the amount of Vitae stored (whichever is lower) and loses that much Vitae as the stone reacts violently with his Blood. When a Dilettante consumes such a stone, this effect is shifted to her own Vitae for the rest of the Scene (she still gains the stored Vitae, however).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-13T12:09:49-07:00","id":1494931,"title":"","content":"Hello again, and welcome to our penultimate entry! Let's see what the Higalit are dreaming...<br /> <br /> This bloodline probably has the highest concept in the book: they mostly remain <i>asleep</i>, or at least reclusive. Unlike the Malocusians, who can shrug off their homebound curse with enough effort, Higalit are burned even by the light of the moon and any other reflected sunlight. They can withstand their bane with high Humanity, but eventually, no matter how much they maintain the Mask, all burn. Combined with their clan bane (greater penalties on frenzy resistance triggered by sunlight), most are bound to their icy havens. But, they have ways around this! With their own special twists of Twilight Projection (Auspex 5), they can manifest their ephemeral forms in the material realm with a bit of effort, walking the world and taking their fill of it, even in the depths of torpor.<br /> <br /> So, this bloodline asks something we don't normally ask of players: have a high-level Discipline to join. You can certainly play a Higalit without Auspex 5, but you can't access their powers straight away. Now, a fifth-dot Discipline isn't nearly as hard to attain as it was in the old experience system, but that's still 6 Experiences at minimum that you've got to attain (assuming you're a starting character who's joined her bloodline and spent all three Discipline dots on Auspex). I thought a lot about this a lot in development, and ultimately I decided I was okay with that. Most bloodlines we've developed are new-character friendly; this one isn't, and I think that's fine. The Higalit are kind of the result of Clan Amari being so bound to the torpor cycle, so I imagine most of their members are those Winter Kings who've had time to ruminate on being frozen solid half the year, even those who are the childer of Dream Wights.<br /> <br /> That said, nothing stops you from playing one from the get-go. Their bane isn't so arduous that it makes going outside totally unfeasible, and it doesn't kick in till you hit Humanity 6 anyway.* I just really liked the idea of what amount to ghost vampires, and I felt Auspex 5 was the most efficient way to do that. I think the author did a great job of making that an attractive (if hard mode) character option.<br /> <br /> This bloodline had a fair bit of fine-tuning in dev. Their bane and the downside of their Merit were initially reversed, but I thought the luminescence made more sense as a quirk of their weird Auspex powers, and burning in moonlight struck me as a good reason for them to develop such powers. I also ended up shifting Resilience to Animalism in their favored Disciplines, because I felt it made more sense for them to have easier access to minions to gather blood and protect their strongholds. I also don't think the bloodline really screams &quot;resilient&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm particularly fond of the Dark Era seed excerpted below. The Winter Kings are kind of odd historically; they're heavily implied to be an offshoot/survivors of another clan, possibly a group of Gangrel, though I <i>think </i>it's more like the original Amari author was drawing a line to something in <b>Half Damned</b> (I don't know for sure, as I never thought to ask, unfortunately). The story seed below is sort of a nod to that.<br /> <br /> Alright, that's it for me for now. Tomorrow, let's look at our final bloodline: the <b>Corajosos</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Higalit: The Ones Who Hide from You</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Dreaming is more real than waking.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <i>The blizzard lasts two days. You fly unseen among its flurries, drawn to the snuffing heat of the creatures trapped within it, man and beast alike. You draw the cooling blood from all of them, swirling it within your form like a stain against the growing snowbanks. By the time the villagers find these corpses, they\u2019ll be frostbitten carcasses with no sign of your touch in the shriveled skin.</i><br /> <br /> <i>You float back toward your corpse, the snow blowing through you. The cold feels almost balmy, no colder than your own heart, frozen deep in the glacier. You can see it glowing from here, a foxfire blue through the snow-whipped night. You\u2019ll have that tended to soon enough, before the blizzard allows any prying eyes to catch sight of that cursed beacon.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Sinking through the solid permafrost, down, down, down\u2026 you find your corpse just as you left it: still dressed in that explorer\u2019s parka from forty years past. Has it really been that long since you last walked in those dead limbs? With an inaudible sigh, you sink back into your ice-cold bones, bringing the wealth of stolen Vitae with you. It doesn\u2019t lessen the frozen state of you, but the luminosity subsides. Good. You won\u2019t have to move your resting place any time soon.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Not so long as you remain lost in the wilds.</i><br /> <br /> Life struggles to survive in the Arctic, but death? Death is the Arctic\u2019s ideal. Exposure spells doom even to the Kindred, and so most of the dead prefer warmer climates. Most. Clan Amari once forged a frozen empire around the Arctic Circle, learning to preserve their Vitae for the long days of summer. Some adapted better than others.<br /> <br /> The Higalit burrow deep into the ice, remaining ever watchful in slumber, their corpses entombed from all possible danger. Even the reflected light of the moon burns their corpses, so most hide away for years, or even decades at a time, only rising when absolutely necessary. But even despite this curse (and unlike their kin), they are not content to while away the summer months. With their own special twists of Auspex, they can walk the earth <i>almost </i>as if they were in the flesh, taking on ephemeral forms to make sure the Requiem doesn\u2019t pass them by. <br /> <br /> Austere and ruthless, the Sunless trade away as much freedom as they can for safety \u2014 theirs and yours. By perfecting this control over their psyches, they overcome the intangible limits of astral projection: Some can even feed in spectral form, while others can Embrace and make ghouls despite their ghostlike state. In times past, a Dream Wight could take over entire villages without ever leaving her haven. <br /> <br /> Like their parent clan, the Dream Wights are almost extinct. The Amari have always preferred a solitary existence, and the Sunless are even more reclusive, though they fiercely defend their hidden strongholds. They rise incorporeal to speak in eerie voices, warning trespassers to depart, and if they aren\u2019t heeded at first, they aren\u2019t above throwing things with unseen hands to force a hasty departure. Or at least, that\u2019s the claim of those few who\u2019ve survived interactions with them. Largely, the Sunless are seen as nothing more than a ghost story, a cautionary tale against venturing too deep into the untouched wilds. <br /> <br /> However, as the ice caps melt, the restless Dream Wights are thawing out. Sudden reversals in drilling operations, decreasing populations in remote Arctic towns, tales of disembodied blood clouds drifting off into the night\u2026 the Higalit may be on the move. They watch the world unfold from a safe distance, influencing others with hints and nudges for their own gratification. They\u2019re not here to play by your rules. They care about only one thing: survival. <br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> You didn\u2019t ask to be thrust into a world so full of danger. Every time you feed, you risk everything. With us, that risk small enough to be drowned in an ice floe. You can sleep and dream without your Requiem slipping by. You can choose how much of yourself to give to the world \u2014 and how often. If you would be untouchable, you\u2019ll find welcome in our chill Embrace. <br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> How do you strike something that isn\u2019t there? A goading whisper, a chilling impulse, a taunt in the dark \u2014 how will you fight us? It would be a mistake to think a ghost can\u2019t harm you. You lash out against the void, at the nothing you find there. Do the others laugh at your fear? Do they tell you it\u2019s all in your head? They may be right; we\u2019re here, in your thoughts, lingering over your shoulder, <i>living through you</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> We\u2019ve poured so much into the dreaming that we don\u2019t know what\u2019s left of our entombed corpses. The more we drift, weightless and untethered, the more we loathe returning to that restrictive sack of bones and withered flesh. But if we don\u2019t\u2026 if we eschew our bodies, they howl with light, a beacon that would summon all our enemies to destroy us. We keep it fed yet it still keeps us prisoner.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan: </b>Amari (<b>Night Horrors: Spilled Blood</b>, p. 77)<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>The Sunless, Dream Wights<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Chasma Curse): </b>The Higalit fear the open world, and for good reason. Any source of reflected or refracted sunlight, including moonlight and the aurora borealis, deals a bashing damage per minute to a Dream Wight unless her [REDACTED]. Resilience cannot negate this damage, though she can mundanely cover herself; see <b>Vampire</b>, p. 102. While dangerous, moonlight alone is not enough to trigger the vampire\u2019s frenzy response (or the Amari clan curse), but Dream Wights who fail to resist their bane are often\u2026 edgy.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Animalism, <i>Auspex</i>, Obfuscate, <i>Protean</i><br /> <br /> <b>In the Dark Eras (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Arthur\u2019s Britannia \u2014 400\u2013500 CE (DE2, p. 86):</b> A peculiar myth is sometimes shared among the Bron bloodline. A fanatical Hedge Knight in search of the Grail supposedly set sail north with his thralls from England\u2019s green shores on a barge of his own construction, believing with all his dead heart that the Christ hid his legacy away in the frozen north beyond the known world. Ice-locked for months, and slowly running out of crewmen to slake his hunger, he eventually came across a gathering of strange beings, intangible yet able to touch the world. These creatures, the \u201cChildren of Michael,\u201d helped restock his larders, gifting him a font of blood everlasting. When he returned to Britain, he claimed angels had gifted him the Grail, but by then, the font had indeed run dry. Modern Bron wonder if there\u2019s any truth to this story, and a few think something divine might still be hidden in the northern wastes.<br /> <br /> <b>New Merit: </b><b>Tethered Dreamer (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Higalit, Auspex \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> <b>Effect: </b>Like the Shadows, Higalit can project their psyches with Twilight Projection, but where the Mekhet only skim reality, the Dream Wights are able to interact with the physical world in limited ways.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback: </b>When using Tethered Dreamer, your character\u2019s physical body phosphoresces. This light is visible for one meter per Vitae she is short of her pool\u2019s natural maximum, and the supernatural nature of this ghostly blue causes it to shine through even opaque materials. Mortals who witness this glow gain the Spooked Condition, potentially bringing danger to your character\u2019s slumbering body.<br /> <br /> <b>Permanent Impermanence (\u2022): </b>Your character only needs to return to her body while in her Twilight Projection after nights equal to her Merit dots plus one. She must still pay a Vitae at the start of each night, however, or else she falls to torpor as usual.<br /> <br /> <b>Phantom Touch (\u2022\u2022): </b>[REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>Haunting Manifestation (\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>Disembodied Thirst (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): </b>[REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>Dreamer\u2019s Kiss (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): </b>[REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">* I <i>believe</i>. I don't think it actually says if bloodline banes work like clan banes in that way, but I've always operated under that assumption.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-13T16:49:12-07:00","id":1494949,"title":"","content":"Any ideas for additional treasures of the Maiyarap? beyond Tahna?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-13T18:07:29-07:00","id":1494952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1494931#post1494931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, this bloodline asks something we don't normally ask of players: have a high-level Discipline to join. You can certainly play a Higalit without Auspex 5, but you can't access their powers straight away. Now, a fifth-dot Discipline isn't nearly as hard to attain as it was in the old experience system, but that's still 6 Experiences at minimum that you've got to attain (assuming you're a starting character who's joined her bloodline and spent all three Discipline dots on Auspex). I thought a lot about this a lot in development, and ultimately I decided I was okay with that. Most bloodlines we've developed are new-character friendly; this one isn't, and I think that's fine. The Higalit are kind of the result of Clan Amari being so bound to the torpor cycle, so I imagine most of their members are those Winter Kings who've had time to ruminate on being frozen solid half the year, even those who are the childer of Dream Wights.<br /> <br /> That said, nothing stops you from playing one from the get-go. Their bane isn't so arduous that it makes going outside totally unfeasible, and it doesn't kick in till you hit Humanity 6 anyway.* I just really liked the idea of what amount to ghost vampires, and I felt Auspex 5 was the most efficient way to do that. I think the author did a great job of making that an attractive (if hard mode) character option.</div> </div> </div> </div>This reminds me: I seem to remember you remarking some time ago on the number of bloodlines that've just wound up getting Auspex as their fourth Discipline, and I notice that's still tending to be a common addition. Do you feel like this is a problem at all as far as design goes, or is this just one of those things to do with the nature of a lot of the bloodlines that've been getting made and updated?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-13T21:06:23-07:00","id":1494957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1494952#post1494952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This reminds me: I seem to remember you remarking some time ago on the number of bloodlines that've just wound up getting Auspex as their fourth Discipline, and I notice that's still tending to be a common addition. Do you feel like this is a problem at all as far as design goes, or is this just one of those things to do with the nature of a lot of the bloodlines that've been getting made and updated?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish I remembered what the context of that was, but it does sound like something I'd say. I might have been talking about <b>Masquerade</b>, actually, as that always seemed to be the filler Discipline. That said, I think the point still stands. I'd say Auspex gets thrown around a lot, at least for updates, because it fits into a lot of categories: prophecy, fate, truth and lies, spiritualism, etc. Conversely, the other four clan powers are a bit more firm in their thematic niches. I wouldn't say that's necessarily a problem, though; it's just the tool that fits the job most often. I find it really interesting that the Mekhet Discipline is so versatile, while they themselves represent the least common vampire archetype. But yeah, I think it might just have something to do with which bloodlines we've updated; anything involving ghosts, for instance, is probably going to get Auspex.<br /> <br /> I just did a very back-of-a-napkin calculation based on the bloodline index in <b>Ageless</b> (i.e., not counting the quick conversions in <b>Devoted </b>or <b>Resurrected</b>) and of the 84 non-Mekhet bloodlines, 31 have Auspex, for about 37%; I'd have to calculate all the other Discipline distributions to see if that's genuinely an over-representation, but I wouldn't be surprised if it was. In comparison, I would bet you money that Protean and Nightmare are heavily under-represented. They're both very specific to their clans (particularly Nightmare),<br /> <br /> And that's just the clan Disciplines. I would guess that Animalism followed by Celerity aren't thrown around a lot either. Animalism for reasons that are probably obvious, and Celerity... I'm not sure why? It might be because Resilience and Vigor have such an obvious duality, so they get switched a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 10-14-2022, 12:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-14T00:22:32-07:00","id":1494960,"title":"","content":"Some time ago I went through all the 1e bloodlines and looked up how many got another Clan's unique Discipline. As far as I can remember, Protean was the least common by a margin. Nightmare might be more niche than Protean, but if you want to do shapeshifting in a bloodline you'll probably just start with the &quot;shapeshifter Clan&quot;.and go from there. And, theoretically speaking, if you want limited or involuntary shapeshifting (which I don't recall from any bloodlines, but I haven't read all of them), it's a great deal easier making that its own thing and instead avoid Protean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-14T11:03:11-07:00","id":1494975,"title":"","content":"Happy Friday, everyone. Let's finish this up!<br /> <br /> It\u2019s appropriate that we\u2019re ending on the <b>Corajosos</b>, as they\u2019re the first thing I wrote for this book. I\u2019d mostly completed their first draft by the time I had to take on my other bloodlines, so I had a lot of time to reflect upon them.<br /> <br /> This bloodline is probably the one that translated the most easily from <b>Ancient Bloodlines</b>. The Corajosos are colonialist bastard Ventrue who used a form of amplified blood sympathy to help build the modern All Night Society, forging an undead trade empire (the Gr\u00e9mio dos Corajosos) before they became victims of their own success. That blood tie effect, Linhagem (Linagem in the original), was/is a really cool power, and quite well designed, so it actually didn\u2019t require much work to give it a 2E glow-up. I didn\u2019t feel it needed to be a Discipline, but it fits really well as a five-dot Merit, and most of the powers from the original book got a fairly straightforward update. The big difference is that Linhagem now ties into Auspex and Dominate, amplifying those powers to affect more natural Kindred abilities. I also more or less directly updated their one Devotion.<br /> <br /> Their bane went through a lot more reworking. In First Edition, they suffered from telepathic overload when other Kindred were around them. It was a fun idea, but the implementation wasn\u2019t all that interesting to me; mostly it curtailed your stats. Our version twists that idea a tad, suggesting that the Corajosos are so in tune with the Vitae of their Kindred, they sometimes tap into the Beast as well.<br /> <br /> While I tried to maintain as much of their backstory as I could, I did have to account for the Gallows Post, who fill a similar historical niche to the Gr\u00e9mio. I doubt that many people have thought about the Corajosos too much since <b>Ancient Bloodlines </b>came out, but I wanted to find a way to mix the old and new lore, and I <i>think </i>I fit them together well enough without retconning anything too severely. Where the Gallows Post are sorta proto-Carthians, the Gr\u00e9mio was firmly Invictus, and I liked the idea that the Brigands were waiting in the wings to pick up the pieces when the Corajosos\u2019 empire collapsed. I also wanted to add a little story seed about the Post possibly making it to North America, since that\u2019s not really discussed in <b>Dark Eras </b>(that I noticed; those are big books!)<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s all 22 bloodlines! Yay! I really enjoyed doing this, and I hope you all had fun following along. Appropriately, the book just hit silver best seller on DTRPG, so I\u2019ll take that as a positive sign. Of course, please feel free to leave your comments and questions; I\u2019ll keep an eye on this thread for a while. And since I haven\u2019t said it in a while, if you enjoyed the book, head on over to the Vault and leave us a review or a star rating. It\u2019s a great way to show people who are hesitant to purchase community content products that our work is worth checking out. I'll also be updating the book todayish, as I think I've caught most typos and mechanical fixes I want to implement. So watch out for that.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I\u2019m gonna take the weekend off to work on Rome-related things, but I might pop in to talk a little bit about the art in this book and share some sketches since that was my other big contribution. I suspect I spent more hours on art for this book than I did on writing.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">And maaaaaaaaaaybe I\u2019ll be back with a little preview of said Rome-related things\u2026</span><br /> <br /> <b>Corajosos: The Ones Who See Right Through You</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cWhat\u2019s a drop? An ocean.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> From Vitae, all things flow, whether the bonds of family or the chains of addiction. Blood is the vampire distilled to her essence: Who are her people? Who is she beneath dead flesh? Who did she eat? If you know enough to read the data flowing through Vitae, you can rise above all the other Licks lapping up the spillage.<br /> <br /> Clan Ventrue is well known for discerning truths from vintages, but some Lords go further. The Corajosos long ago learned that, if information is power, then the information hidden in the Blood is the most powerful of all. With it, they bought an empire. Empires <i>are</i> bought, after all. They\u2019re forged upon the altar of slaughter, but conquest is a comma, not a stop. Without commerce, imperialism is just piracy, and while the sword can carve out a space, it can never mend it. The Bold Ones saw that gap and filled it with nothing less than the Vitae in their veins.<br /> <br /> Once merely a family of Portuguese Lords, the Telepaths latched on early to the mortal Age of Discovery. Hidden away on transcontinental journeys in cargo holds, they hoped to forge a new path, and when they returned to Iberia, their Vitae was changed. These <i>corajosos</i> (\u201cbold ones\u201d) could not only navigate the ties of Vitae better than any Kindred on the continent, but they could also use the powers of the Blood through them, moving information and orders over vast distances. Where they gained this ability \u2014 whether by their own design or pillaged from foreign Kindred \u2014 is debated, but the results were speedy. Their consortium, the Gr\u00e9mio dos Corajosos, soon became the richest Kindred trade guild in Europe \u2014 and not just for goods. With their advance scouts, the Bold Ones learned the secrets and customs of far-flung Kindred, sending back intelligence in the blink of an eye for sale or their consortium\u2019s own avaricious designs.<br /> <br /> While the Gr\u00e9mio never rose to the same heights as the Dead Julii and their Camarilla, its influence is still felt tonight. With their network, the Corajosos facilitated the spread of the Traditions and the five covenants (particularly the Invictus) throughout the world \u2014 the foundation of the modern All Night Society to some; a blood-slick imperialist crime to others.<br /> <br /> It couldn\u2019t last, of course. Information loses its value once everyone can access it, and within a few centuries, European Kindred had enough footholds all over the New World to dispense with the Gr\u00e9mio\u2019s tricks. Tonight, the golden age of picking civilizations clean is long lost, but in its absence, the Corajosos have adapted to the benefits of global communication. Modern Telepaths are the functionaries of Clan Ventrue. They\u2019re go-betweens and couriers, the Licks you send for when you need a message moved through the securest medium possible: Vitae. Some belong to international coteries with waypoints all over the Earth, handing off communiqu\u00e9s without ever touching a computer or a mailbox. Others enhance their talents with mortal high tech, using the Internet to create vast intelligence networks that don\u2019t need to transfer a single byte of confidential data. Yet others are loners and spies, using unknowing mortal thralls to move intel without even a hint of a paper trail.<br /> <br /> Still, temporal, tangible power is hard to give up. Some of the bloodline\u2019s elders have never desired to be anything but Bold Ones, and a few plot to grasp back some of the empire they lost. However, many Kindred, especially those who fought and won against the horrors of colonialism, swore to never see the Corajosos rise again, and they would be happy for any excuse to wipe the stain of their bloodline off the map they helped draw. If the Telepaths do try to make their dreams of revanchism a reality, it will be a war of global proportions.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> You don\u2019t want to be contained. The world is vast, yet the dead would spend their nights in cloisters. Once, the All Night Society wrapped a net around the globe \u2014 a net we crafted in blood \u2014 and it might again. Don\u2019t just be another fish in a small pond: Be a shark in the sea.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> The world is vast, but the Blood is oh so thick, and it never, <i>ever</i> lies. Every drop is just another entry in our ledgers, and you\u2019re just chock full of data.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> Everything we learn, the Beast learns as well. It\u2019s the worst kind of voyeur, and its interests grow more depraved the more you feed it. And who\u2019s to say you shouldn\u2019t? When you can know everything, little can stop you. That includes yourself.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Origins (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> Once upon a midnight darkly, a lovely lass picked flowers from the garden of the King of Birds, and for her crime, she was carried off by the monstrous monarch. Her brother, a brave lad, searched the world for his sister, slaying the King\u2019s many siblings and supping on the secrets of their blood. Still, the King of Birds was as clever as he was mighty, and he carried his stolen bride off to a peak far beyond her brother\u2019s reach. However, the lad, now more beast than boy, had learned that blood flies further than wings, and he bled upon the mountain base to send his sister a message of salvation. As the King rested his head upon her lap, she cracked one of his eggs upon his head, killing him with a single blow and lapping up the sweet yolk, claiming his throne for herself and her sibling. Now the beautiful Queen of Birds and her beastly brother seek to teach the whole world what comes of picking flowers \u2014 distantly ever after.<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames:</b> Telepaths, the Bold Ones (among themselves), Colonizers (derogatory)<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Sympathetic Curse):</b> The Telepaths navigate the space between dead minds, but such intimacy is a double-edged sword. If another vampire in a Corajoso\u2019s presence gains the Tempted Condition, she suffers it herself unless [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Animalism, <i>Auspex</i>, <i>Dominate</i>, Resilience<br /> <br /> <b>In the Dark Eras (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Fallen Blossoms \u2014 1640\u20131660 CE (DE1, p. 294): </b>Japan\u2019s <i>kaikin</i> (<i>sakoku</i>) policy is a major setback for the Bold Ones, and it comes at a particularly ill-opportune moment. The Gr\u00e9mio is in shambles by the time the Shogunate closes Japan, which is all the worse because it was one of the bloodline\u2019s last footholds in Asia. Of course, opportunity sometimes comes out of adversity: Before the expulsion of Europeans, an elder of the line manages to Embrace, and he leaves his new, native childe in charge of maintaining his holdings until the heat dies down. However, this childe will need protection in case anyone realizes what she really is.<br /> <br /> <b>New Merit</b><br /> <br /> With Linhagem, the Corajosos amplify their blood ties, folding the corners of the earth together beneath voyeuristic eyes.<br /> <br /> In addition to accessing the following Merit, Corajosos gain Close Family or Distinguished Palate for free upon induction into the bloodline (player\u2019s choice). If a character already has one of these Merits, she must take the other. If she has both, she gains an Experience instead.<br /> <br /> <b>Linhagem (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Corajoso, Auspex \u2022, Dominate \u2022<br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> Linhagem is a melding of Dominate\u2019s raw mental power and the sixth sense of Auspex, and with it, the Telepaths can navigate sanguine paths that bind the All Night Society together.<br /> <br /> <b>Blood Affinity (\u2022):</b> To understand the roads that link all Kindred, a Bold One must first understand where she\u2019s going. Your character adds her Linhagem dots to all Taste of Blood rolls.<br /> <br /> <b>Binding Ties (\u2022\u2022):</b> Your character applies her Linhagem dots to any Discipline roll that would benefit from a blood bond or Discipline sympathy. If the usual bonus is equal to or higher than her Merit rating, she gains a +1 on top of that usual bonus.<br /> <br /> <b>Sanguine Secrets (\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>Blood Lies (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>Distant Mastery (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> [REDACTED]<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321